(131, 2, 2, 10, 'Future of IT Infrastructure: AI, Edge, Automation, and Sustainable Operations', 'future-of-it-infrastructure-ai-edge-automation-and-sustainable-operations', 'Modern IT infrastructure is evolving with AI, edge computing, automation, and sustainable operations to support faster, smarter, and more efficient digital environments. Organizations are adopting intelligent monitoring, self-service automation, and energy-efficient practices to improve performance, scalability, and long-term business resilience.', '[\"IT Infrastructure\",\"Enterprise Technology\",\"Cloud Infrastructure\",\"Modern IT\",\"Digital Transformation\",\"Future of IT\",\"AIOps\",\"Edge Computing\",\"Automation\",\"Sustainable Infrastructure\"]', 'banner_image-1784047291518-980527263.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784047141734,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"firstName\"},{\"id\":1784047141886,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lastName\"},{\"id\":1784047142032,\"name\":\"zip_code\",\"label\":\"Zip Code\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Zip Code\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"zipCode\"},{\"id\":1784047142175,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"contact\"},{\"id\":1784047142335,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"},{\"id\":1784047142478,\"name\":\"address\",\"label\":\"Address\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Address\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"address\"},{\"id\":1784047142631,\"name\":\"city\",\"label\":\"City\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"City\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"city\"},{\"id\":1784047142785,\"name\":\"country\",\"label\":\"Country\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Country\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"country\"},{\"id\":1784047142958,\"name\":\"state\",\"label\":\"State\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"State\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"state\"}]', 'https://5198-182-156-137-106.ngrok-free.app/api/users', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Future of IT Infrastructure: AI, Edge, Automation, and Sustainable Operations</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The future of IT infrastructure is being shaped by four powerful forces: artificial intelligence that enables intelligent operations, edge computing that brings processing closer to users, automation that eliminates manual toil, and sustainability that ensures responsible resource usage. As businesses become increasingly dependent on digital systems, infrastructure must evolve to support unprecedented speed, intelligence, resilience, and environmental responsibility.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">IT teams are undergoing a fundamental transformation-moving from reactive, manual system management to proactive, intelligent operations supported by automation, AI-driven insights, cloud optimization, and real-time observability. This shift is not merely about adopting new technologies; it represents a new philosophy of infrastructure management that prioritizes agility, efficiency, and long-term sustainability.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI Operations (AIOps) Transform Infrastructure Management</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations (AIOps) is revolutionizing how infrastructure teams monitor, manage, and optimize complex systems. By applying machine learning and advanced analytics to operational data, AIOps enables teams to move beyond traditional monitoring and embrace truly intelligent operations.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Core capabilities of AIOps:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Pattern detection and anomaly identification:</strong> AI algorithms continuously analyze metrics, logs, and traces to identify unusual patterns that may indicate emerging issues-often before they impact users.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Predictive analytics:</strong> Machine learning models forecast resource needs, capacity constraints, potential failures, and performance degradation before they occur, enabling proactive intervention.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Intelligent alert management:</strong> AI reduces alert fatigue by correlating related alerts, suppressing duplicates, prioritizing critical issues, and providing contextual information to accelerate response.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Root cause analysis:</strong> When incidents occur, AI accelerates diagnosis by correlating events across systems and suggesting probable causes, dramatically reducing mean time to resolution (MTTR).</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Automated remediation:</strong> For common, well-understood issues, AIOps can trigger automated fixes without human intervention, enabling self-healing infrastructure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Why AIOps matters:</strong> The scale and complexity of modern infrastructure exceed human capacity to monitor and respond manually. AIOps provides the speed, accuracy, and scalability needed to manage distributed, dynamic environments effectively.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Begin with high-quality data collection and observability practices. Start with narrow use cases like alert reduction or anomaly detection. Build confidence before expanding to automated remediation.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Edge Infrastructure Brings Processing Closer to Data Sources</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Edge computing is experiencing rapid growth as businesses recognize the need for faster data processing closer to users, devices, sensors, and business locations. Rather than sending all data to centralized cloud data centers, edge infrastructure processes information locally or regionally.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key edge use cases:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Manufacturing and industrial IoT:</strong> Real-time processing of sensor data for quality control, predictive maintenance, and operational optimization without sending everything to the cloud.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Retail and hospitality:</strong> In-store inventory management, personalized customer experiences, payment processing, and real-time analytics.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Healthcare:</strong> Processing patient monitoring data, medical imaging analysis, and remote care applications where low latency is critical.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Logistics and supply chain:</strong> Real-time tracking, route optimization, and fleet management.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Autonomous systems:</strong> Immediate decision-making for vehicles, drones, and robotics where milliseconds matter.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Content delivery:</strong> Reducing latency for streaming, gaming, and web applications through geographically distributed edge nodes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Infrastructure implications:</strong> Edge computing introduces new operational challenges, including managing distributed locations, ensuring consistent security policies, maintaining observability across edge nodes, and handling intermittent connectivity. Standardized edge platforms and centralized management tools are evolving to address these complexities.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Identify use cases that genuinely require edge capabilities based on latency requirements, data volume, or connectivity constraints. Evaluate edge platform options based on security, manageability, and integration with your existing cloud and on-premise environments.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Automation and Self-Service Become the Default Operating Model</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Infrastructure automation is no longer optional-it is becoming the standard operating model for modern IT teams. Automation extends across provisioning, scaling, backup, monitoring, security, and governance workflows. Self-service platforms enable teams to move faster while maintaining organizational control and compliance.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Automation priorities:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Infrastructure as Code (IaC):</strong> All infrastructure defined in version-controlled code for consistency, repeatability, and auditability across environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Automated provisioning:</strong> Developers and teams can spin up complete development, testing, and production environments on demand with minimal human intervention.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Policy-based scaling:</strong> Dynamic resource adjustment based on real-time demand, balancing performance and cost automatically.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Automated security workflows:</strong> Vulnerability scanning, patch management, compliance checks, and access reviews integrated into infrastructure pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Backup and disaster recovery:</strong> Scheduled, verified backups with automated testing of restore capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Self-service portals:</strong> Internal developer platforms that provide approved tools, templates, and workflows, enabling teams to move independently while maintaining governance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Why automation matters:</strong> Manual infrastructure management is slow, error-prone, and cannot scale with modern demands. Automation improves consistency, reduces human error, accelerates delivery, and frees engineers to focus on higher-value work.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Audit current manual processes and prioritize automation based on frequency, error-proneness, and time savings. Build reusable automation libraries. Implement guardrails that enable self-service while preventing misuse.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Sustainable IT Operations Become a Strategic Imperative</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Sustainability is rapidly evolving from a corporate social responsibility initiative to a core business requirement. IT infrastructure consumes significant energy and resources, and organizations are under increasing pressure from regulators, customers, investors, and employees to reduce their environmental impact.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sustainability initiatives for IT infrastructure:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Energy-efficient hardware:</strong> Selecting energy-optimized servers, storage arrays, and networking equipment that minimize power consumption.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Data center optimization:</strong> Implementing advanced cooling technologies, leveraging renewable energy sources, and continuously monitoring Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE).</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Cloud sustainability:</strong> Choosing cloud providers with strong sustainability commitments and carbon-neutral operations. Leveraging carbon-aware workload scheduling that runs compute during times when renewable energy is available.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Resource efficiency:</strong> Rightsizing cloud instances, eliminating idle resources, designing for efficiency, and scheduling non-critical workloads to maximize utilization.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Hardware lifecycle management:</strong> Extending hardware useful life through proper maintenance, responsible disposal, and recycling programs for e-waste.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sustainable procurement:</strong> Evaluating vendors based on their environmental practices and choosing partners with demonstrated sustainability commitments.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Business benefits:</strong> Beyond environmental responsibility, sustainable IT practices often reduce operational costs, improve brand reputation, and help organizations meet regulatory requirements and investor expectations.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Measure and report on your infrastructure carbon footprint. Set reduction targets aligned with organizational sustainability goals. Evaluate cloud providers based on sustainability commitments. Consider renewable energy options for on-premise data centers.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Observability Evolves Beyond Traditional Monitoring</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As infrastructure becomes more distributed across cloud, edge, containers, and microservices, traditional monitoring-tracking individual components-is insufficient. Observability provides a holistic understanding of system behavior and user experience.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Observability pillars expanded:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Metrics:</strong> Quantitative data points (CPU, memory, request rates, error rates, latency) that provide health indicators.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Logs:</strong> Structured event records that enable troubleshooting, forensic analysis, and pattern identification.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Traces:</strong> Distributed tracing that follows requests across service boundaries to identify bottlenecks and failures.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Profiles:</strong> Continuous code profiling for performance optimization and resource attribution.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>User experience data:</strong> Real-user monitoring (RUM) and synthetic testing that reflect actual customer interactions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Business benefits:</strong> Observability enables faster incident detection (reduced MTTD), quicker resolution (reduced MTTR), proactive performance optimization, and better understanding of user experience and business impact.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Implement integrated observability platforms. Standardize instrumentation using open standards like OpenTelemetry. Build dashboards tailored to different audiences (engineering, management, business stakeholders). Focus on actionable insights rather than data collection.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Edge and Cloud Integration Deepens</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Rather than seeing edge and cloud as separate domains, organizations are increasingly treating them as a continuum. Workloads are placed where they make the most sense based on latency, cost, data sovereignty, and capability requirements.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Integration approaches:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Unified management:</strong> Centralized tools that manage both edge and cloud infrastructure from a single pane of glass.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Consistent security policies:</strong> Identity, access controls, and security standards applied uniformly across all locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Seamless data flow:</strong> Data moves between edge and cloud as needed, with appropriate filtering and transformation.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Application portability:</strong> Workloads can be deployed to any location in the continuum based on changing requirements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Design with the cloud-edge continuum in mind, not as separate silos. Invest in platforms that support hybrid management. Build skills in both cloud and edge technologies.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Resilience Engineering Becomes Central</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As infrastructure complexity grows, ensuring reliability through resilience engineering becomes critical. Organizations are moving from reactive incident management to proactive resilience design.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Resilience practices:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Chaos engineering:</strong> Intentionally introducing failures to test system resilience and identify weaknesses before they cause customer-impacting incidents.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Fault injection testing:</strong> Simulating component failures, network partitions, and dependency disruptions to validate recovery mechanisms.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Disaster recovery automation:</strong> Automated failover and recovery with regular testing, not just planning documents.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Multi-region and multi-cloud resilience:</strong> Designing systems that can survive region-level or provider-level failures.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Immutable infrastructure:</strong> Replacing failed components rather than attempting repair, ensuring consistent known-good states.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Implement resilience testing in your CI/CD pipelines. Document failure modes and recovery procedures. Test disaster recovery regularly, not just annually. Embrace \"fail fast\" and \"learn from failure\" cultures.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Infrastructure Sustainability Measurement Matures</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Organizations are moving from qualitative sustainability commitments to quantitative measurement and reporting. Carbon accounting for IT infrastructure is becoming a standard practice.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Measurement approaches:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Carbon intensity tracking:</strong> Measuring emissions per unit of compute, storage, or network traffic.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Supply chain visibility:</strong> Understanding emissions embedded in hardware manufacturing, transportation, and disposal.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Real-time energy monitoring:</strong> Tracking energy consumption at the component, server, rack, and data center levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Reporting frameworks:</strong> Aligning with standards like Greenhouse Gas Protocol, ISO 14001, and sustainability reporting requirements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Implement monitoring for energy consumption and carbon emissions. Establish baseline measurements. Set reduction targets. Integrate sustainability metrics into regular infrastructure reporting.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">FinOps Extends to Edge and Distributed Infrastructure</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Financial operations (FinOps) practices that started with cloud are expanding to cover all infrastructure, including edge, on-premise, and hybrid environments.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>FinOps expansion:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Edge cost visibility:</strong> Understanding costs associated with distributed edge deployments, including hardware, power, connectivity, and management.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Capacity planning:</strong> Forecasting infrastructure needs and costs across all environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Showback and chargeback:</strong> Transparent allocation of infrastructure costs to business units, even across hybrid and edge environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Efficiency optimization:</strong> Identifying waste in on-premise and edge infrastructure, not just cloud.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Extend cost tagging and allocation practices to all infrastructure. Build comprehensive cost visibility across environments. Make cost a consideration in architectural decisions.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Skills and Organizational Models Evolve</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The changing infrastructure landscape demands new skills and organizational structures. Traditional IT operations roles are evolving into platform engineering, site reliability engineering (SRE), and AIOps engineering positions.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Skill requirements:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Automation expertise:</strong> Experience with infrastructure-as-code, configuration management, and automation pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Cloud-native knowledge:</strong> Deep understanding of containers, Kubernetes, serverless, and cloud services.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Security awareness:</strong> Zero Trust principles, security automation, and compliance understanding.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Data analysis and AI:</strong> Ability to work with monitoring data, build dashboards, and leverage AIOps tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sustainability awareness:</strong> Understanding energy efficiency and sustainable infrastructure practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Cross-functional collaboration:</strong> Ability to work closely with development, security, and business teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Organizational changes:</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Platform teams build internal developer platforms that enable self-service.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SRE teams focus on reliability engineering and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AIOps engineers specialize in AI-driven operations and automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">GreenOps or sustainability teams focus on carbon footprint reduction.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to prepare:</strong> Invest in training and skill development. Create career paths that reward automation, security, and sustainability expertise. Build cross-functional teams that bridge traditional silos.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Conclusion</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Future-ready infrastructure will combine AI-driven operations, edge computing capabilities, comprehensive automation, robust security, and sustainable practices. Organizations that plan early and invest strategically will be significantly better positioned for digital growth, operational resilience, and competitive advantage.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Strategic priorities:</strong></p><ol><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Implement AIOps</strong> to manage increasing complexity and reduce manual effort.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Adopt edge computing</strong> where latency, data volume, or connectivity require it.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Automate everything repeatable</strong> across provisioning, monitoring, scaling, and security.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Embed sustainability</strong> in infrastructure planning, measurement, and operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Build observability</strong> that provides holistic system understanding.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Design for resilience</strong> through chaos engineering and disaster recovery automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Extend FinOps</strong> to all infrastructure investments.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Develop talent</strong> with modern infrastructure skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Modernize legacy systems</strong> strategically.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Measure and improve</strong> continuously based on data-driven insights.</p></li></ol><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Infrastructure is no longer merely a cost center-it is a strategic enabler of business success. The right infrastructure strategy delivers speed, resilience, security, innovation capacity, and sustainability. Organizations that treat infrastructure as a strategic asset will outperform those that view it as simply an operational necessity.</p>', 'Future of IT Infrastructure: AI, Edge, Automation and Sustainability ', 'Explore the future of IT infrastructure with AI operations, edge computing, automation, sustainable infrastructure, cloud optimization, and smarter IT management. ', 'IT Infrastructure, Enterprise IT, Cloud Infrastructure, Digital Transformation, Infrastructure Modernization, Future of IT Infrastructure, AIOps, Edge Computing, Sustainable IT ', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-02-06 14:31:07', 'published', 109444, 3, 11, NULL, '2023-02-06 14:31:07', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(132, 2, 3, 5, 'The Real Cost of Cybersecurity for a Mid-Size Company', 'the-real-cost-of-cybersecurity-for-a-mid-size-company', 'Cybersecurity budgets in mid-size companies rarely fail because they are insufficient-they fail because they are framed incorrectly. This article reveals why security spending must shift from technical tools to business-aligned intent, and how operational drag, identity risk, and misaligned investments create hidden costs that threaten growth.', '[\"Cybersecurity\",\"Mid-Size Company Security\",\"Identity Access Management\",\"Business Risk Management\",\"Security Budgeting\",\"Zero Trust\",\"Operational Drag\",\"Cyber Risk\",\"CISO Strategy\",\"IT Security Costs\",\"Ponemon Institute\",\"Intent-Aligned Security\"]', 'banner_image-1784050337549-982095793.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2>From Data to Decisions: Embedding AI into Strategy for Competitive Edge</h2><p>Executives​‍​‌‍​‍‌​‍​‌‍​‍‌ and tech professionals are united in their opinion that decisions are the main drivers of business growth, not data. However, the majority of organizations are sitting on vast amounts of data that they are not utilizing. These include customer signals, operational patterns, and market fluctuations, all of which are waiting to be transformed into actionable insights. AI is the technology that makes this transition from waiting to progress. And those companies that are strategically putting AI at the core of their business rather than simply using it as a tool are quickly getting ahead of the game.</p><h2>AI Adoption Is Rising – and So Is the Competitive Gap</h2><p>Recent industry studies indicate that 88 percent of organizations have adopted AI in at least one of their business functions. Adoption of generative AI jumped 65% of organizations report regular gen-AI use in at least one business function in 2024 – nearly double compared to a year earlier.</p><p>What is even more impressive is that over half of the businesses having AI deployed in multiple areas report a revenue increase, which is twice as high as the case of those companies running isolated AI pilots. In other words, AI is not a good investment just because it is fashionable, but mainly because it changes the way decisions are made. 78% of organizations now report using AI in at least one business function, up from 55% a year earlier.&nbsp;</p><p>Imagining AI as a true engine for business growth rather than simply an automation add-on changes everything. Many still look at AI as a tool for cost-efficiency and routine task execution. Useful, yes - but not strategic. The real competitive edge emerges when AI becomes a driver of innovation, revenue, and decision intelligence. AI agents play a key role here, acting autonomously to learn, decide, and execute across workflows in real time, improving efficiency, accuracy, and business outcomes while accelerating growth.&nbsp;</p><p>One may recall the example of personalization as the power of AI. Based on AI models, customer recommendations may generate increased conversions by up to 35% within online commerce. With AI technology, forecasting could lead to a reduction of mismatches in the supply chain by 20-50%. And companies gaining speed in launching new products due to using predictive insights reduce time-to-market by 30-45%. In companies using AI broadly (multiple functions), those “high performers” are nearly 3× as likely to report revenue gains of more than 10%</p><p>The figures reflected here point out a simplistic pattern: AI becomes a source of quantifiable value only when it is utilized as an enabler of decision-making, rather than staying idle in a laboratory.</p><h2>Ways through Which Firms Strategize AI Integration Without a Complicated Process</h2><p>There exists a clearly defined plan that most successful AI implementers follow in their journey of integrating AI technologies into their operations. Contrary to what one may think, this plan is business first and technical later.</p><p>1. Establish Concise Goals</p><p>The decisions taken by AI should always be aligned with the desired outcomes of the business:</p><ul><li><p>Increased retention</p></li><li><p>Delivery in less time</p></li><li><p>Customer experience of higher quality</p></li><li><p>Opportunities for new revenue</p></li></ul><p>When objectives are the ones leading the model -i.e., goals come before the means- there is hardly any hindrance in the process of assimilation.&nbsp;</p><p>2. Get Ready for Data Infrastructure</p><p>In order to function well, AI depends on reliable and integrated data. Companies that take measures to ensure their data is in good shape have reported up to three times greater return on investment in AI compared to those that neglect this aspect.</p><p>3. Move On From Experiments To Fully Functional Projects</p><p>Testing on a limited scale is a method through which one can confirm the viability of a concept. However, the edge over competitors only arises when Artificial Intelligence impacts such areas as:</p><ul><li><p>Marketing</p></li><li><p>Operations</p></li><li><p>Sales</p></li><li><p>Finance</p></li><li><p>Product Development</p></li></ul><p>Value is multiplied by expansion since enhancement is compounded further over departments. Use of AI in finance functions rose to 58% in 2024, up significantly from prior years.</p><p>4. Evaluate, Progress, and Repeat</p><p>Top-performing companies monitor the key performance indicators that were their benchmark, evaluate the changes brought about by AI, improve their models, and broaden their use cases. They look at it not as a one-time implementation but as a continuous learning ​‍​‌‍​‍‌​‍​‌‍​‍‌cycle.</p><h2>What​‍​‌‍​‍‌​‍​‌‍​‍‌ “Data-to-Decision” Looks Like in Practice</h2><p>Think of an enterprise that depended on quarterly reports to set the prices. With AI, the pricing strategy is changed every day according to the demand, competitors’ moves, and customers’ intent.</p><p>Or a retailer that was only able to guess which product to promote. AI now detects trending preferences early and suggests the most suitable product to the right customer - without any human intervention.</p><p>Or a manufacturing company that was only able to react to the breakdown of its equipment. AI is now able to predict the time of inactivity days ahead and thus, schedule the exact maintenance.</p><p>These are not examples of future possibilities. They are real scenarios that are happening right now in different industries – quietly changing the traditional ways of working.</p><h2>Conclsuion</h2><p>Incorporating AI in the business model is not about pursuing the latest technology trend. Rather, it is about facilitating quicker, more intelligent, and more confident decision-making. The effect of AI on business growth is not instant, but rather, when AI is harmonized with business goals and expands across different departments, the growth becomes exponential. Organizations that choose to implement AI now will not only be able to maintain their competitive position but will also be able to consistently lead their industries.</p>', 'The Real Cost of Cybersecurity for a Mid-Size Company | IntentTech', 'Cybersecurity budgets fail because they\'re framed incorrectly. Learn why mid-size companies must shift from technical tools to business-aligned intent to reduce hidden operational costs and improve security outcomes.', 'cybersecurity cost, mid-size company security, business risk management, identity access management, security budgeting, zero trust architecture, operational drag, cyber risk mitigation, CISO strategy, hidden security costs, Ponemon Institute, intent-aligned security, data breach costs, mid-market cybersecurity', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-02-08 10:14:38', 'published', 218312, 0, 5, NULL, '2023-02-08 10:14:38', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(133, 2, 3, 2, 'How AI is Transforming CRM to Help Businesses Deliver Better Customer Experiences', 'how-ai-is-transforming-crm-to-help-businesses-deliver-better-customer-experiences', 'Discover how AI-powered CRM software is revolutionizing customer relationship management through predictive scoring, sentiment analysis, intelligent automation, and personalized experiences. Learn practical strategies for implementing AI in your CRM to boost sales, enhance customer satisfaction, and drive business growth.\r\n\r\n', '[\"AI CRM\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Customer Relationship Management\",\"Predictive Analytics\",\"Sentiment Analysis\",\"AI Chatbots\",\"Customer Experience\",\"Sales Automation\",\"Lead Scoring\",\"Customer Retention\",\"Business Intelligence\",\"Digital Transformation\",\"Marketing Automation\",\"Customer Service\"]', 'banner_image-1784050817101-239331274.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">How AI is Transforming CRM to Help Businesses Deliver Better Customer Experiences</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Artificial intelligence can help customer relationship management (CRM) softwares automate routine business processes like entering customer data, cleaning redundant information, reducing human errors, and using data analytics and forecasting to improve decision-making.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Customer relationship management (CRM) software has long been a staple for businesses of all sizes. It helps businesses track customer interactions, manage sales pipelines, and provide customer support. But in recent years, AI has begun to transform CRM, making it even more powerful and effective. CRM systems now use AI to automate tasks, personalise customer experiences, and make better decisions.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In today’s digital world, it is essential for businesses to adopt AI capabilities to stay ahead of the curve. AI-based CRM can help businesses to increase efficiency and productivity, improve customer experience and execute well-informed and data-backed decisions.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Although a relatively new concept, the prospect of using AI in a CRM tool is picking up pace as an industry standard. Businesses of all sizes are adopting AI-based CRM softwares in an attempt to notch-up their customer relationships and scale their businesses. Let us understand one by one how AI-based CRM can actually help your business.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">What are the current capabilities of AI in CRM?</h3><h5 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>AI-powered chatbots and virtual assistants</strong></h5><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI-powered chatbots and virtual assistants in CRM software are computer programs that use artificial intelligence (AI) to simulate conversation with humans. They can be used to automate a variety of tasks, including:</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Qualifying leads</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Answering customer questions</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Scheduling appointments</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Providing support</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Collecting feedback</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI-powered chatbots and virtual assistants can be integrated with CRM software to provide a more seamless and personalised customer experience. For example, a chatbot could be used to qualify leads on the company’s website, and then pass those leads to sales representatives for follow-up. Or, a virtual assistant could be used to answer customer questions about their account or products, and then escalate more complex issues to human support agents.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI-powered chatbots and virtual assistants can provide:</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">24/7 customer support</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ability to answer customer questions quickly and accurately</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The intelligence to qualify leads and schedule appointments, which can free up sales representatives to focus on closing deals</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Automation of tasks that would otherwise be performed by human employees</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Enhanced customer experience by remembering customer preferences and providing relevant information</p></li></ul><h5 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Predictive scoring</strong></h5><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">One of the strongest features of AI in CRM, predictive scoring uses machine learning algorithms to analyse a wide range of data points, including customer interactions, purchase history, and website behaviour, to determine which leads are most likely to convert into paying customers. It works by assigning a score to each lead based on their behaviour and other relevant data. This score can then be used to prioritise leads and focus sales efforts on those that are most likely to result in a sale.&nbsp;</p><h5 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sentiment Analysis&nbsp;</strong></h5><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Sentiment analysis is the process of analysing digital text to determine if the emotional tone of the message is positive, negative, or neutral. Today, companies have large volumes of text data like emails, customer support chat transcripts, social media comments, and reviews. For example, a sales team can use AI to identify leads that are most likely to convert into customers based on their reviews. For example, a lead who is very positive about the company’s products or services is more likely to convert than a lead who is neutral or negative.</p><h5 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Real-time data analysis</strong></h5><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI in CRM can help with real-time data analysis in a number of ways. For example, AI can be used to:</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Identify patterns and trends:</strong>&nbsp;AI can analyse large amounts of customer data in real time to identify patterns and trends that would be difficult or impossible for humans to spot on their own. This information can then be used to improve marketing campaigns, customer service, and other business operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Predict customer behaviour:&nbsp;</strong>AI can also be used to predict customer behaviour based on their past interactions with the company. This information can then be used to personalise the customer experience and offer more relevant products and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Automate tasks:</strong>&nbsp;AI can also be used to automate tasks such as&nbsp;lead scoring, customer segmentation, and customer support. This can free up employees to focus on more strategic tasks.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A use case can be that of a sales team which uses AI to identify leads that are most likely to convert into customers, and then prioritise their outreach efforts accordingly.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">In What Ways Can Businesses Benefit From an AI-Based CRM Software?</h3><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Predicting customer needs:</strong>&nbsp;AI can analyse customer data to identify patterns and trends that can be used to predict customer needs. This information can then be used to proactively reach out to customers with relevant offers and support.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Personalising the customer experience:</strong>&nbsp;By analysing customer demographics, purchase history, and other data points, AI can personalise customer experience by tailoring interactions and offerings to each individual customer’s needs and preferences.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Automating tasks:</strong>&nbsp;By automating recurring yet critical tasks that are involved in customer relationship management, such as&nbsp;lead generation, qualification, and nurturing. This frees up customer service representatives to focus on more complex and strategic tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Providing insights:</strong>&nbsp;AI can provide insights into customer behaviour, preferences, and satisfaction. This information can be used to improve the customer experience, develop new products and services, and make better business decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Make better decisions:</strong>&nbsp;AI can provide businesses with insights into customer behaviour and trends. This information can be used to improve marketing campaigns, product development, and overall business strategy.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Here are a few specific examples of how AI-infused CRM is being used to improve customer experiences:</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A financial services company uses AI to analyse customer data and identify customers who are at risk of churning. The company then proactively reaches out to these customers with offers and support to help them stay with the company.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">An e-commerce company uses AI to personalise the customer experience by recommending products to customers based on their purchase history and browsing behaviour. The company also uses AI to automate tasks such as order processing and customer support.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A healthcare provider uses AI to analyse patient data and identify patients who are at risk of developing certain diseases. The provider then proactively reaches out to these patients to offer preventive care and support.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Overall, AI-infused CRM is a powerful tool that can help businesses deliver better customer experiences. By automating tasks, predicting customer needs, and personalising the customer experience, AI can help businesses build stronger customer relationships and improve their bottom line.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For marketers, AI-infused CRM can be a game-changer. By using AI to gain insights into customer behaviour and preferences, marketers can create more targeted and effective campaigns. They can also use AI to automate tasks such as lead generation and nurturing, freeing up their time to focus on more strategic initiatives.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If you’re not already using AI-powered CRM, now is the time to start. It’s one of the best investments you can make to improve your customer experience and grow your business.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Tips for getting started with AI-powered CRM</h4><ol><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Identify your needs:</strong>&nbsp;What are your top priorities when it comes to customer relationship management? Are you looking to improve customer satisfaction, reduce churn, or increase sales? Once you know your needs, you can start to look for AI-powered CRM solutions that can help you achieve your goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Choose the right solution:</strong>&nbsp;There are a number of different AI-powered CRM solutions available on the market. When choosing a solution, it’s important to consider the size of your business, your budget, and your specific needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Implement and integrate:</strong>&nbsp;Once you’ve chosen a solution, it’s important to implement it properly and integrate it with your existing systems. This will help you to get the most out of your investment.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Train your team:</strong>&nbsp;Make sure to train your team on how to use the new AI-infused CRM solution. This will help them to get the most out of it and provide the best possible customer experience.</p></li></ol><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>', 'How AI is Transforming CRM to Deliver Better Customer Experiences | TGS Tech Info', 'Discover how AI-powered CRM software uses predictive scoring, sentiment analysis, and intelligent automation to improve customer relationships, boost sales, and drive business growth. Learn implementation tips for your business.\r\n\r\n', 'AI CRM, Artificial Intelligence CRM, AI-powered CRM benefits, predictive scoring in CRM, sentiment analysis CRM, AI chatbots for customer service, customer relationship management AI, AI sales automation, personalized customer experience, AI in customer service, machine learning CRM, lead scoring with AI, AI sales forecasting, CRM automation tools, AI customer insights', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-02-10 16:57:09', 'published', 102796, 0, 7, NULL, '2023-02-10 16:57:09', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL);
INSERT INTO `contents` (`id`, `user_id`, `content_type_id`, `category_id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `tags`, `banner_image`, `pdf_file`, `video_file`, `email_subject`, `email_template`, `case_study_headline`, `case_study_summary`, `custom_fields`, `webhook_url`, `builder_layout`, `builder_content_elements`, `builder_page_data`, `webhook_field_mapping`, `content`, `seo_meta_title`, `seo_meta_description`, `seo_meta_keywords`, `scheduled_publish_date`, `webinar_date`, `hosted_by`, `platform`, `webinar_type`, `join_link`, `published_date`, `status`, `view_count`, `views_count`, `reading_time`, `admin_comment`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_visible_on_site`, `redirect_url`) VALUES
(134, 2, 3, 17, 'Power of Customer Data Platforms (CDPs) for Hyper-Personalization Marketing', 'power-of-customer-data-platforms-cdps-for-hyper-personalization-marketing', 'Discover how Customer Data Platforms (CDPs) enable hyper-personalization marketing by integrating customer data, delivering real-time insights, and creating tailored experiences that boost engagement, loyalty, and conversions. Learn how CDPs help brands understand individual customers and drive business growth.\r\n\r\n', '[\"Customer Data Platform\",\"Hyper-Personalization Marketing\",\"Personalized Marketing\",\"Customer Experience\",\"Customer Engagement\",\"Data Integration\",\"Marketing Technology\",\"Customer Loyalty\",\"Conversion Optimization\",\"Real-Time Marketing\",\"Customer Segmentation\"]', 'banner_image-1784051103083-695029195.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2>Power of Customer Data Platforms (CDPs) for Hyper-Personalization Marketing</h2><p>In the ever-evolving landscape of digital marketing, personalization has emerged as a game-changer. Today’s consumers expect brands to understand their preferences and needs, and they are more likely to engage with and remain loyal to businesses that offer tailored experiences. This shift in consumer behavior has given rise to the concept of hyper-personalization marketing, and at the heart of this strategy lies the Customer Data Platform (CDP).</p><h3>Understanding Hyper-Personalization Marketing</h3><p>Hyper-personalization marketing goes beyond the traditional one-size-fits-all approach. It involves creating highly targeted and customized content and experiences for individual customers. The goal is to make customers feel understood, valued, and engaged, ultimately driving conversion and loyalty.</p><p>Hyper-personalization involves not only using demographic data but also understanding customer behaviors, preferences, and even real-time interactions. It’s about delivering the right message to the right person at the right time. This level of&nbsp;personalization&nbsp;can significantly impact a brand’s relationship with its customers.</p><h3>The Role of CDPs in Hyper-Personalization</h3><p>Customer Data Platforms play a pivotal role in achieving hyper-personalization marketing. A CDP is a centralized repository that collects and stores data from various sources, including website interactions, email responses, social media activity, and offline interactions. This consolidated data enables marketers to gain a 360-degree view of each customer.</p><h3>Here’s how CDPs empower hyper-personalization marketing:</h3><p><strong>1. Data Integration:</strong>&nbsp;CDPs seamlessly integrate data from various touchpoints, erasing data silos and providing a holistic view of customer interactions. This integration allows marketers to create more accurate customer profiles.</p><p><strong>2. Real-time Insights:</strong>&nbsp;With real-time data processing, CDPs allow marketers to access up-to-the-minute insights about individual customer behaviors and preferences. This is crucial for timely and relevant marketing campaigns.</p><p><strong>3. Segmentation and Targeting:&nbsp;</strong>CDPs enable the creation of highly specific customer segments. Marketers can use these segments to target customers with content and offers that are most likely to resonate with them.</p><p><strong>4. Personalized Content:&nbsp;</strong>Armed with a wealth of data, CDPs make it easier to craft content that speaks directly to individual customers. Whether it’s product recommendations, personalized emails, or tailored website experiences, CDPs provide the tools for creating content that feels personal.</p><p><strong>5. Automated Campaigns:&nbsp;</strong>CDPs support automation by triggering personalized marketing campaigns based on customer behavior. For example, if a customer abandons a shopping cart, the CDP can trigger an email with a tailored message and product recommendations.</p><h3>The Impact of Hyper-Personalization Marketing</h3><p>Hyper-personalization marketing has a profound impact on the customer journey and, consequently, a brand’s bottom line. Let’s explore some of the notable effects:</p><p><strong>1. Enhanced Customer Engagement:&nbsp;</strong>Customers are more likely to engage with personalized content. This results in longer website visits, increased click-through rates, and a higher likelihood of sharing content.</p><p><strong>2. Improved Customer Loyalty:&nbsp;</strong>Personalized experiences make customers feel valued, fostering loyalty and increasing the likelihood of repeat purchases.</p><p><strong>3. Higher Conversion Rates:&nbsp;</strong>By delivering relevant content and offers, hyper-personalization marketing increases conversion rates, driving revenue and profit.</p><p><strong>4. Reduced Marketing Costs:&nbsp;</strong>By targeting only the most relevant customers, marketers can optimize their ad spend and marketing resources.</p><p><strong>5. Reduced Churn:&nbsp;</strong>Understanding customer behavior allows brands to identify potential churn risks and intervene with personalized retention strategies.</p><h3>Challenges of Implementing Hyper-Personalization Marketing</h3><p>While hyper-personalization offers numerous benefits, it’s not without its challenges. Managing vast amounts of customer data, ensuring data privacy and security, and maintaining real-time capabilities can be complex. CDPs address many of these challenges by providing a centralized, secure, and scalable solution for data management.</p><p>In the age of hyper-personalization marketing, Customer Data Platforms are the backbone of successful customer-centric strategies. They provide the tools and insights necessary to understand individual customer preferences, behaviors, and needs. With CDPs, marketers can deliver personalized content and experiences that resonate with customers, resulting in improved engagement, loyalty, and conversion rates. To stay ahead in the highly competitive digital landscape, harness the power of CDPs and embrace hyper-personalization marketing to create lasting customer relationships and drive business success. Your brand’s future could depend on it.</p>', 'Power of CDPs for Hyper-Personalization Marketing | Customer Data Platform Guide', 'Learn how Customer Data Platforms (CDPs) enable hyper-personalization marketing with real-time insights, data integration, and personalized content. Boost customer engagement, loyalty, and conversions with CDP-powered strategies.', 'Customer Data Platform, CDP, hyper-personalization marketing, personalized marketing, customer engagement, data integration, marketing automation, customer loyalty, real-time insights, customer segmentation', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-02-14 11:40:40', 'published', 189045, 0, 4, NULL, '2023-02-14 11:40:40', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(135, 2, 2, 16, 'Why the Future of HR Technology Needs More Women in Leadership', 'why-the-future-of-hr-technology-needs-more-women-in-leadership', 'Artificial intelligence is transforming how companies recruit, evaluate, and manage talent. But who designs these systems matters enormously. This article explores why HR technology-from AI hiring tools to workforce analytics-produces better outcomes when women lead its development, architecture, and governance. Beyond diversity arguments, this is about trust, fairness, risk management, and building systems that reflect the real complexities of modern work.', '[\"Women in HR Technology\",\"HR Tech Leadership\",\"Diversity in Tech\",\"AI in HR\",\"Algorithmic Bias\",\"Gender Equity in Workplace\",\"HR Technology Trends\",\"Future of Work\",\"Workforce Analytics\",\"Talent Management\",\"People Operations\",\"HR Innovation\",\"Women in Leadership\",\"HR Digital Transformation\",\"HR Product Development\"]', 'banner_image-1784051693010-591971768.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Artificial intelligence is reshaping how companies recruit, evaluate, and manage people. At the same time, the workforce itself is demanding fairness, transparency, and flexibility in ways that older HR systems were never designed to support.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Human Resources, as a profession, has long included strong female leadership. Yet the deeper layers of HR technology, product development, platform architecture, venture funding, and enterprise buying decisions remain far more male-dominated than the profession it serves.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">More women shaping HR technology is not simply a diversity argument. It is a design argument. A governance argument. In some ways, it is a risk management argument.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Below are ten reasons the future of HR technology is stronger when more women are in the room where these systems are designed and deployed.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">1. HR Technology Is About People, Not Just Platforms</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The HR tech market likes to talk about automation. Workflow orchestration. AI-powered hiring pipelines.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">However, the real measure of these systems is not technical sophistication. It is whether employees trust them.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Women leaders in HR have historically pushed for systems that account for lived workplace realities. Caregiving responsibilities. Career breaks. Unequally distributed opportunities.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Those realities rarely appear in product roadmaps unless someone insists they should.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">2. AI in Hiring Carries Bias Risk That Cannot Be Engineered Away</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Algorithmic hiring tools promise efficiency. They screen candidates faster than any human recruiter could.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">However, the underlying training data often reflects decades of historical hiring patterns. Those patterns include gender bias, even when companies claim otherwise.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Women leaders tend to push harder on these questions. Not because they distrust technology, but because they have experienced the consequences of flawed systems.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Sometimes that means slowing deployment. Sometimes, rejecting tools that look impressive but cannot explain how decisions are made.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">That friction is healthy.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">3. Employee Experience Is Not a Soft Metric Anymore</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Many HR technology vendors still frame employee experience as an engagement feature. Surveys, dashboards, sentiment analysis.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The problem is that engagement tools often measure symptoms rather than causes.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Women leaders in HR frequently focus on structural factors instead. Career progression visibility. Psychological safety. Pay transparency.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">HR technology that captures those realities requires deeper thinking than a quarterly engagement score.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">4. Workforce Analytics Can Easily Become Surveillance</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Modern HR platforms track everything. Productivity patterns. meeting frequency. collaboration networks.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Some organizations interpret that data as insight. Others treat it as a monitoring system.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The difference comes down to leadership choices.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Women executives in HR technology discussions often raise questions about how data affects trust. Whether analytics tools empower employees or quietly pressure them.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The answer is rarely obvious.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">5. Hybrid Work Exposed Blind Spots in HR Systems</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The pandemic accelerated remote and hybrid work. HR technology vendors responded quickly with collaboration analytics and digital workplace platforms.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">However, many of those tools were built around assumptions that favored traditional work patterns.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Women leaders often highlighted a different issue. Flexibility is not just about location. It is about caregiving schedules, life transitions, and uneven expectations across teams.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Technology that ignores those dynamics may reinforce inequities rather than solve them.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">6. Product Innovation Improves When Perspectives Expand</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The HR technology market is crowded. Hundreds of vendors are promising similar capabilities.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">True innovation usually emerges when teams approach workforce challenges from unexpected angles.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Women founders and product leaders have introduced ideas that were previously overlooked. Skills-based hiring models. Returnship platforms. Caregiver support benefits are integrated into HR systems.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These ideas rarely originate from homogeneous leadership teams.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">7. Ethical Governance of HR AI Needs Broader Leadership</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Enterprise leaders are starting to ask harder questions about <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://hrtechnologyinsights.com/featured-article/what-happens-when-your-boss-is-an-algorithm-the-rise-of-ai-managers\">AI governance</a>. Not only accuracy. Also, fairness, accountability, and explainability.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">HR technology sits in a particularly sensitive position. Decisions about people’s careers increasingly pass through algorithmic systems.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Women leaders frequently push for governance frameworks that go beyond compliance checklists. Clear audit trails. Bias testing. Human oversight.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is not glamorous work. But it determines whether AI in HR earns long-term credibility.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">8. The HR Tech Ecosystem Still Lacks Visible Role Models</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Conferences in the HR technology industry often showcase impressive innovation. Yet keynote stages and startup founder lists still skew heavily male.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Representation matters here in practical ways. Investors notice who gets visibility. Young professionals notice who seems welcome in technical leadership roles.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Women leaders in HR technology change that dynamic simply by occupying the space.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">9. Talent Platforms Shape Opportunity Distribution</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Recruiting systems, internal mobility platforms, and performance management tools influence who gets seen inside organizations.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When those systems prioritize narrow career paths or outdated performance signals, they quietly reinforce existing inequalities.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Women leaders tend to challenge these assumptions. They question whether promotion algorithms reflect potential or just tenure.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is uncomfortable territory. But necessary.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">10. HR Technology Is Becoming Strategic Infrastructure</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ten years ago, HR systems were mostly administrative. Payroll, benefits, compliance.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Today, they influence workforce planning, skills development, and organizational strategy.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">That shift makes leadership diversity even more important. The technology now shapes how companies think about talent itself.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If only one perspective defines those systems, the result will be incomplete.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Decisions Behind the Systems</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The conversation about women in technology often focuses on coding pipelines or engineering roles. HR technology presents a different kind of challenge.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Here, the profession already includes many women. The power to shape the technology behind it does not.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Closing that gap will not happen through symbolic gestures or annual awareness campaigns. It will happen when more women lead HR tech startups, architect enterprise workforce platforms, and influence the decisions behind the algorithms quietly running inside modern organizations.</p>', 'Why the Future of HR Technology Needs More Women in Leadership | HR Tech & Diversity', 'AI is transforming HR-but who designs these systems matters. Discover why women leaders are essential for fair, trustworthy, and effective HR technology that serves real workforce needs.', 'women in HR technology, HR tech leadership, diversity in technology, AI in human resources, algorithmic bias in hiring, gender equity in workplace, future of work technology, HR innovation, ethical AI in HR, workforce analytics, talent management systems, women in tech leadership', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-02-16 15:23:11', 'published', 147489, 3, 5, NULL, '2023-02-16 15:23:11', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL);
INSERT INTO `contents` (`id`, `user_id`, `content_type_id`, `category_id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `tags`, `banner_image`, `pdf_file`, `video_file`, `email_subject`, `email_template`, `case_study_headline`, `case_study_summary`, `custom_fields`, `webhook_url`, `builder_layout`, `builder_content_elements`, `builder_page_data`, `webhook_field_mapping`, `content`, `seo_meta_title`, `seo_meta_description`, `seo_meta_keywords`, `scheduled_publish_date`, `webinar_date`, `hosted_by`, `platform`, `webinar_type`, `join_link`, `published_date`, `status`, `view_count`, `views_count`, `reading_time`, `admin_comment`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_visible_on_site`, `redirect_url`) VALUES
(136, 2, 2, 16, 'The AI Hiring Gap: Why LinkedIn\'s Skills Data Reveals a Management Crisis, Not a Skills Shortage', 'the-ai-hiring-gap-why-linkedins-skills-data-reveals-a-management-crisis-not-a-skills-shortage', 'LinkedIn\'s latest Skills on the Rise data shows prompt engineering, LLMOps, and AI integration skills growing faster than traditional programming languages. But hiring leaders are misreading the signal. This isn\'t a skills transition-it\'s a management transition disguised as a workforce trend. Organizations aren\'t struggling to find people who can use AI tools. They\'re struggling to find people willing and able to take responsibility for decisions produced with those tools. This article unpacks what the data actually means, why hiring models haven\'t caught up to operating models, and how companies should rethink talent evaluation, role design, and accountability in the age of AI-assisted work.', '[\"AI Skills Gap\",\"AI Talent Management\",\"AI Workforce\",\"Future of Work\",\"AI Hiring Strategy\",\"Prompt Engineering\",\"LLMOps\",\"Talent Evaluation\",\"AI Operations\",\"AI Governance\",\"AI Risk Management\",\"Human-AI Collaboration\"]', 'banner_image-1784052055976-298040678.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hiring leaders think the AI transition is a skills transition. It isn’t. What the latest LinkedIn Skills on the Rise data actually shows is a management shift hiding inside a workforce trend.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Organizations are not struggling to find people who can use AI tools. They are struggling to find people willing and able to take responsibility for decisions produced with those tools.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The fastest-growing capabilities now combine prompt engineering, system integration, and people coordination. That combination is not accidental. It reflects a change in the nature of work itself.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI systems do not simply help employees produce output. They generate recommendations, classifications, risk signals, and customer-facing actions. Someone inside the organization must validate those outcomes, intervene when they fail, and stand behind the result.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Most companies are still hiring as if they are adding productivity. In practice they are assigning accountability. The hiring model has not caught up to the operating model, and the LinkedIn data quietly exposes the gap.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Rise of AI-Enabled Work Isn’t About Code</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It’s About Decision Flow</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Listen: prompt engineering and large-language model work dominate the growth list, but that doesn’t mean engineering leaders should hire prompt jockeys and call it strategy.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Prompt design is not just syntax mastery. It’s shaping how systems make decisions - a managerial act in technical clothing.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Coding itself is not disappearing. Python and foundational languages still matter. However, the centre of gravity has shifted.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Engineering success in 2026 is less about building components and more about orchestrating autonomous and semi-autonomous systems so they produce reliable, compliant output.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This is work that lives at the intersection of domain context, data pipelines, prompt structures, and risk management. That intersection is where real organisational leverage lives. Most hiring teams are still chasing traditional stacks. That’s a mistake.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Signal Inside the Data</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The pattern is unusually consistent. The fastest-growing engineering capabilities are not programming languages but AI interaction skills.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Retrieval-Augmented Generation, LLMOps, and frameworks such as LangChain are rising alongside tools like GitHub Copilot and Google Gemini.&nbsp;</p><img src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\"><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Together they point to a change in what engineers actually do day-to-day. Less writing software from scratch. More structuring context, connecting models to company data, and supervising machine output.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Soft Skills on a Technical Skills List Reveals a Deeper Reality</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">LinkedIn’s report includes team collaboration and people management in what it calls <em>“fastest-growing engineering skills.”&nbsp;</em></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It means this: engineering teams are recognising that technical execution is inseparable from human orchestration.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When engineers have to work across product, legal, ethics, data governance and compliance to deploy AI systems, being good at handoffs matters. Not just good - mission-critical. That’s not a soft add-on. That’s part of delivery.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hiring for communication and leadership inside technical orgs is not fluff. It’s a response to project complexity that AI has amplified, not eliminated.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Entry-Level Work Is Paradoxically Expanding and Contracting</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">There’s a weird contradiction this time. Entry-level coding tasks used to be the training ground for rising engineers. However, with generative systems already capable of writing, refactoring and debugging code, a chunk of that starter work is evaporating.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the same time, organizations still need foundation builders - people who can understand context, integrate APIs, and operate production workflows.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">However, that work isn’t entry-level in the classical sense. It requires complex judgement.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Skills Growth Doesn’t Equal Talent Availability</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Look around. Companies are advertising for prompt engineers, LLMOps specialists, and AI integrators like they’re commodities, but they aren’t. The fact they’re listed as ‘fastest-growing’ is a clue: demand is outrunning supply.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hiring leaders confuse learning velocity with depth of expertise. That gap will produce hiring mistakes - costly ones - unless expectations are anchored in what people can actually deliver versus what they can label on a profile.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The moment machines participate in producing decisions, the company is no longer evaluating technical skill alone. It is evaluating operational judgment under uncertainty. Most hiring processes are not designed to measure that.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Evaluation Problem No One Is Talking About</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">There is a deeper issue hidden underneath the hiring confusion. Many hiring managers do not actually know how to evaluate AI operators.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Traditional engineering interviews were built to assess code correctness, architecture decisions, and system design patterns. AI-augmented work is different. A candidate can generate a working solution using tools, context retrieval, and iterative prompting without writing much original code at all. That makes it harder to distinguish genuine capability from tool familiarity.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As a result, companies are increasingly selecting candidates based on vocabulary alignment instead of operational competence. The organization believes it hired an AI practitioner.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In reality, it hired someone proficient at discussing AI. The evaluation model has not caught up with the work model.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Until leadership learns how to assess judgment, supervision, and failure-handling in machine-assisted workflows, hiring errors will not be rare. They will be systemic.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Put Less Faith in Static Roles, More in Capability Statements</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Job descriptions are outdated. They assume roles are stable and predictable. They’re not.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">LinkedIn’s skill growth patterns show that the boundaries between roles are dissolving at the same time that expectations are rising. Prompt engineering, people coordination, system integration, operational risk - all in one job description.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">That means hiring leaders should stop grammatical role writing and start writing capability statements: <em>“Can operate X, evaluate risk with Y, and deliver outcomes in Z timeframe.”</em></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hiring the person who checks all boxes on a job description means hiring someone who is already a unicorn. Unicorns are mythical in practice.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">What This Actually Changes Inside Organizations</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The implication of the skills report is not that jobs are changing. Organizations always adapt to new tools. The implication is that responsibility is being redistributed inside companies.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When employees rely on AI to generate outputs that affect customers, pricing, approvals, or compliance, the company still owns the decision. If no individual or team clearly owns validation and escalation, errors do not remain technical problems. They become operational incidents.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Companies that adapt hiring, evaluation, and management structures around this shift will gain leverage and speed. Companies that do not will still deploy AI, but they will do so without defined ownership of outcomes.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">That creates a predictable pattern: inconsistent decisions, internal blame cycles, and eventually regulatory or customer trust issues.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This is why the LinkedIn data matters. It is not forecasting a new talent market. It is revealing a new management requirement. The organizations that recognize this will redesign roles around accountability for machine-assisted decisions.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The ones that don’t will believe they adopted AI successfully right up until a failure forces them to discover who was actually responsible.</p>', 'The AI Hiring Gap: Why LinkedIn Skills Data Reveals a Management Crisis | AI Talent Strategy', 'Prompt engineering and LLMOps are rising fast. But hiring leaders are misreading the data. The real challenge isn\'t finding AI users-it\'s finding people who take responsibility for AI decisions.', 'AI Skills Gap,LinkedIn Skills on the Rise,AI Talent Management,AI Accountability,AI Hiring Strategy', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-02-22 13:06:42', 'published', 90981, 3, 6, NULL, '2023-02-22 13:06:42', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL);
INSERT INTO `contents` (`id`, `user_id`, `content_type_id`, `category_id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `tags`, `banner_image`, `pdf_file`, `video_file`, `email_subject`, `email_template`, `case_study_headline`, `case_study_summary`, `custom_fields`, `webhook_url`, `builder_layout`, `builder_content_elements`, `builder_page_data`, `webhook_field_mapping`, `content`, `seo_meta_title`, `seo_meta_description`, `seo_meta_keywords`, `scheduled_publish_date`, `webinar_date`, `hosted_by`, `platform`, `webinar_type`, `join_link`, `published_date`, `status`, `view_count`, `views_count`, `reading_time`, `admin_comment`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_visible_on_site`, `redirect_url`) VALUES
(137, 2, 2, 16, 'AI at Work in HR Tech and Employee Experience', 'ai-at-work-in-hr-tech-and-employee-experience', 'Artificial intelligence is fundamentally reshaping the expectations placed on HR leadership. No longer confined to traditional people management, HR leaders now bear accountability for workforce capacity, productivity outcomes, and organizational risk alongside finance and operations. This article explores how AI is transforming talent acquisition, workforce planning, employee experience, and HR workflows-and why speed without structure is the greatest risk facing HR technology today. The question is no longer whether HR will adopt AI, but whether it will be implemented as part of workforce strategy or applied superficially as another software feature.', '[\"AI in HR\",\"HR Leadership\",\"Artificial Intelligence at Work\",\"Talent Acquisition\",\"Workforce Planning\",\"HR Technology\",\"Future of Work\",\"AI Governance\",\"Generative AI in HR\",\"HR Digital Transformation\",\"HRIS\",\"Talent Management\",\"HR Automation\"]', 'banner_image-1784052422893-657243186.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI at work is reshaping the expectations placed on HR leadership.&nbsp; HR leaders now operate far beyond traditional people management responsibilities.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">They are accountable for workforce capacity, productivity outcomes, and organizational risk alongside finance and operations leadership.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Boards expect measurable returns from AI investments, while employees expect a more responsive and supportive work environment rather than additional layers of automation. This tension is precisely why AI at work in HR tech has become a leadership priority.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The question is no longer whether HR will adopt AI. It is whether it will be implemented as part of workforce strategy or applied superficially as another software feature.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Talent Acquisition Is Becoming a Data Science Function</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Recruiting was the first visible AI use case, but the shift is deeper than resume screening.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">According to Global LinkedIn 2024 talent data, AI-enabled sourcing&nbsp;significantly reduces time to identify qualified candidates. Yet speed is not the strategic lever. Signal quality is.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Modern HR tech platforms analyze skills adjacency, project exposure, and career progression patterns. This matters in a labor market defined by skills shortages and hybrid roles. Organizations are hiring for capability clusters, not static job descriptions.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the same time, regulatory scrutiny is rising. The Equal Employment Opportunity Commission has increased oversight of automated decision systems in hiring. AI must inform decisions, not replace human judgment. Governance is no longer optional.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Workforce Planning Is Shifting from Roles to Skills</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The more significant disruption is in workforce strategy.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The World Economic Forum projects that 44 percent of core skills will change by 2027. Traditional headcount planning models cannot keep up with that velocity.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI-powered HR platforms are building dynamic skills graphs from performance data, learning systems, and project history. This enables leaders to see capability gaps in near real time and redeploy internal talent before turning to external hiring.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">But here is the constraint. Data fragmentation.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Most enterprises still operate across disconnected HRIS, ATS, and LMS environments. AI layered on inconsistent taxonomies produces impressive dashboards with questionable reliability. The pace of AI adoption is outstripping data readiness in many organizations.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Employee Experience: Automation at Scale</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI-driven HR service agents are now standard in large enterprises. Operationally, this reduces service backlog and improves access across distributed workforces.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Strategically, the risk is perception. Employees accept automation that removes friction. They resist automation that feels like monitoring. Sentiment analysis and productivity analytics must be governed transparently or they will erode trust faster than they create insight.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Generative AI Is Compressing HR Workflows</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Generative AI is accelerating policy drafting, learning content creation, and performance documentation. McKinsey &amp; Company reported in 2024 that a substantial portion of administrative HR activities is technically automatable.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The productivity gain is clear. So is the accountability burden.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Performance feedback and policy language carry legal implications. HR leaders cannot outsource compliance risk to a language model.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Real Trend: Speed Without Structure Fails</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The defining HR technology trend is not AI adoption. It is AI compression. Deployment cycles are shorter. Vendor roadmaps are moving quarterly, not annually. Expectations from executive leadership are immediate.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The organizations keeping pace are not simply buying AI features. They are standardizing skills taxonomies, formalizing AI governance, and tying AI outputs to workforce metrics such as internal mobility, time to productivity, and retention of high performers.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI at work is accelerating HR transformation. The question for leadership is whether structure is accelerating at the same rate.</p>', 'AI at Work: How HR Leadership Is Being Reshaped by Artificial Intelligence | HR Tech Strategy', 'AI is reshaping HR leadership beyond traditional people management. Explore how talent acquisition, workforce planning, and governance are evolving-and why structure must keep pace with speed.', 'AI in HR,HR Leadership,Artificial Intelligence at Work,Talent Acquisition AI,Generative AI HR,People Analytics', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-02-24 17:49:13', 'published', 7440, 3, 3, NULL, '2023-02-24 17:49:13', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(138, 2, 2, 16, 'What the Three Laws of Robotics Mean for HR Tech Governance', 'what-the-three-laws-of-robotics-mean-for-hr-tech-governance', 'Isaac Asimov\'s three laws of robotics were written for science fiction, yet they offer a surprisingly practical governance framework for AI in HR. This article explores how hiring algorithms, performance analytics, and workforce management systems must prioritize harm prevention, human authority, and accountability-before efficiency. Because when AI makes decisions about people\'s careers, the stakes are far too high for blind trust.', '[\"HR Technology\",\"AI in HR\",\"Algorithmic Bias\",\"Employment Law\",\"AI Governance\",\"Workforce Analytics\",\"HR Compliance\",\"HR Innovation\",\"People Operations\",\"HR Digital Transformation\"]', 'banner_image-1784052826475-46659701.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In 1942, Isaac Asimov wrote a short story titled \"<em>Runaround</em>.\" He wasn’t trying to design a compliance policy. He was trying to make science fiction believable. Yet his <strong>three laws of robotics</strong> now read like a governance framework for AI systems operating inside modern organizations.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">HR technology has quietly become one of the most consequential deployment environments for artificial intelligence. Recruiting screeners, internal mobility matching, performance analytics, attrition prediction, automated disciplinary flagging, and compensation benchmarking.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hiring screeners, promotion analytics, behavioral monitoring, internal mobility matching, and attrition prediction systems are already making or shaping employment decisions across large organizations. In 2024 alone, AI-enabled hiring tools screened over 30 million job applications in the United States, while generating hundreds of discrimination complaints.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Unlike marketing AI or sales forecasting, HR decisions sit directly at the intersection of employment law, discrimination risk, and reputational exposure.&nbsp;</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The First Law: Do Not Harm Humans</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Asimov’s first law</em>: A robot may not harm a human being, or, through inaction, allow a human to come to harm.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hiring algorithms already shape who gets interviews. The U.S. EEOC’s technical guidance on AI in employment makes clear that employers remain legally accountable for discriminatory outcomes produced by automated hiring tools, even when those tools are provided by third-party vendors.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The New York City Automated Employment Decision Tool (AEDT) law now requires bias audits and public disclosure of automated hiring systems used in recruitment. Multiple U.S. states are drafting similar rules, and the White House’s 2023–2024 AI Executive Order framework instructed federal agencies to scrutinize employment-related AI under civil rights law.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Here is the governance implication: HR AI harm rarely appears as a system failure. It appears as a statistically subtle pattern.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A hiring model does not need to malfunction to create legal exposure. Even a modest statistical disparity against applicants over 40 can support a disparate-impact claim, as seen in ongoing U.S. litigation over AI screening tools.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">So the first law for HR leaders becomes measurable: Not “avoid biased AI.” Instead, prove the absence of disparate impact.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">That requires ongoing monitoring, not vendor certification. Annual audits will not hold up. Employment decisions happen daily.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Governance shift: </em>HR technology teams now need model performance dashboards similar to financial controls. Adverse impact ratios. Selection rate tracking. Post-hire outcomes segmented by protected class proxies.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Second Law: Obey Human Instructions</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Asimov’s second law:</em> A robot must obey orders given by humans unless those orders conflict with the First Law.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In practice, AI systems are not obedient. They are optimized. And optimization follows metrics, not intent.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Recruiting platforms often train on “successful employees.” That sounds reasonable. Until you ask what “successful” means. Promotion rate? Manager ratings? Retention?</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Each of those contains managerial subjectivity. In a 2024 Stanford HAI review of enterprise AI systems, researchers observed that organizations frequently encode internal management preferences into algorithms without recognizing that they have formalized them into policy. The algorithm becomes a quiet rulebook.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Managers then start trusting the system more than their own judgment. Not because the system is smarter, but because it looks objective.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">HR leaders call this automation bias. Psychologists call it authority substitution.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The governance failure is subtle. Humans think they are giving instructions to software. In reality, the software begins shaping human decisions.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A recruiter stops advancing a candidate because the system labeled them “low fit.” The recruiter cannot articulate why. The algorithm cannot legally explain why. Yet the decision stands.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">That breaks Asimov’s second law. The machine is no longer obeying human judgment. Human judgment is deferring to machine output.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Governance response, therefore, cannot rely on “human in the loop.” Regulators increasingly view passive approval as insufficient oversight. The 2024 NIST AI Risk Management Framework guidance clarifies that human review must be meaningful, informed, and empowered to override the system.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Which means HR leaders must train managers on how AI works. Not technically. Operationally.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A manager approving a termination flagged by an algorithm should understand model confidence, input variables, and false positive rates. Otherwise, the human reviewer is ceremonial.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Many HR organizations have deployed AI faster than they have trained supervisors to question it.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>The Third Law: Protect the Robot’s Existence</strong></h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Asimov’s third law</em>: A robot must protect its own existence as long as it does not conflict with the first two laws.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Here is the modern translation: enterprise systems protect themselves through opacity.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Vendors increasingly restrict model transparency, citing intellectual property protection. Explainability becomes limited to confidence scores and generic feature importance statements.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Yet employment decisions are legally discoverable. In litigation, courts can compel disclosure of decision logic. Employers, not vendors, will be required to defend outcomes.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This creates a structural governance contradiction.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Procurement teams often accept black-box HR AI tools because they perform well in pilot metrics like time-to-hire. Legal teams, however, must defend those decisions under Title VII and ADA standards. The system is optimized to protect itself. The employer must justify it.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Recent cases in employment litigation have begun testing algorithmic accountability standards. Courts are increasingly receptive to the argument that the lack of explainability itself may demonstrate negligence in employment decision-making.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Zendesk’s recent acquisition of Unleash expands its employee service capabilities by embedding AI-powered enterprise search into daily workflows.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The third law, therefore, collides with the first. A system designed to protect proprietary functioning may prevent an employer from proving it did not harm employees.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This is no longer a technology selection issue. It is a governance architecture issue.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">HR leaders now need cross-functional oversight committees, including legal, data science, and compliance. Not quarterly. Continuous.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Algorithm Is Already Your Manager</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI in HR is not a tooling decision anymore, and not even a digital transformation initiative. It is the delegation of managerial judgment to a system that does not carry legal responsibility, while the organization still does.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">That makes HR technology governance less about model accuracy and more about institutional accountability.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These systems now influence who gets hired, who advances, and who exits. They operate inside employment law, not IT architecture. Treating them like productivity software is the mistake many organizations are making.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Asimov pictured robots on factory floors and space stations. The modern version sits inside performance reviews, candidate rankings, and disciplinary alerts.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The sequence still matters. Prevent harm first. Keep human judgment authoritative second. Only then worry about protecting the system.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Many companies optimized for efficiency before legitimacy. The next phase of HR AI adoption will be defined by reversing that order.</p>', 'Asimov\'s Three Laws of HR AI | Ethical Governance for Workforce Technology', 'AI shapes who gets hired, promoted, and managed. Asimov\'s three laws of robotics offer a powerful governance framework for ethical, accountable HR technology. Essential reading for HR leaders.', 'HR AI Governance,Algorithmic Bias in Hiring,Employment Law AI Compliance,AI Discrimination Lawsuits,HR Technology Ethics,Workforce Analytics Compliance', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-02-28 12:32:44', 'published', 109255, 1, 6, NULL, '2023-02-28 12:32:44', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(139, 2, 10, 16, 'Maximizing the Role of HR with Analytics', 'maximizing-the-role-of-hr-with-analytics', 'Modern HR analytics is transforming how organizations attract, retain, and manage talent-moving HR from educated guesswork to data-driven strategic decision-making. Yet while analytics adoption in operations reaches 77%, HR lags at just 14%. This article explores how workforce analytics tools provide deep visibility into skills gaps, performance, and future workforce needs, enabling HR to become a true agent of business success. Discover why data-driven insights are no longer optional in today\'s fiercely competitive talent landscape.', '[\"HR Analytics\",\"People Analytics\",\"Workforce Analytics\",\"Data-Driven HR\",\"HR Technology\",\"Talent Management\",\"Human Resources Innovation\",\"HR Strategy\",\"People Operations\",\"HR Data\"]', 'banner_image-1784053438204-745134963.webp', 'pdf_file-1784053438388-436718923.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784053291565,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784053291757,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784053291926,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"},{\"id\":1784053292093,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">Introduction</h2><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Deep-dive analytics tools have completely transformed the way many organizations do business, helping to remove the guesswork from major areas of operations and provide everybody with the clear, actionable answers they need to make informed business decisions.<br>The benefits of sophisticated analytics are being reaped across the business. However, according to Deloitte, HR is lagging-only 14 percent of companies use analytics in HR, compared to 77 percent using these tools in operations.<br>With the speed of change increasing and new business models emerging every day, modern organizations demand faster and more precise actions from HR than ever before. Today’s employees and candidates expect their experiences from internal systems such as HR to be as simple and convenient as<br>those they receive in their personal lives (such as when they’re buying things online). As the war for the best talent grows increasingly fierce, HR simply cannot do without the insight and agility delivered by modern analytics.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">How analytics tools are helping increase the efficiency and strategic value of HR</h2><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Today, talent is your business’ top competitive differentiator. The people you employ and the skills among them determine your ability to innovate and respond to market and business changes at speed-and ultimately define your capabilities as a business.<br>The HR department is tasked with the incredibly difficult and important task of attracting, retaining, and managing that talent effectively. It’s a tough job-and as competition for talent increases, it’s only getting harder-but modern HR analytics can make it more manageable. The Boston Consulting Group says that prioritizing data-driven insights is one of the three hallmarks of truly great modern HR departments, and when you consider how inefficient paper-based workforce analysis is, it’s easy to see why.<br>For decades, key HR decisions have been made using complex spreadsheets of raw data that staff have to manually examine by hand and spend hours trying to extract insight from. This isn’t just massively time-consuming; it can also lead to inconsistent or incorrect decisions that end up costing the business millions<br>in both mistakes and missed opportunities.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">One of the big questions HR constantly has to ask is whether the business has the right people to support development projects and achieve its strategic goals. With access to the right analytics, HR can stop asking questions about its data and cut straight to the answers. The deep workforce visibility granted by analytics offers immediate insight into skills gaps, performance, potential future issues, and development needs at a glance-all through a simple, visual dashboard.<br>Evidence-based decision-making will replace the “educated” guess. With that information at their fingertips, HR professionals are equipped to take on a more strategic role within their organization and become agents of business change and success.<br>The team can make well-informed decisions for the organization’s future instead of deducing from anecdotal information and experiences. Precise analysis also frees HR professionals from repetitive, manual information analysis to focus more time on more strategic priorities, e.g., attracting talent that can help the business rise above the competition and stay ahead.</p>', 'HR Analytics: Transforming People Decisions from Guesswork to Data-Driven Strategy', 'HR analytics delivers deep workforce visibility into skills gaps, performance, and future needs. Discover why data-driven HR is essential for winning the talent war and driving business success.', 'HR analytics, people analytics, workforce analytics, data-driven HR, HR technology, talent management, workforce planning, HR strategy, talent acquisition, employee retention, skills gap analysis', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-02 14:15:15', 'published', 187696, 1, 3, NULL, '2023-03-02 14:15:15', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(140, 2, 10, 5, '27 Best Practice Tips on Amazon Web Services Security Groups', '27-best-practice-tips-on-amazon-web-services-security-groups', 'AWS Security Groups are among the most frequently used-and frequently misconfigured-components in cloud environments. This white paper, based on over 15 years of hands-on experience with AWS since 2008, presents 27 actionable best practices for configuring, managing, and automating Security Groups. From least-privilege access controls and proper naming conventions to automated auditing, IAM governance, and disaster recovery planning, these proven tips help organizations strengthen their cloud security posture, reduce attack surfaces, and maintain operational excellence in AWS environments. ', '[\"AWS Security Groups\",\"AWS Security\",\"Security Group Configuration\",\"AWS VPC Security\",\"DevSecOps\",\"AWS Automation\",\"Security Compliance\",\"IAM Policies\",\"AWS Operations\",\"Network Security\",\"Cloud Risk Management\",\"Cloud Security Posture\",\"Security Automation\"]', 'banner_image-1784053801803-973983903.webp', 'pdf_file-1784053801887-942757655.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784053542069,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784053542525,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784053542821,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784053543033,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>AWS Security Groups are one of the most used and abused configurations inside an AWS environment if you are using them on cloud for quite a long time. Since AWS security groups are simple to configure, users, many times ignore the importance of it and do not follow best practices relating to it. In reality, operating on AWS security groups every day is much more intensive and complex than configuring them once. A fact that nobody talks about! So, in this article, based on our experience in dealing with AWS Security groups since 2008, here are a set of best practices related to configuration and day-to-day operations.</p><p>In the world of security, proactive and reactive speed determines the winner. So, a lot of these best practices should be automated. AWS released so many features in the last few years relating to security, that we should not visualize security groups in isolation. But it just does not make sense anymore. The Security Group should always be seen in the overall security context. Let’s start with the pointers.</p><h4><strong>About the Author</strong></h4><p>Harish Ganesan was the Chief Technology Officer (CTO) of SecureKloud, responsible for the overall technology direction of the SecureKloud products and services. He has around two decades of experience in architecting and developing Cloud Computing, E-commerce, and Mobile application systems. He has also built large internet banking solutions that catered to the needs of millions of users, where security and authentication were critical factors. He is also a prolific blogger and frequent speaker at popular cloud conferences.</p>', 'AWS Security Groups: 27 Best Practice Tips for Cloud Security', 'AWS Security Groups are frequently misconfigured. Discover 27 proven best practices for configuration, automation, and operations from 15+ years of AWS experience.', 'AWS Security Groups, AWS security best practices, cloud security, security group configuration, least privilege access, AWS VPC security, network security AWS, AWS Config rules, security automation', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-06 10:58:46', 'published', 179969, 0, 2, NULL, '2023-03-06 10:58:46', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(142, 2, 10, 2, 'Agentic AI advantage: Unlocking next-level value', 'agentic-ai-advantage-unlocking-next-level-value', 'Agentic AI represents a significant leap forward from generative AI, empowering organizations to automate complex processes, foster human-AI collaboration, and unlock unprecedented business value. Unlike traditional AI systems that simply respond to prompts, AI agents make real-time decisions, adapt to new situations, and learn from interactions-all under appropriate human oversight. From task-oriented document analysis to fully autonomous value chain transformation, the applications are vast. Discover KPMG\'s TACO framework™ for navigating the agentic AI landscape and learn how to turn AI into your competitive edge.', '[\"Agentic AI\",\"Autonomous AI\",\"AI Agents\",\"Generative AI\",\"Enterprise AI\",\"AI Strategy\",\"KPMG\",\"AI Governance\",\"AI Technology\",\"Business Automation\",\"Digital Transformation\",\"AI Adoption\",\"Future of AI\"]', 'banner_image-1784055823545-625917779.webp', 'pdf_file-1784055823777-305083619.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784055766621,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784055766783,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784055766954,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784055767109,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2>Welcome to the age of agentic AI</h2><p>Agentic AI represents a leap forward from generative AI, empowering organizations to automate complex processes, foster human-AI collaboration and unlock unprecedented business value.</p><p>AI agents bring the agency that AI systems need. They blend advanced reasoning from LLMs with planning, orchestration, knowledge, data mining, guardrails and governance to achieve organizational goals through meaningful action.</p><p>They make real-time decisions, adapt to new situations and learn from their interactions and reinforced feedback - all under appropriate levels of human oversight. The range of real-world applications is vast, from task-oriented agents that extract and compare data or documents against standards, to fully autonomous agents capable of transforming entire value chains.</p><h2>From experimentation to implementation&nbsp;-&nbsp;Choosing the right agent for the task</h2><p>KPMG has developed a structured classification system called the TACO frameworkᵀᴹ - Taskers, Automators, Collaborators and Orchestrators - that helps organization make sense of the evolving agentic AI landscape and how to leverage its full capabilities.</p><h2>How KPMG can help</h2><p>Turn AI into your competitive edge&nbsp;- from strategy to execution, with a people - centric approach grounded in trust. KPMG offers a portfolio of services tailored to help you overcome key barriers to agentic AI adoption, with trust and responsible use at every stage of the journey.</p><ul><li><p><strong>KPMG AI Jumpstart - Starting the AI journey</strong></p></li></ul><p>Accelerate your path to value from proof-of-concept to launch to adoption at scale.</p><ul><li><p><strong>KPMG AI Strategy - Creating a path to value</strong></p></li></ul><p>Help shape your agentic AI strategy and business case with an actionable roadmap.</p><ul><li><p><strong>KPMG AI Trust - Enabling trust</strong></p></li></ul><p>AI Trust to help you design, build and deploy agentic AI solutions in a responsible and ethical way.</p><ul><li><p><strong>KPMG AI Workforce - Aligning people and change</strong></p></li></ul><p>Unlock the full potential of agentic AI for, and with, your people during the journey.</p><ul><li><p><strong>KPMG AI Technology - Building data foundations for AI</strong></p></li></ul><p>High-quality data, advanced technology and trust come together to help ensure that AI and other emerging technologies can deliver actionable, accurate and reliable outcomes that create real value.</p>', 'Agentic AI: From Generative Assistants to Autonomous Business Value', 'Agentic AI goes beyond generative AI to make real-time decisions, adapt to new situations, and transform value chains. Discover KPMG\'s TACO framework™ for successful enterprise AI adoption.', 'agentic AI, autonomous AI, AI agents, generative AI, enterprise AI, AI strategy, AI transformation, KPMG, AI governance, responsible AI, AI trust, AI workforce, AI technology, business automation, AI implementation, digital transformation, AI decision-making, human-AI collaboration, AI value creation, TACO framework, AI orchestration, intelligent automation, AI adoption, future of AI', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-08 16:41:17', 'published', 136758, 1, 2, NULL, '2023-03-08 16:41:17', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(143, 2, 10, 5, 'Cybersecurity considerations 2025', 'cybersecurity-considerations-2025', 'CEOs view cybersecurity as the top threat to business growth, and the stakes have never been higher. Drawing from KPMG\'s annual Cybersecurity Considerations report, this article explores eight critical priorities for CISOs in 2025-from the evolving CISO role and AI adoption to platform consolidation, digital identity, and resilience by design. Discover how organizations can mitigate risk, drive growth, and build robust security in an era of ubiquitous digital connections and emerging technologies.', '[\"Cybersecurity 2025\",\"CISO Priorities\",\"Cybersecurity Trends\",\"AI and Cybersecurity\",\"Digital Identity\",\"Cyber Resilience\",\"Risk Management\",\"KPMG Cybersecurity Report\",\"AI Security\",\"Zero Trust\",\"Information Security\",\"Business Resilience\"]', 'banner_image-1784056318460-131583191.webp', 'pdf_file-1784056318591-726297598.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784056265119,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784056265278,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784056265438,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784056265597,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>The digital landscape continues to evolve at pace&nbsp;- unleashing significant challenges and a sense of urgency amid the need for robust cybersecurity measures. Ubiquitous digital connections and fast-emerging technologies such as AI appear to be redefining almost every facet of our professional and personal lives, making cybersecurity not just a business concern but a universal issue that affects all aspects of society. The&nbsp;KPMG 2024 Global CEO Outlook&nbsp;reveals that CEOs view cybersecurity as the top threat to businesses over the last decade.</p><p>The sixth global installment of KPMG’s annual Cybersecurity considerations report examines current and emerging obstacles that organizations are facing across various industries&nbsp;- and eight key cybersecurity considerations they should focus on as the rapid pace of change accelerates in today’s dynamic environment. The KPMG annual Cybersecurity considerations report identifies eight key considerations that CISOs should prioritize in 2025 to help mitigate risk, drive business growth and build resilience.</p><p>Explore the eight key cyber considerations and uncover the key actions organizations can take as they seek to accelerate recovery times, reduce the impact of incidents on employees, customers, and partners and aim to ensure their security plans enable - rather than expose - the business.</p><h2>Explore the eight key cybersecurity considerations for 2025</h2><ul><li><p><strong>The ever-evolving role of the CISO</strong></p></li></ul><p>What CISOs and their teams focus on, and how they interact with the rest of the organization is fluid, as the cybersecurity function becomes more broadly embedded within and better understood across the organization.</p><ul><li><p><strong>The power of the people</strong></p></li></ul><p>As organizations continue to transform their business models in the face of new digital disruptions, many are experiencing real challenges around workload, which is exacerbating the long-discussed cyber skills gap. AI and automation can help, but there is an underlying risk of talent attrition as many teams struggle to cope.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Embed trust as AI proliferates</strong></p></li></ul><p>AI is here to stay and has a place in virtually every organizational function, but there are a number of key cyber and privacy challenges that have the potential to affect the adoption and deployment of AI.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Harness AI for cyber: Racing ahead vs racing safely</strong></p></li></ul><p>Many factors appear to be contributing to the buzz around AI adoption, from a lack of training to the fear of missing out and possibly falling behind. A key challenge is weighing the potential benefits of integrating AI into cyber and privacy functions against the potential risks.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Platform consolidation: Embrace the potential but recognize the risks</strong></p></li></ul><p>Increasingly, many global organizations are looking to reduce the complexity and cost of their technology. Organizations that choose to do so by consolidating tools and services on to a single, or a limited number of platforms should seek to identify and navigate the inherent risks.</p><ul><li><p><strong>The digital identity imperative</strong></p></li></ul><p>Although there are several initiatives around digital identity sprouting up worldwide, interoperability between systems and enhanced authentication due to the emergence of deepfakes remain challenging, whether because of regulations, risk appetite, and/or public opinion regarding the processing of personal and biometric data.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Smart security for smart ecosystems</strong></p></li></ul><p>The rise of smart devices and products worldwide is challenging and changing traditional views and approaches toward security, prompting many regulators to introduce new regimes to ensure these products meet basic security requirements.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Resilience by design: Cybersecurity for businesses and society</strong></p></li></ul><p>Organizations should find a way, from the CISO on down, to create a broad, holistic culture of resilient security throughout their enterprise and with the aim of ensuring all stakeholders are on the same page.</p>', 'Cybersecurity Considerations 2025: Eight Priorities Every CISO Must Address', 'CEOs rank cybersecurity as the top business threat. Explore KPMG\'s eight key cybersecurity considerations for 2025, including AI risks, digital identity, platform consolidation, and resilience by design.', 'cybersecurity 2025, CISO priorities, cybersecurity trends, AI and cybersecurity, digital identity, platform consolidation, cyber resilience, security leadership, risk management, KPMG cybersecurity, AI security, smart device security, cyber skills gap, CISO role, security strategy, information security, cybersecurity governance', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-10 11:24:48', 'published', 138885, 0, 3, NULL, '2023-03-10 11:24:48', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(144, 2, 3, 5, 'Students and teachers fight back cyber attack on University Network', 'students-and-teachers-fight-back-cyber-attack-on-university-network', 'In a remarkable display of resilience, students and staff at UC Irvine joined forces to counter a sophisticated cyber attack on their Discord network. When hackers infiltrated the platform serving 3,000 users with disturbing content and demanded a $1,000 ransom, the university community responded swiftly-banning malicious accounts globally and showcasing the power of collective action against digital threats. This inspiring story demonstrates how educational communities can effectively fight back against cyber criminals.', '[\"Cyber Attack\",\"University Cyber Security\",\"Discord Hack\",\"Student Cybersecurity\",\"Educational Institution Security\",\"Cyber Resilience\",\"Incident Response\",\"Student-Teacher Collaboration\",\"Digital Security\",\"Cybersecurity Awareness\",\"Online Safety\"]', 'banner_image-1784056971950-261762483.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>In recent times, educational institutions have frequently fallen victim to cyber-attacks, with universities, schools, and other facilities being targeted. However, amidst the usual narrative of cyber vulnerabilities, a recent incident stands out as students and staff collaborated to thwart a sophisticated digital attack.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">On January 9, 2024, a hacking group executed a cyber attack on Discord servers associated with the University of California (UC), Irvine. The messaging and social media application served as a communication platform for disseminating crucial curriculum updates to a community of 3,000 users, comprising students and teachers.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><br>Despite the educational institution’s efforts to maintain a secure environment, the hackers successfully infiltrated the discord network, unleashing distressing images and videos featuring both humans and animals. Alina Kim, a college student, described the content as disturbing, including scenes of animal torture and physical abuse.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Responding swiftly, Kim and a group of students, guided by IT staff and teachers, took proactive measures to counter the attack. They systematically banned accounts responsible for spreading the offensive content. While this action may seem modest, its implications are significant-each account ban affects the user globally across all Discord servers, preventing criminals from accessing the account anywhere in the world to perpetuate their malicious activities.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Adding to the gravity of the situation, the hackers brazenly demanded a $1000 ransom to cease their content postings on the university network. This departure from the usual tactics, where defacement and objectionable content dissemination are typically associated with state-funded actors, suggests the involvement of smaller threat actors driven by financial motives.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the face of this digital onslaught, the commendable aspect of the story lies in the resilience of the students and staff who valiantly confronted the hackers. Their collective efforts deserve immense appreciation, as they not only defended their educational community but also showcased the power of unity against cyber threats.</p>', 'UC Irvine Cyber Attack: How Students and Teachers Fought Back and Won', 'When hackers attacked UC Irvine\'s Discord network with disturbing content and a ransom demand, students and teachers united to ban malicious accounts globally. Read their inspiring cyber defense story.', 'UC Irvine cyber attack, Discord hack, university cyber security, student cyber defense, cyber attack on university, educational institution security, ransomware demand, Discord server attack, university network security, cyber resilience, student-teacher collaboration', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-14 15:07:19', 'published', 148007, 0, 2, NULL, '2023-03-14 15:07:19', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(145, 2, 10, 2, 'Beyond the Dashboard: Where AI Helps Enterprise Supply Chains - and Where It Doesn\'t', 'beyond-the-dashboard-where-ai-helps-enterprise-supply-chains-and-where-it-doesnt', 'Supply chains are generating more data than ever, yet most organizations remain stuck looking at dashboards without understanding the \"why\" behind the numbers. This white paper cuts through the AI hype to reveal where machine learning truly drives value-and where human intuition still reigns supreme. Learn how to turn static inventory visibility into actionable intelligence, fix broken lead time data, and avoid the common pitfalls that cause AI initiatives to fail. Discover a practical framework for moving from passive reporting to proactive, data-driven decision-making.', '[\"AI in Supply Chain\",\"Inventory Optimization\",\"Supply Chain Analytics\",\"Lead Time Reduction\",\"Data-Driven Supply Chain\",\"Digital Transformation\",\"S&OP\",\"Supply Chain Visibility\",\"Machine Learning\",\"Operational Efficiency\"]', 'banner_image-1784059817299-842602989.webp', 'pdf_file-1784059817461-101378626.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784059762926,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784059763095,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784059763263,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784059763958,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Supply chains today are drowning in data but still struggling to answer critical questions. Inventory is visible but not always explainable. Lead times exist in the system, but don’t always reflect reality. Improvement opportunities are identified, yet often fail to translate into action.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this white paper, explore four common challenges that prevent organizations from turning supply chain data into better decisions, and learn where AI can provide real value by improving diagnostics, prioritizing action, and uncovering patterns across complex operations.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">What You’ll Learn</h3><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Where AI really improves supply chain outcomes and where it doesn’t</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How to turn “visible” inventory into something you can actually explain and act on</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why many AI initiatives fail and what it takes to drive real impact</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How to spot hidden inefficiencies in lead times, planning settings, and governance</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Download the White Paper</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Discover how leading organizations are moving beyond dashboards to create greater visibility, stronger alignment, and more effective supply chain decisions.</p>', 'Beyond the Dashboard: Where AI Helps Supply Chains', 'Discover where AI delivers real value in supply chains and where it doesn\'t. Learn to turn data into action and fix hidden inefficiencies.', 'AI supply chain, inventory management, supply chain analytics, lead time accuracy, data-driven decisions, supply chain optimization, machine learning logistics', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-16 13:50:50', 'published', 194100, 0, 1, NULL, '2023-03-16 13:50:50', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL);
INSERT INTO `contents` (`id`, `user_id`, `content_type_id`, `category_id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `tags`, `banner_image`, `pdf_file`, `video_file`, `email_subject`, `email_template`, `case_study_headline`, `case_study_summary`, `custom_fields`, `webhook_url`, `builder_layout`, `builder_content_elements`, `builder_page_data`, `webhook_field_mapping`, `content`, `seo_meta_title`, `seo_meta_description`, `seo_meta_keywords`, `scheduled_publish_date`, `webinar_date`, `hosted_by`, `platform`, `webinar_type`, `join_link`, `published_date`, `status`, `view_count`, `views_count`, `reading_time`, `admin_comment`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_visible_on_site`, `redirect_url`) VALUES
(146, 2, 10, 1, 'The Quantum Paradox', 'the-quantum-paradox', 'The threat of quantum computing is already here. Nation-state actors are actively executing \"Harvest Now, Decrypt Later\" strategies, stealing encrypted supplier data to break later. This white paper from former Gartner analyst William McNeill and apexanalytix\'s Akhilesh Agarwal reveals why AI-enabled procurement transformation introduces a critical security risk if not built on a quantum-ready foundation.', '[\"Quantum Computing\",\"Post-Quantum Cryptography\",\"Procurement\",\"Supply Chain Risk\",\"Cyber Security\",\"Harvest Now Decrypt Later\",\"NIST Standards\",\"Digital Transformation\",\"apexanalytix\",\"P2P Solutions\",\"AI Security\"]', 'banner_image-1784060024294-682731673.webp', 'pdf_file-1784060024458-834452794.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2>Is your Procurement transformation future-proofed against the quantum threat?</h2><p>Your transformation initiatives might be introducing a critical security risk.</p><p>This white paper from former Gartner analyst William McNeill and apexanalytix’s President of P2P Solutions and Technology Akhilesh Agarwal highlights the critical importance of building your AI-enabled processes on a future-proof foundation.&nbsp;</p><p>The US Government has issued a stark warning: nation-states are hoarding encrypted data, ready to break the code when quantum computers catch up. Experts say that could be as soon as 2030. Will your sourcing, onboarding, risk and data management tools embrace the new security standard in time?</p><p><strong>Download the white paper today and find out!</strong></p>', 'The Quantum Paradox: Future-Proof Your Procurement Against Quantum Threats | apexanalytix', 'Nation-states are hoarding your encrypted supplier data for future decryption. Download this white paper from former Gartner analysts to learn how to future-proof your procurement transformation against the quantum threat before 2030.', 'Quantum computing threat, post-quantum cryptography procurement, supply chain security, Harvest Now Decrypt Later, quantum risk management, NIST PQC standards, procurement transformation security, apexanalytix white paper, supplier data protection, quantum-safe sourcing', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-20 17:33:21', 'published', 128046, 1, 1, NULL, '2023-03-20 17:33:21', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(147, 2, 10, 1, 'How ACTIVE®’s one-person ops team doubled revenue with the support of Amazon Supply Chain Services', 'how-activers-one-person-ops-team-doubled-revenue-with-the-support-of-amazon-supply-chain-services', 'Discover how ACTIVE®, a household cleaning brand with a one-person operations team, doubled its revenue by leveraging Amazon Supply Chain Services (ASCS). This case study details how they used Amazon Global Logistics (AGL) and Amazon Warehousing & Distribution (AWD) to streamline international shipping, simplify inventory management, and expand to new sales channels. Learn how a lean team can achieve remarkable growth and operational efficiency with Amazon\'s integrated logistics network ', '[\"Amazon Supply Chain Services\",\"ASCS\",\"ACTIVE® case study\",\"logistics\",\"supply chain\",\"e-commerce\",\"FBA\",\"Amazon Global Logistics\",\"AGL\",\"Amazon Warehousing & Distribution\",\"AWD\",\"revenue growth\",\"inventory management\",\"lean team\",\"CPG\",\"household cleaning\",\"cross-border logistics\",\"multi-channel fulfillment.\"]', 'banner_image-1784060263290-166048326.webp', 'pdf_file-1784060263369-790575291.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784060224014,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784060224166,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784060224334,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784060224470,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">How ACTIVE®\'s one-person ops team doubled revenue with the support of Amazon Supply Chain Services</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For growing brands managing complex logistics with lean teams, Amazon Supply Chain Services (ASCS) offers a powerful network of end-to-end solutions - without the added overhead. ACTIVE®’s one-person operations team leveraged ASCS to streamline international shipments, expand customer reach, and increase cash flow. The result? A business that doubled in scale, powered by Amazon’s logistics network.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this case study you’ll learn:</h3><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How a single-person ops team scaled international shipping without adding headcount</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Which Amazon Supply Chain Services ACTIVE® used to simplify cross-border logistics</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Strategies for expanding customer reach through Amazon’s fulfillment network</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How ASCS helped ACTIVE® improve cash flow alongside business growth</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why partnering with Amazon’s logistics infrastructure can be a growth multiplier for lean operations teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>', 'How ACTIVE®\'s One-Person Ops Team Doubled Revenue with Amazon Supply Chain', 'See how ACTIVE® achieved 100% YoY revenue growth with a lean team of one using Amazon Supply Chain Services. Learn about their success with AGL, AWD, and streamlined logistics.', 'Amazon Supply Chain Services, ASCS, ACTIVE case study, logistics growth, e-commerce fulfillment, Amazon Global Logistics, AGL, Amazon Warehousing & Distribution, AWD, lean operations, inventory planning, revenue growth, CPG logistics, cross-border shipping, multi-channel fulfillment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-22 12:16:52', 'published', 52933, 2, 1, NULL, '2023-03-22 12:16:52', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(148, 2, 10, 2, 'The Supply Chain AI Readiness Report: Why Operational Discipline Determines Agentic AI Success', 'the-supply-chain-ai-readiness-report-why-operational-discipline-determines-agentic-ai-success', 'While AI pilots are common, scaling them remains elusive for over 95% of supply chain organizations. This report, a joint study by GEP and UVA Darden, reveals that the key to success is not superior technology, but \"operational discipline\"-the foundational work of data governance, process redesign, and workflow integration. The research identifies a small \"Performance Elite\" who have achieved massive productivity gains by investing in AI readiness and governance before deployment, creating \"Intelligent Value Streams.\" It maps the six operational dimensions that separate these leaders from those stuck in \"pilot purgatory.\"', '[\"Supply Chain AI\",\"Agentic AI\",\"AI Readiness\",\"Operational Discipline\",\"Digital Transformation\",\"AI Governance\",\"Supply Chain Management\",\"AI Pilot Purgatory\",\"Intelligent Value Streams\"]', 'banner_image-1784060474241-834824587.webp', 'pdf_file-1784060474324-648555961.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784060349758,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784060350542,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784060350799,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784060351006,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Every quarter a supply chain AI program stays in pilot, the cost isn’t static. It compounds.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Not just the direct AI spend. The opportunity cost of delayed productivity gains. The rework when pilots scale on broken processes. The margin erosion that comes from operating without AI-ready governance.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The 5% who broke through invested in readiness first. Structured investment logic. Enterprise value as the success metric. Operational redesign before deployment.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">They didn’t spend more on AI. They spent first on making the operation ready for it.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The research maps exactly what that looks like across six operational dimensions.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this report, you’ll learn:</h3><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why most organizations are stuck in AI pilot mode-and what it takes to scale</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How operational discipline, not technology, drives real AI success</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why the biggest barriers to AI are business and workflow challenges-not technical ones</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How leading companies are redesigning work with “Intelligent Value Streams”</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What’s holding organizations back-and how to close the readiness gap for AI adoption</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>', 'The Supply Chain AI Readiness Report: Operational Discipline for Agentic AI', 'Why do 95% of AI pilots fail to scale? Discover how operational discipline and governance, not technology, drive agentic AI success in supply chains, based on the GEP & UVA Darden report.', 'supply chain AI readiness, agentic AI, operational discipline, AI governance, AI pilot purgatory, GEP UVA Darden report, intelligent value streams, supply chain AI scaling', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-24 14:59:23', 'published', 70526, 2, 1, NULL, '2023-03-24 14:59:23', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(149, 2, 10, 2, 'AI in Warehousing: Improving Performance Across the Intralogistics Lifecycle', 'ai-in-warehousing-improving-performance-across-the-intralogistics-lifecycle', 'Discover how artificial intelligence is transforming warehouses from static storage hubs into dynamic, intelligent nerve centers that drive performance and resilience', '[\"Intralogistics\",\"Warehouse Optimization\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Supply Chain\",\"AI in Warehousing\",\"Logistics\",\"Operational Efficiency\",\"Warehouse Lifecycle\",\"Performance Improvement\",\"Data-Driven Operations\",\"Throughput\"]', 'banner_image-1784060666685-37650165.webp', 'pdf_file-1784060666755-126037426.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>Warehouse operations are becoming more complex than ever. E-commerce growth, expanding SKU assortments and rising expectations for speed and accuracy are pushing traditional, rule-based warehouse processes to their limits. To stay competitive, organizations need more adaptive, data-driven operations.</p><p>Artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming how warehouses operate, enabling greater visibility, smarter decision-making and continuous optimization across the intralogistics lifecycle.</p><p>In this eBook, you’ll learn:</p><ul><li><p>Why AI is reshaping modern warehouse and supply chain operations</p></li><li><p>Where AI delivers the most value across the warehouse lifecycle</p></li><li><p>How AI improves visibility, accuracy and throughput</p></li><li><p>Real-world AI use cases across yard management, receiving, execution, inventory and outbound logistics</p></li><li><p>How to evaluate and prioritize AI investments for your organization</p></li></ul><p>Download this eBook&nbsp;to gain a practical, structured perspective on how AI can deliver measurable performance improvements across your warehouse operations and how to identify the right opportunities for implementation.</p>', 'Improve Performance Across the Intralogistics Lifecycle with AI', ' Learn how AI transforms warehouse operations, improving visibility, accuracy, and throughput. Discover real-world use cases and how to prioritize AI investments for measurable performance gains.', 'intralogistics lifecycle, AI warehouse optimization, supply chain performance, improve warehouse throughput, AI in logistics, warehouse automation, operational efficiency, data-driven warehousing', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-28 10:42:54', 'published', 188831, 0, 1, NULL, '2023-03-28 10:42:54', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(150, 2, 10, 16, 'UKG Pro Forecasting: Take the Guesswork Out of Workforce Planning with the Power of UKG AI', 'ukg-pro-forecasting-take-the-guesswork-out-of-workforce-planning-with-the-power-of-ukg-ai', 'UKG Pro Forecasting leverages patented, self-tuning machine learning to transform historical data into highly accurate workforce predictions. By automatically analyzing your unique business patterns, it eliminates guesswork and optimizes schedules to meet real-time demand. The system continuously self-calibrates, ensuring your staffing levels remain precise during seasonal peaks and unexpected fluctuations. This empowers managers to make smarter, data-driven adjustments instantly while delivering timely schedules to employees. Ultimately, it turns your organization’s historical data into a strategic asset for ideal, purpose-driven coverage.', '[\"UKG Pro Forecasting\",\"workforce planning\",\"AI scheduling\",\"machine learning forecasting\",\"employee scheduling software\",\"demand forecasting\",\"workforce management\",\"UKG Dimensions\",\"predictive staffing\",\"labor optimization\",\"seasonal scheduling\",\"HR technology\",\"auto-tuning algorithm\",\"staff planning.\"]', 'banner_image-1784061414684-676492753.webp', 'pdf_file-1784061414755-14004535.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784061369670,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784061369848,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784061370174,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784061370383,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>UKG Pro® Forecasting (formerly UKG Dimensions® Forecasting) optimizes your schedules by making accurate and timely predictions based on data trends and patterns from your own business. Over time, our patented, self-tuning machine-learning (ML) algorithm automatically analyzes and learns from this data fine-tuning itself to continue providing accurate forecasts to help your business create optimized schedules that meet the demands of your business.</p><p>Deliver timely schedules to every person by using an accurate forecast that provides:</p><ul><li><p>Effective periodic or seasonal coverage with self-tuning insights&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Leverage the full power of data to use patterns in the past to predict the future&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Analyze staffing measurements to make smarter adjustments in the moment&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Ideal schedules influenced by purposeful workforce management data across the organization’s history</p></li></ul><p>But this is only the tip of the iceberg,&nbsp;Fill out the form and download it now.&nbsp;</p>', 'UKG Pro Forecasting: AI-Powered Workforce Planning & Scheduling', 'Eliminate guesswork with UKG Pro Forecasting. Our patented self-tuning ML algorithm delivers accurate predictions & optimized schedules based on your business data. Download now.', 'UKG Pro Forecasting, workforce planning AI, predictive scheduling, machine learning workforce, UKG Dimensions forecasting, labor demand forecasting, employee schedule optimization, seasonal staffing, workforce data analytics, HR forecasting tool', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-03-30 16:25:25', 'published', 142578, 0, 1, NULL, '2023-03-30 16:25:25', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(151, 2, 10, 6, 'Transform Your Business With Expert Salesforce Consulting & Development Services', 'transform-your-business-with-expert-salesforce-consulting-and-development-services', 'Unlock the full power of Salesforce with expert consulting and development services designed for your unique business needs. Our comprehensive suite covers everything from strategic consultation to seamless implementation and minute customizations, ensuring your CRM works exactly the way you need it to. We bridge the gap between Salesforce\'s vast capabilities and your operational goals, driving smoother workflows and smarter customer interactions. With a dedicated team of certified experts, we guarantee a tailored, hassle-free deployment that accelerates your digital transformation. Elevate your customer experience and maximize your ROI with a Salesforce solution built for growth.', '[\"Salesforce consulting\",\"Salesforce development\",\"CRM implementation\",\"Salesforce customization\",\"Salesforce services\",\"cloud CRM\",\"Salesforce experts\",\"digital transformation\",\"customer experience management\",\"Salesforce integration\",\"CRM optimization\",\"business process automation\",\"Salesforce solutions.\"]', 'banner_image-1784062022965-247707316.webp', 'pdf_file-1784062023264-876664860.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784061986838,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784061987119,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784061987358,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784061987614,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Leverage Our Comprehensive Salesforce Service Suite</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Salesforce is the most powerful cloud-based CRM in the world. But, in order to maximize its true potential, you need a dedicated partner who understands its nuances and can tailor it to suit your specific business needs and objectives effectively.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Our complete gamut of Salesforce services can help you leverage its true potential. From consultation to minute customization, our team of Salesforce experts is dedicated to ensuring your implementation is smooth and tailored to your unique requirements, empowering your business to thrive in the digital age.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Ready to elevate customer experience?</strong></p>', ' Expert Salesforce Consulting & Development Services | Tailored CRM Solutions', ' Maximize your Salesforce ROI with expert consulting, seamless implementation, and custom development. Transform customer experiences with our comprehensive CRM services. Get started today!', ' Salesforce consulting services, Salesforce development, CRM implementation, Salesforce customization, cloud CRM solutions, Salesforce experts, digital transformation, customer experience, Salesforce integration, business CRM.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-04 11:08:56', 'published', 141398, 1, 1, NULL, '2023-04-04 11:08:56', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(152, 2, 10, 5, 'Critical Capabilities When Evaluating Human Risk Management Platforms', 'critical-capabilities-when-evaluating-human-risk-management-platforms', 'Human Risk Management (HRM) represents a paradigm shift from traditional security awareness training, evolving from passive learning into active, real-time threat mitigation. This whitepaper explores how HRM platforms leverage data-driven analytics to identify, quantify, and remediate human cyber risks before breaches occur. Unlike outdated annual training, modern HRM provides immediate, contextual coaching to employees at the exact moment of risky behavior, effectively stopping attacks in their tracks. Discover the critical capabilities that separate next-generation HRM solutions from legacy SAT programs and learn how to build a truly proactive human defense layer. Download now to transform your organization\'s approach to human-centric security.', '[\"Human Risk Management\",\"HRM platform\",\"security awareness training\",\"cyber risk mitigation\",\"real-time security coaching\",\"human cyber risk\",\"behavioral security\",\"phishing prevention\",\"security culture\",\"risk quantification\",\"employee security training\",\"proactive cybersecurity\",\"insider threat management\",\"security behavior analytics.\"]', 'banner_image-1784062269971-147847412.webp', 'pdf_file-1784062270125-858006015.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784062229127,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784062229295,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784062229462,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784062229631,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>Human Risk Management (HRM) is more than just the next step in security awareness training (SAT)-it’s a fundamental shift in how organizations approach human security risks.</p><p>A more innovative, proactive approach is required. One that provides real-time guidance to employees to mitigate an attack before it succeeds while also providing training at the moment of risky behavior. This is why real-time security coaching has emerged as a powerful two-pronged mitigation strategy for stopping these attacks.</p><p>Download this whitepaper to understand:</p><ul><li><p>The difference between security awareness training and human risk management</p></li><li><p>How HRM platforms take a data-driven approach to human cyber risk</p></li><li><p>The key capabilities to allow an HRM platform to identify, quantify and mitigate human risk effectively</p></li></ul><p><strong>Download this whitepaper today!</strong></p>', 'Critical Capabilities for Evaluating Human Risk Management Platforms', 'Discover the key capabilities of Human Risk Management platforms. Learn how HRM goes beyond SAT with real-time coaching & data-driven risk mitigation. Download the whitepaper.', 'Human Risk Management platform, HRM capabilities, security awareness training vs HRM, human cyber risk, real-time security coaching, cyber risk mitigation, behavioral analytics security, employee threat detection, proactive cybersecurity, risk quantification, security culture transformation, HRM whitepaper', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-06 15:51:27', 'published', 79255, 1, 1, NULL, '2023-04-06 15:51:27', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(153, 2, 10, 3, 'Build vs. Buy: The Reality of Production-Grade RAG', 'build-vs-buy-the-reality-of-production-grade-rag', 'While DIY retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) prototypes show promise initially, they consistently fail when scaled across complex data sources and growing enterprise use cases. This whitepaper reveals the hidden operational costs of building in-house-from broken ingestion pipelines to unreliable retrieval and escalating maintenance overhead. It explores why production-grade AI demands deterministic source attribution, governed access, hybrid search capabilities, and continuous evaluation to maintain trust. More importantly, it demonstrates how RAG-as-a-Service centralizes these critical functions, eliminating compounding technical debt while enabling faster, safer, and multi-use-case deployment. Discover the reality behind the build-versus-buy decision and unlock reliable enterprise AI at scale.\r\n\r\n', '[\"RAG\",\"retrieval-augmented generation\",\"enterprise AI\",\"RAG-as-a-Service\",\"build vs buy RAG\",\"production-grade AI\",\"hybrid retrieval\",\"generative AI governance\",\"AI evaluation\",\"document ingestion\",\"enterprise search\",\"AI scalability\",\"LLM deployment\",\"governed AI\",\"AI observability.\"]', 'banner_image-1784063234868-242460698.webp', 'pdf_file-1784063234934-790799759.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784063076038,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784063076232,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784063076415,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784063076583,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A concise guide explaining why DIY retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems can often break when scaled, and how a production‑grade, governed RAG‑as‑a‑Service solution simplifies ingestion, retrieval, evaluation and security to deliver reliable enterprise AI.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">This comprehensive whitepaper covers:</h3><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DIY RAG prototypes work early, but fail as complexity, data sources and use cases grow</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Enterprise AI requires more than just a good model, but also deterministic retrieval, source attribution and governed access</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Production‑grade RAG demands hybrid retrieval, built‑in evaluation and full observability to maintain trust at scale</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Maintenance of DIY pipelines creates compounding operational costs across ingestion, re‑embedding and ranking</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">RAG‑as‑a‑Service centralizes ingestion, retrieval and governance-enabling faster, safer, multi‑use‑case deployment</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>', 'Build vs. Buy RAG: Production-Grade Enterprise AI Reality', 'Discover why DIY RAG systems break at scale and how governed RAG-as-a-Service ensures reliable ingestion, retrieval, evaluation & security. Download the whitepaper now.', 'Build vs buy RAG, production-grade RAG, retrieval-augmented generation, enterprise AI deployment, RAG-as-a-Service, DIY RAG challenges, hybrid retrieval, AI governance, scalable AI, generative AI evaluation, document ingestion pipeline, AI observability, enterprise search solutions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-10 13:34:58', 'published', 162080, 2, 1, NULL, '2023-04-10 13:34:58', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(154, 2, 10, 5, 'The Unified Identity Prescription – Securing Modern Healthcare & Empowering Caregivers', 'the-unified-identity-prescription-securing-modern-healthcare-and-empowering-caregivers', 'Legacy IAM architectures are failing modern healthcare-fragmented identity data creates security gaps, delays clinician access, and compromises patient care. This whitepaper introduces the unified identity data foundation: an approach that aggregates and synchronizes identity data across all sources to establish a single, authoritative view of every user. It reveals how identity silos and manual provisioning drive operational risks, compliance failures, and security vulnerabilities while hindering multi-role clinicians from delivering timely care. Discover how unified identity transforms IAM from a technical bottleneck into a strategic enabler-accelerating M&A, strengthening Identity Security Posture Management (ISPM), and empowering caregivers with contextual, role-based access.', '[\"healthcare IAM\",\"unified identity\",\"healthcare cybersecurity\",\"identity data foundation\",\"caregiver access\",\"legacy IAM\",\"identity silos\",\"identity security posture management\",\"ISPM\",\"healthcare compliance\",\"role-based access control\",\"RBAC\",\"healthcare M&A\",\"clinician access management\",\"patient data security\",\"identity governance\",\"healthcare IT security.\"]', 'banner_image-1784063598975-223614669.webp', 'pdf_file-1784063599036-116056554.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h3>What This White Paper Examines:</h3><p>This white paper introduces the concept of a unified identity data foundation-an approach that aggregates, rationalizes, and synchronizes identity data across all sources to create a single, authoritative view of every user. It will help you understand:</p><ul><li><p>Why legacy IAM architectures are failing modern healthcare environments</p></li><li><p>How fragmented identity data impacts clinician access, patient care, and security</p></li><li><p>The operational and security risks created by identity silos and manual provisioning</p></li><li><p>The role of a unified identity data foundation in improving access, governance, and ISPM</p></li><li><p>How healthcare organizations can support multi-role clinicians with contextual, role-based access</p></li><li><p>The identity security and compliance implications of poor data hygiene</p></li><li><p>How unified identity accelerates secure healthcare M&amp;A and day-one collaboration</p></li></ul><p>Learn how unified identity data transforms IAM from a technical bottleneck into a strategic enabler for modern healthcare.</p><p><strong>Download the White Paper</strong></p>', 'Unified Identity Prescription: Securing Healthcare & Empowering Caregivers', 'Discover how a unified identity data foundation replaces legacy IAM, improves clinician access, strengthens security, and accelerates healthcare M&A. Download the whitepaper now.', 'unified identity healthcare, healthcare IAM, identity data foundation, caregiver access management, healthcare cybersecurity, legacy IAM challenges, identity silos, ISPM healthcare, role-based access healthcare, healthcare compliance, clinician identity, healthcare M&A security, identity governance healthcare, patient data protection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-12 17:17:29', 'published', 177639, 0, 1, NULL, '2023-04-12 17:17:29', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(156, 2, 10, 11, 'A Practical Guide to Performance Testing for Enterprise Systems', 'a-practical-guide-to-performance-testing-for-enterprise-systems', 'Most performance testing fails to catch real-world failures like queue backups, memory leaks, and concurrent user spikes. This whitepaper breaks down how load, stress, and endurance testing work together to reveal your system\'s true breaking points. Learn a practical, repeatable strategy tailored for ERP, WMS, and supply chain environments-so you stop guessing and start scaling with confidence.', '[\"Performance Testing\",\"Load Testing\",\"Stress Testing\",\"Endurance Testing\",\"Enterprise Systems\",\"ERP Performance\",\"WMS Testing\",\"Supply Chain Software\",\"Application Performance Management\",\"Software Quality Assurance\",\"Non-Functional Testing\",\"System Scalability\",\"Performance Engineering\",\"DevOps\",\"Site Reliability Engineering\",\"Peak Load Testing\",\"Memory Leak Detection\",\"Continuous Testing\",\"IT Infrastructure\",\"Risk Mitigation\"]', 'banner_image-1784122839033-640639272.webp', 'pdf_file-1784122839116-626151075.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784122783780,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\\t\"},{\"id\":1784122783949,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784122784106,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784122784253,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Most systems don’t fail all at once. They slow down, back up, and quietly break when demand hits from every direction at once. What passed testing last week suddenly struggles under peak volume, overlapping processes, or hours of sustained use.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This white paper challenges the idea that one type of performance test is enough. It shows how load, stress, and endurance testing work together to reveal what your system will actually do when it matters. Because confidence doesn’t come from passing a test. It comes from knowing how your system behaves under pressure.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">What You’ll Learn:</h3><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why performance issues slip through even when testing is in place</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What load testing really proves, and where it falls short</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How stress testing exposes breaking points before production does</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why endurance testing uncovers slow failures most teams miss</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How to combine all three approaches into a practical, repeatable strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What performance testing looks like across real ERP, WMS, and supply chain workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How to move from one-time testing to continuous performance confidence</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If your systems only pass tests under ideal conditions, you’re still guessing. Download the white paper to see how a layered performance testing strategy helps you find issues early, fix them faster, and move forward with confidence before pressure hits production.</p>', 'A Practical Guide to Performance Testing for Enterprise Systems | Load, Stress & Endurance Testing Whitepaper', 'Learn how load, stress, and endurance testing work together to uncover hidden system failures in ERP, WMS & supply chain. Download the practical guide to performance testing for enterprise systems.', 'performance testing guide, enterprise performance testing, load testing strategy, stress testing for ERP, endurance testing best practices, system scalability testing, WMS performance testing, supply chain software testing, non-functional testing guide, continuous performance testing, application performance management, IT risk mitigation', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-14 12:00:00', 'published', 6952, 3, 2, NULL, '2023-04-14 12:00:00', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(157, 2, 10, 5, 'Strengthening Identity Security: Governance, Visibility and Autonomous Remediation January 2026', 'strengthening-identity-security-governance-visibility-and-autonomous-remediation-january-2026', 'As identity-led cyberattacks escalate-fueled by AI-driven social engineering and compromised credentials-organizations face critical gaps in visibility, governance, and recovery. This whitepaper examines the urgent need to strengthen identity security posture through enhanced threat detection, rightsizing access controls, and autonomous remediation. It also highlights the overlooked risk of identity platform configuration data and the necessity of backup and resilience strategies for systems like Microsoft Entra ID.', '[\"Identity Security\",\"IAM\",\"ITDR\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"Threat Detection\",\"Credential Theft\",\"Autonomous Remediation\",\"Microsoft Entra ID\",\"Access Governance\",\"Zero Trust\",\"AI Threats\",\"Dark Web Monitoring\",\"Service Accounts\",\"Identity Misuse\",\"Cyber Resilience\"]', 'banner_image-1784123966723-789207793.webp', 'pdf_file-1784123966786-684914323.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784123818924,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784123819124,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784123819325,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784123819596,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>Threats against identities and their protections are worsening. Cybercriminals are more interested in stealing and abusing compromised credentials, organizations often can’t detect exposed credentials on the dark web, and visibility into the actions and behaviors of service accounts is lacking. Threat actors are increasingly leveraging social engineering for compromising credentials. Internally, most organizations lack the optics and processes to detect identity-led threats.</p><p>New identity security solutions are emerging to protect identities-both human and non-human-by layering additional protections on identity and access management tools. These include solutions for visibility, governance, and autonomous remediation. While the organizations in this research claim high maturity for current identity security deployments, evidence of high maturity is lacking for most. All organizations must urgently revisit their identity security protections, deploy new or advanced solutions to strengthen identity security posture, and reduce exposure to the negative implications of identity-led threats.</p><h2>KEY TAKEAWAYS</h2><p>The key takeaways from this research are:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Identity-led and identity-implicated threats are escalating</strong><br>72.1% of the organizations in this research say that the threat level of 15 identity-led and identity-implicated cyberattacks has increased or remained unchanged over the past 12 months. The use of AI by threat actors to create highly personalized attacks had the most significant increase.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>The importance of identity security technologies is rising rapidly</strong><br>Across 22 identity-related capabilities, average importance is anticipated to increase from 47% two years ago to 68.1% in two years. The ability to detect identity misuse persists as the most important capability, and capabilities that enable the rightsizing of access rights increase in importance the most.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Claims of high maturity in identity security deployments lack supporting evidence</strong><br>68.7% of organizations claim their current identity security deployments are mature, yet flow-on outcomes undermine this assertion. Organizations claiming high maturity would be well advised to check alignment with actual outcomes-and take the necessary steps to address systemic weaknesses.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Improving visibility into identity threats is fundamental</strong><br>Over three quarters of organizations have less than full and complete visibility into 14 different identity threats and security fundamentals. Lack of visibility into identity vulnerabilities is a critical shortcoming to address because identity-led attacks start with just one compromised identity-related asset, such as a credential for sale on a dark web forum. Enhanced visibility combined with automated detection and remediation of compromised credentials is essential for closing this gap.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Identity configurations in identity platforms need resilience and recovery options</strong><br>Identity configuration data-especially in platforms like Microsoft Entra ID-is a blind spot in many security strategies. Organizations must back up identity platforms as they would any other critical system to ensure resilience and recovery.</p></li></ul><p></p>', 'Strengthening Identity Security: Governance, Visibility & Autonomous Remediation 2026', '72% of organizations face rising identity-led threats. Learn how to close visibility gaps, rightsize access, and back up identity platforms like Entra ID to stay secure in 2026.', 'identity security, identity threat detection, ITDR, IAM governance, credential theft prevention, autonomous remediation, Microsoft Entra ID backup, access rights management, AI cyber threats, dark web credential monitoring, service account visibility, identity security posture, zero trust identity, 2026 cybersecurity trends', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-18 14:43:31', 'published', 81846, 3, 3, NULL, '2023-04-18 14:43:31', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL);
INSERT INTO `contents` (`id`, `user_id`, `content_type_id`, `category_id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `tags`, `banner_image`, `pdf_file`, `video_file`, `email_subject`, `email_template`, `case_study_headline`, `case_study_summary`, `custom_fields`, `webhook_url`, `builder_layout`, `builder_content_elements`, `builder_page_data`, `webhook_field_mapping`, `content`, `seo_meta_title`, `seo_meta_description`, `seo_meta_keywords`, `scheduled_publish_date`, `webinar_date`, `hosted_by`, `platform`, `webinar_type`, `join_link`, `published_date`, `status`, `view_count`, `views_count`, `reading_time`, `admin_comment`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_visible_on_site`, `redirect_url`) VALUES
(159, 2, 3, 19, 'How Blockchain Is Revolutionizing B2B Transactions in 2025', 'how-blockchain-is-revolutionizing-b2b-transactions-in-2025-159', 'Blockchain is transforming B2B transactions by enabling faster cross-border payments, automated smart contracts, and tamper-proof record-keeping-all without middlemen or delays. From streamlining procurement to enhancing supply chain transparency, this blog explores how FinTech and blockchain together are reshaping business-to-business commerce in 2025. Discover how companies are leveraging this technology to build trust, reduce costs, and accelerate global trade.', '[\"Blockchain\",\"FinTech\",\"B2B Payments\",\"Smart Contracts\",\"Cross-Border Transactions\",\"Digital Transformation\",\"Supply Chain Finance\",\"Enterprise Blockchain\",\"Cryptocurrency\",\"Payment Automation\",\"B2B FinTech\",\"Distributed Ledger Technology\",\"Trade Finance\",\"Digital Identity Verification\",\"2025 Tech Trends\"]', 'banner_image-1784127184006-512178044.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>What if every deal your business made was instantly verified, recorded, and trustless – no emails, no middlemen, no delays? </strong>That’s not a futuristic vision. It’s already happening. In 2025, blockchain has moved far beyond cryptocurrency headlines to become a foundational tool for B2B transactions across industries. From automating contracts to streamlining cross-border payments, companies are using blockchain to build faster, more secure, and more transparent business relationships.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">B2B cross-border transactions using blockchain are expected to hit 745 million globally in 2025, with Europe handling 466 million and Asia contributing over one-third. Whether you’re a manufacturer in the U.S. or a distributor in India, blockchain is changing how business is done, with speed and trust built into every step. Let’s see how blockchain is revolutionizing B2B transactions in practical ways and why it’s relevant now.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">B2B Business Is Changing and Blockchain Is a Good Fit</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How businesses collaborate has evolved significantly over the past few years. With more partners, more digital systems, and more cross-border transactions, pressure to do so faster and more intelligently has increased. But most companies are still bound by old ways of working: lengthy email chains, error-plagued spreadsheets, and disconnected systems.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Blockchain is well-suited to this new world. It allows a collaborative digital ledger that tracks every stage of a transaction from contract, through payment, to delivery, in a manner that all parties can see. Once something has been added, it cannot be altered without consensus. That provides a shared version of the truth that everyone can rely on.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This works particularly well for companies with several layers of suppliers, such as manufacturing, pharma, or electronics, where incorrect communication could lead to severe delays. With blockchain, there is no need to speculate on who did what and when; it’s all documented.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">How Blockchain Smart Contracts Automate Business Deals?</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Smart contracts automate business transactions. Rather than having to wait for someone to verify a delivery or send an email before processing a payment, smart contracts do it all on their own. They are digital “if this, then that” instructions that reside on the blockchain.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Suppose a shipping firm promises to deliver an item to a customer on a specific date. A smart contract can be programmed to pay the moment the GPS tracks verify that the package has arrived. No paperwork reminders or delays.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This type of automation assists teams with minimizing repetitive work and diminishing back-and-forth between units. It also decreases opportunities for human miscalculation or conflicts, thus making business processes smoother and faster as a whole.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Supply Chains Are Becoming More Transparent and Faster</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">One of the largest problems with global supply chains is that businesses only get to see one part of the picture. A supplier might know when the product departs their warehouse, but not its arrival. A buyer may not be aware if components originated from an authorized source. Blockchain remedies this by providing a single, unified view for all parties.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Every product’s journey from raw material to end user is tracked step by step. Everyone in the chain has access to the same real-time updates, and changes are registered instantaneously. This is particularly useful in those industries where traceability is paramount, such as food, drugs, and electronics.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For instance, when a batch of food is discovered to be unsafe, blockchain can identify specifically where the problem originated, eliminating unnecessary time and wastage. Blockchain in 2025 also enables businesses to demonstrate to customers that their products have proof of ethical sourcing, fair labor practices, or sustainability, fostering greater trust in the brand.&nbsp;</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Payments Across Borders Are Faster and Less Painful</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When companies make international payments, things can become complicated. There are various banks, currencies, time zones, and regulations to navigate. Transactions may take days, and fees can add up quickly.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Blockchain alters that. Rather than routing through multiple banks and clearinghouses, companies can utilize blockchain platforms to transfer payments directly, securely, and in many cases, within minutes. This is particularly beneficial for firms that make recurring payments to overseas suppliers or partners.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These transactions are also accompanied by built-in records, which means they can be audited and verified with ease. And since the system is decentralized, it won’t be held back by a single point of failure. That means companies have more control and predictability over how they handle cash flow.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Identity Checks Are Becoming More Reliable</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the B2B universe, how you know who you’re working with really matters. But it takes slow, repetitive, and risky identity checks to find out. It’s not safe or effective to send passport scans or tax forms via email. With blockchain, businesses can verify and share identity details more securely. Digital IDs stored on a blockchain can confirm someone’s credentials without exposing all their data. It’s kind of like showing your driver’s license to prove your age, without revealing your home address.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This makes it faster to onboard new vendors or partners and decreases the risk of fraud. In high-trust industries, such as banking, healthcare, or government contracting, this technology makes it possible to maintain fast and secure sensitive transactions.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Vendor and Procurement Workflows Are Being Streamlined</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Purchasing goods or services from other companies was once a paperwork-intensive activity. Departments were required to deal with quotes, contracts, invoices, and delivery notes, many of which were in several systems. It was simple for errors to fall through the cracks.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Blockchain systems now assist businesses in managing procurement more efficiently. Each action from request to receipt is recorded and transparent to all authorized users. Businesses can see which suppliers are performing against contract terms and which suppliers are lagging behind. They can also eliminate redundant orders or overlooked payments.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Procurement staff save time spent on follow-ups and have more time to make strategic choices. It also becomes simpler to make suppliers accountable and negotiate improved terms in the long term.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Various Systems May Now Interoperate</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">One of the reasons that businesses waited to utilize blockchain technology in the past was that various platforms were unable to communicate with one another. If your supplier worked with a different blockchain, it was difficult to send data or synchronize transactions.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">That’s not true anymore. In 2025, new software will allow blockchains to interface with the business applications businesses are already using, such as CRMs or ERPs. APIs (application programming interfaces) enable bringing blockchain data into the tools that teams work with daily.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This allows a business to utilize its preferred blockchain and still integrate with partners who utilize other platforms. No longer must you choose between function and compatibility; you can have both.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">How Various Industries Utilize Blockchain Today?</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Blockchain is not limited to a particular industry. It’s being applied across numerous industries where B2B relationships are central to the business:</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Manufacturing</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Factories use blockchain to trace parts from suppliers, log inspections, and track inventory movements in real time. This helps meet safety standards and plan production more efficiently. It also reduces delays caused by miscommunication and allows quicker responses to quality issues. Manufacturers can share verified data with partners without risking sensitive information.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Healthcare</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pharma companies track medicines from labs to clinics to prevent counterfeits. Hospitals verify supplier credentials and manage vendor contracts with less risk. Blockchain also helps maintain patient data privacy while allowing secure information exchange between authorized parties. This leads to safer drug distribution and faster regulatory compliance.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Retail</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Retailers use blockchain to prove product authenticity, manage deliveries from global suppliers, and automate supplier payments based on delivery confirmations. It also enhances customer trust by providing transparent supply chain histories. Retailers can quickly identify and resolve issues with shipments, reducing stockouts and improving satisfaction.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Logistics</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Shipping companies use it for smoother customs checks, shipment tracking, and verifying delivery routes-all without manual updates or paperwork. Blockchain reduces paperwork errors and speeds up clearance processes at borders. It enables real-time collaboration between carriers, customs agents, and clients, cutting down delays and costs.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Energy</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Utility providers are using blockchain to manage power trades, track usage across regions, and settle bills faster with smart contracts. It supports peer-to-peer energy trading, allowing businesses to buy and sell excess power directly. Blockchain also improves transparency in renewable energy credits, helping companies meet sustainability goals.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Speed Bumps Still Exist in 2025</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Despite blockchain’s giant leaps, some speed bumps still exist. Public blockchains sometimes slow down when everybody tries to get on at the same time. Not all industries have come to standardize on common practices, which can complicate setup.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Privacy is also an issue. Companies want to provide enough information to establish trust, but not so much that their competitors get to view delicate details. Deploying blockchain on existing systems can be slow and costly, as well.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">And then there is the regulatory aspect. Digital contracts and foreign payments must comply with legislation that is lagging behind the technology. Companies need to be attentive to keep compliance from becoming a problem.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">What Business Leaders Need to Pay Attention To?</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If you’re a business leader venturing into blockchain, begin by choosing one segment where it might be useful. Perhaps it’s paying suppliers. Perhaps it’s tracking contracts. Pilot it with a small segment and scale up once you witness the outcomes.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Joining industry associations can keep you ahead of standards and prevent you from building alone. It’s also an investment worth making in training your staff on how to use this technology in ways that benefit your company.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Lastly, be practical. Concentrate on concrete business results. Don’t pursue buzzwords. Utilize blockchain wherever it offers definite value and bypass it wherever it doesn’t.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Way Forward: A More Open, Trusted B2B Economy</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Blockchain is not a fad. It’s becoming an integral part of the way businesses do business and cooperate. With it, businesses can create faster, more transparent, and more trustworthy partnerships.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In a world where trust and speed are more important than ever, blockchain enables companies to eliminate uncertainty and establish trust on every transaction. And although the technology will continue to change, the message is clear: Companies that adopt it now will be more responsive, more secure, and better positioned for the future.</p>', 'How Blockchain Is Revolutionizing B2B Transactions in 2025', 'Discover how blockchain and FinTech are transforming B2B transactions in 2025-from faster cross-border payments to automated smart contracts and transparent supply chains. Learn practical applications across industries.', 'blockchain B2B transactions,FinTech blockchain,smart contracts B2B,cross-border payments blockchain,supply chain blockchain,enterprise blockchain 2025,B2B FinTech solutions,digital identity blockchain,trade finance blockchain,blockchain payment automation,decentralized B2B transactions,blockchain procurement,vendor management blockchain,blockchain in manufacturing,blockchain in logistics', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-20 10:26:02', 'published', 329732, 0, 9, NULL, '2023-04-20 10:26:02', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(162, 2, 3, 17, 'How AI Is Reshaping B2B Lead Generation in the IT Sector', 'how-ai-is-reshaping-b2b-lead-generation-in-the-it-sector', 'AI is transforming B2B lead generation in the IT sector-moving beyond automation to intelligence-driven engagement. This blog explores how predictive analytics, hyper-personalization, real-time qualification, and ABM precision are reshaping the lead funnel. Discover how IT marketers can leverage AI to convert intent into insight, shorten sales cycles, and drive predictable revenue growth.', '[\"AI in B2B Lead Generation\",\"MarTech\",\"Marketing Technology\",\"Predictive Analytics\",\"ABM\",\"Account-Based Marketing\",\"Lead Scoring\",\"Marketing Automation\",\"Generative AI\",\"Sales Intelligence\",\"IT Marketing\",\"Conversational AI\",\"Hyper-Personalization\",\"Demand Generation\",\"Martech Stack\",\"AI Marketing Tools\",\"Sales Enablement\",\"Intent Data\",\"CRM Integration\",\"SDR Productivity\"]', 'banner_image-1784129752900-653518359.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"banner\",\"title\",\"pdf\",\"content\",\"landing\",\"webhook\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p><strong><em>“AI is not just another tool-it’s the toolbox.” -</em></strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sundarpichai/\"><strong><em> </em></strong></a><strong><em>Sundar Pichai, CEO, Google.</em></strong></p><p>This quote captures the revolution occurring in B2B lead generation in the entire IT industry. The conventional demand generation tactics – cold emails, manual scoring, and static segmentation no longer work. Decision-makers now anticipate personalized contact, rapid response, and intelligent dialogue from the initial point of contact. That’s where AI in B2B Lead Generation comes into play.</p><p>The tech-savvy IT sector is quickly embracing AI to convert intent data into insight and engagement into conversion. This change, though, goes beyond automation; it’s about embedding intelligence within each layer of the funnel. Let’s break down the way AI is transforming lead generation in tech-powered B2B markets.</p><h2>Pinpointing Buyer Intent with Predictive Intelligence</h2><p>In conventional B2B models, form-fills or website clicks are generally what marketers use to gauge interest. But AI technology now goes a few steps further by examining behavioral signals across multiple channels like search queries, content consumption, and even social engagement.</p><p>With the help of machine learning models, AI platforms have the ability to grade leads not only on activity, but on potential to convert. These predictive scores enable IT marketers to concentrate on leads with the greatest revenue potential.</p><p>For instance, an <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Account-based_marketing\">ABM </a>(Account-Based Marketing) platform enabled by AI can recognize changes in a company’s IT team recently researching multi-cloud security and initiate extremely contextualized outreach before the lead completes a single form. This active intelligence removes uncertainty and drastically shortens sales cycles.</p><h2>Automating Hyper-Personalized Engagement at Scale</h2><p>Generic messaging and email blasts don’t cut it with technical buyers. They’re information-overloaded and apt to disengage. AI disrupts this paradigm by facilitating hyper-personalization at scale.</p><p>Natural Language Processing (NLP) and AI-powered content engines can customize email copy, landing pages, and ad messaging using the buyer’s industry vertical, technographic characteristics, past content engagement, and buying cycle stage.</p><p><strong><em>63% of marketers are already using generative AI in their content strategies, and another 27% plan to adopt it within the next six months.</em></strong></p><p>By pushing CRM information into AI platforms, IT marketers can automatically produce content that speaks to unique pain points. An example is a cloud optimization software company pitching cloud optimization solutions to DevOps leaders, as opposed to CIOs. This sort of context-driven personalization is not feasible without AI. And it can drive conversions directly.</p><h2>Facilitating Real-Time Lead Qualification and Routing</h2><p>One of the biggest underestimated advantages of AI in B2B Lead Generation is the way it eliminates the lag between action and follow-up. With legacy models, a lead could download a whitepaper and wait hours or days in a queue before being qualified and reached out to.</p><p>AI robots and smart workflows now qualify leads in real-time against pre-defined criteria and conversation analysis. Solutions such as Drift and Qualified can interact with visitors based on behavior, ask qualifying questions via chat, and direct sales-ready leads in real-time to SDRs or AEs.</p><p>In the technology industry, where purchasing committees are convoluted and sales cycles are lengthy, the pace is a discriminator. AI closes the interval between interest and engagement, enhancing the buying experience and sales results.</p><h2>Making Data Overload Strategic Insight</h2><p>The typical B2B tech firm manages staggering volumes of data, CRM history, and webinar registrations, to case study downloads and demo requests. The problem is not gathering data but joining the dots.</p><p>AI analytics software combines disconnected data and discovers trends people tend to overlook. To illustrate, AI is able to help discover which content streams drive pipeline establishment, which job functions interact most prior to deal progressions, and which channel delivers the highest ROI for enterprise accounts.</p><p>By seeing these insights, AI enables revenue teams and marketers to optimize and double down on campaigns and channels continuously. It is simpler to double down on what is working and shift quickly when something is not. This loop of data-to-insight is key to remaining competitive in the IT market.</p><h2>Streamlining ABM Strategies with AI Precision</h2><p>Account-based marketing is now a B2B IT sales necessity. But in the absence of AI, it can become manpower-intensive overnight. AI introduces much-needed precision and efficacy into ABM deployment.</p><p>AI extends ABM capabilities by distinguishing high-fit accounts by ICP and intent signals, segmenting audiences dynamically on firmographic and technographic changes, personalizing outreach by account stage or departmental function, and scoring engagement across account stakeholders for complete funnel insight.</p><p>For instance, if a data infrastructure provider wishes to reach fintech companies that are considering hybrid cloud options, AI can tell them which firms qualify, what they are reading, and who the major influencers are. This allows for stronger alignment between sales and marketing and increased deal velocity.</p><h2>Enhancing Campaign ROI through Intelligent A/B Testing</h2><p>Marketers have traditionally depended on A/B testing to refine copy, CTAs, and creatives. Conventional A/B testing, however, is usually slow and limiting. AI makes multivariate testing at scale automatic. It can test hundreds of variations across several segments, identify patterns, and redirect budgets to high-performing assets in real time.</p><p>This comes in handy, especially in IT-centric campaigns, where various personas, like CISOs and Solutions Architects, react to varied languages, images, and formats. AI does not only tell you what worked. It tells you why it worked and what’s next.</p><h2>Increasing SDR Productivity with Smart Assistants</h2><p>Sales Development Representatives (SDRs) waste an enormous amount of time researching leads, crafting emails, and maintaining CRMs. AI solutions are now automating these mundane tasks, leaving SDRs to concentrate on the conversations that seal the deal.</p><p>AI assistants can auto-email sequences from buyer intent, propose follow-up timing from behavior signals, summarize call notes through voice-to-text and sentiment analysis, and auto-populate CRM entries with minimal human intervention.</p><p>In IT sales, with products being complex and technical, stakeholders needing customized conversations, this productivity gain is revolutionary. AI doesn’t replace SDRs-it enhances their performance.</p><h2>Incorporating AI in the Existing Martech Stack</h2><p>One concern is whether AI will make existing marketing systems more complicated. But today’s AI tools are designed to integrate into CRMs, MAPs (such as HubSpot or Marketo), and intent platforms seamlessly. B2B Lead Generation’s AI is most effective when it enhances, rather than replaces, your current stack.</p><p>For instance, synchronizing AI-powered lead scores directly into Salesforce, data feeding predictive insights into marketing automation flows, and dynamic content creation within email tools become effortless. Integration is not technical, it’s strategic. IT companies that align AI capabilities across marketing and sales stacks realize quicker time to value.</p><h2>Preparing for the Future of AI-Driven Lead Gen</h2><p>The use of AI in B2B Lead Generation is not a short-term trend, it’s a long-term transformation. As models become more accurate and generative AI becomes more contextual, we’ll see conversational AI handling deeper technical questions, self-optimizing campaigns with minimal human input, AI forecasting pipeline health and conversion risks, and emotion-aware personalization that adapts in real time.</p><p>IT firms that adopt this change now will future-proof their growth plans. But it has to be done with a plan. AI requires good data, well-defined objectives, and human intervention to provide ROI. The objective isn’t automation, but augmentation.</p><h2>Redefining Lead Generation as Intelligence-Driven Growth</h2><p>The technology industry is shifting away from lead quantity and towards lead intelligence. AI not only provides leads it also makes you understand, interact, and convert them like never before.</p><p>With AI, personalization is accurate, timing is impeccable, targeting is intelligent, and sales alignment is tighter. The effect is evident: acceleration in pipelines, improved conversions, and more predictable revenues. Businesses that incorporate AI into B2B Lead Generation today won’t only create more leads, but they’ll create the right ones.</p>', 'How AI Is Reshaping B2B Lead Generation in the IT Sector (2026 Guide)', 'Discover how AI-powered MarTech is transforming B2B lead generation in IT-from predictive intent scoring to hyper-personalization and real-time qualification. Boost conversions & shorten sales cycles.', 'AI in B2B lead generation,MarTech,marketing technology,AI marketing,predictive lead scoring,account-based marketing,ABM automation,IT lead generation,AI sales intelligence,conversational AI,hyper-personalization,demand generation,marketing automation,B2B IT marketing,intent data,AI-powered CRM,lead qualification,SDR productivity,generative AI marketing,2026 marketing trends', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-24 16:09:33', 'published', 186694, 0, 7, NULL, '2023-04-24 16:09:33', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(163, 2, 3, 17, 'How AI and Machine learning drive smarter Demand Generation for IT', 'how-ai-and-machine-learning-drive-smarter-demand-generation-for-it', 'AI and machine learning are redefining demand generation for IT-shifting from manual targeting to machine-guided orchestration. This blog explores how predictive analytics, hyper-personalization, and AI-first metrics are transforming B2B tech marketing. Learn to build a demand engine that doesn\'t just react to the market, but learns from it.\r\n\r\n', '[\"AI in Demand Generation\",\"MarTech\",\"Marketing Technology\",\"Machine Learning Marketing\",\"B2B IT Marketing\",\"Predictive Analytics\",\"Demand Intelligence\",\"AI Marketing Tools\",\"Marketing Automation\",\"Pipeline Marketing\",\"Intent Data\",\"Predictive Lead Scoring\",\"B2B Tech Marketing\",\"AI-Powered Marketing\",\"Marketing Stack\",\"Demand Generation Strategy\",\"ML in Marketing\",\"Buyer Intelligence\",\"Sales & Marketing Alignment\",\"2025 Marketing Trends\"]', 'banner_image-1784131684440-810745151.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"banner\",\"title\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>In 2025, demand generation has become less of a marketing function and more of a predictive science. For B2B <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://intenttechpub.com/blog/3d-printing-in-niche-manufacturing-trends-to-watch-in-tech-integration/\">tech </a>firms, especially those in high-stakes sectors like <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://intenttechpub.com/tech/hybrid-computing-trends-that-are-changing-the-us-b2b-landscape/\">cloud computing</a>, cybersecurity, and enterprise software, the traditional model of lead capture is no longer sustainable. What’s changed isn’t just the tools; it’s the entire architecture of decision-making.</p><p>At the heart of this transformation is a shift from manual targeting to machine-guided orchestration, where demand is not just generated but engineered. This is Demand Generation for IT, reimagined through the lens of <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://intenttechpub.com/tech/why-ambient-intelligence-will-lead-industrial-automation-by-2026/\">artificial intelligence</a> (AI) and machine learning (ML), not as buzzwords, but as fundamental drivers of strategic precision.</p><h2><strong>Rethinking Demand Generation: Why IT Needs a New Framework</strong></h2><p>The average IT buying process in 2025 involves more touchpoints, more decision-makers, and less tolerance for generic content than ever before. Cold emails and static landing pages have been replaced by real-time personalization engines and AI-informed journey mapping.</p><p>Traditional demand generation treated buyers as a segment. Today, AI treats them as signals dynamic, evolving, and often unpredictable. B2B tech firms are no longer relying on gated PDFs and drip campaigns. Instead, they’re using algorithms that anticipate when a CTO is likely to enter a research phase or when a <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/devops/what-is-devops/\">DevOps </a>lead is ready to evaluate deployment options.</p><p>This evolution has forced IT marketers to abandon intuition in favor of iteration, constantly training their systems to learn from failure and scale what works. In short, the old playbook is not just outdated; it’s incompatible with the complexity of modern enterprise buying behavior.</p><h2><strong>The New Mindset: Demand Generation as a Machine-Guided System</strong></h2><p>Artificial intelligence has flipped the script. It’s no longer about generating demand by broadcasting messages, but about detecting demand through patterns and behavioral triggers.</p><p>Consider this: a machine learning model can now analyze thousands of digital breadcrumbs - webinar registrations, API calls, intent signals, content dwell time, and determine not only who is in-market, but who will be in-market soon. This predictive layer is fundamentally changing the economics of Demand Generation for IT.</p><p>What used to be the job of an SDR team, qualifying leads, segmenting prospects, and identifying buying stages, is now augmented by unsupervised ML models that self-optimize based on outcome data. These systems learn faster than human teams and pivot in real-time, making campaign adjustments on the fly.</p><p>But the innovation doesn’t stop at prediction. AI is helping IT marketers choreograph personalized experiences across channels. Instead of creating one-size-fits-all journeys, companies are deploying modular content flows that adapt automatically based on how prospects behave. This shift is enabling better buyer alignment, shorter sales cycles, and stronger pipeline efficiency.</p><h2><strong>Personalization Without Paralysis: AI as the Strategic Filter</strong></h2><p>One of the biggest challenges for demand gen teams in tech is personalization at scale. Without AI, the complexity becomes overwhelming. The average buyer journey in B2B IT might include ten stakeholders, four platforms, and a dozen pieces of content. Coordinating that without machine support is chaos.</p><p>AI doesn’t just enable personalization, it filters out noise. It prioritizes which variables matter: timing, messaging format, pain points, and solution awareness. It understands the difference between a decision-maker reading a white paper and a practitioner searching for documentation. And then it adjusts outreach accordingly.</p><p>For example, a cloud security vendor using AI in their demand gen program might notice that infrastructure architects in financial firms tend to convert after interacting with compliance-related content. The AI system tags these behaviors, adjusts the content stream for similar accounts, and prompts human reps to follow up with a targeted risk assessment, all within hours.</p><p>This is how AI transforms personalization from guesswork to systemized value delivery.</p><h2><strong>Redefining Demand Gen Metrics in the Age of AI</strong></h2><p>In 2025, traditional metrics like click-through rates and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.gartner.com/en/sales/glossary/marketing-qualified-lead-mql-\">MQL </a>volume no longer capture the complexity of B2B buyer behavior, especially in IT. AI-first demand generation focuses on predictive, actionable metrics that reflect real intent and funnel momentum.&nbsp;</p><p>One key metric is predictive lead score accuracy, which uses ML models to assess how likely a lead is to convert based on behavioral and firmographic data. Another is buyer stage velocity, tracking how quickly prospects move between funnel stages, helping teams identify friction points.</p><p>Finally, personalization responsiveness rate measures how prospects engage with dynamic, AI-tailored content in real time. These metrics don’t just show what happened, they guide what should happen next. For IT marketers, adopting AI-first KPIs turns data into foresight, enabling smarter decisions and faster conversions in an increasingly competitive market.</p><h2><strong>Beyond the Hype: What AI Can’t Replace</strong></h2><p>Despite the optimism, AI isn’t a silver bullet. It’s a multiplier, not a magician. Human creativity still defines strategy, tone, narrative, and trust. Machine learning can’t empathize with a CIO navigating digital transformation, but it can help you reach them at the right moment, with the right message, in the right channel.</p><p>AI also requires infrastructure, clean data, consistent feedback loops, and organizational alignment. Without these foundations, the promise of smart demand generation collapses under the weight of complexity. In other words, machines don’t replace marketers; they raise the standard for what marketers must manage and master.</p><h2><strong>Building the Next-Gen Demand Engine</strong></h2><p>To succeed in 2025 and beyond, tech companies must approach demand generation not as a campaign, but as a system. One that blends AI-powered intelligence with human insight. One that treats data not as an output, but as a competitive input.</p><p>Start with questions: What signals are we ignoring? What parts of the journey are we assuming instead of measuring? Where is friction happening, and how can automation reduce it without compromising trust?</p><p>Then build your stack around those answers, not around what’s trending, but around what drives decisions. AI and machine learning are tools, yes. But more than that, they are partners in building a demand engine that doesn’t just react to the market, it learns from it.</p><h2><strong>A Smarter Path Forward</strong></h2><p>As AI and ML reshape the contours of B2B marketing, Demand Generation for IT is being reborn not through new channels, but through new capabilities. What defines success now isn’t who shouts loudest, but who listens best. Who captures not just leads, but also learnings. And who evolves fast enough to stay relevant in a marketplace that never stops moving?</p><p>For IT companies willing to rethink, retool, and reinvest, 2025 won’t just be the year of smarter demand generation. It’ll be the year of demand intelligence, and the competitive edge will belong to those who see AI not as an add-on, but as the core operating system of modern growth.</p>', 'How AI & Machine Learning Drive Smarter Demand Generation for IT (2025 Guide)', 'Discover how AI and ML are transforming demand generation for IT-from predictive lead scoring to hyper-personalization. Learn to build an intelligence-driven demand engine for B2B tech success.', 'AI in demand generation, machine learning marketing, MarTech, B2B IT marketing, predictive analytics, demand intelligence, AI marketing tools, lead scoring, marketing automation, pipeline marketing, intent data, B2B tech marketing, AI-powered demand gen, ML models marketing, buyer intelligence, 2025 marketing trends, IT demand generation, predictive lead scoring accuracy, buyer stage velocity, personalization responsiveness rate', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-26 11:52:04', 'published', 274275, 0, 6, NULL, '2023-04-26 11:52:04', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(164, 2, 7, 2, 'Making AI work for you: from explainable to agentic', 'making-ai-work-for-you-from-explainable-to-agentic', 'Global supply chains are under pressure from geopolitics, sustainability demands, and talent shortages. This ebook shows how AI-specifically the UnisonIQ framework-helps you move from reactive planning to decision-centric, agentic operations. Packed with real-world cases and Zero100 insights, it’s your practical guide to turning disruption into a competitive advantage.', '[\"Supply Chain Planning\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Agentic AI\",\"Decision-Centric Planning\",\"UnisonIQ\",\"Supply Chain Resilience\",\"Geopolitical Risk\",\"Zero100\",\"Operations Strategy\",\"Digital Transformation\"]', 'banner_image-1784135740541-364601440.webp', 'pdf_file-1784135652714-906546487.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784135602416,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784135602625,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784135602824,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784135603009,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Global supply chains are being reshaped by forces that are both unpredictable and deeply structural. Geopolitical realignment, trade policy shifts, sustainability demands, and talent shortages are rewriting the rules of global trade. For supply chain leaders, the real risk isn’t disruption itself, it’s not staying ahead of what’s coming.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The mandate is clear: act fast, adapt continuously, and make smarter decisions to rise above your competitors. This e-book shows you how to do just that by strengthening your supply chain planning with a powerful AI framework like UnisonIQ.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key areas explored in the e-book:</h3><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why AI matters now for supply chain planning, and how it can deliver measurable value, starting today</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How to move from process-centric to decision-centric planning</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How to employ your teams for the agentic age</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How leading companies are implementing AI for measurable outcomes</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Grounded in real-world cases and the latest insights from analysts like Zero100, this practical guide gives you the clarity and structure you need to keep pace in today’s fast-changing supply chain landscape.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ready to strengthen your supply chain planning with AI and turn disruption into opportunity?</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Download the free e-book now!</p>', 'Making AI Work for You: From Explainable to Agentic – Free Supply Chain Ebook', 'Learn how AI-powered supply chain planning turns disruption into opportunity. Download this free ebook with real-world cases, Zero100 insights, and a practical framework for decision-centric, agentic operations.', 'AI supply chain, supply chain planning, agentic AI, decision-centric planning, UnisonIQ, supply chain resilience, Zero100, AI in logistics, supply chain digital transformation, predictive supply chain, free supply chain ebook, AI framework for operations', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-04-28 15:35:35', 'published', 68829, 0, 1, NULL, '2023-04-28 15:35:35', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(165, 2, 7, 3, 'Websites Supercharged: Content Storage Transformed into an Answer Engine', 'websites-supercharged-content-storage-transformed-into-an-answer-engine', 'Generative search-powered by agentic retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)-transforms your website and CMS content into a trusted answer engine. This ebook shows you how to replace outdated keyword search with natural-language, citation-backed answers that accelerate customer journeys and empower internal teams. Learn how agentic RAG unlocks the real value of unstructured content across marketing, sales, support, and product workflows.', '[\"Generative AI\",\"Agentic RAG\",\"Retrieval-Augmented Generation\",\"CMS\",\"Content Management\",\"Enterprise Search\",\"Generative Search\",\"Answer Engine\"]', 'banner_image-1784137804764-101927600.webp', 'pdf_file-1784137804962-75901548.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784137676344,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784137676505,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784137676680,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784137676824,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Download this practical guide showing how generative search-powered by agentic retrieval‑augmented generation (RAG)-turns existing website and content management system (CMS) content into a trusted, contextual answer engine that accelerates customer journeys, empowers internal teams and unlocks the real value of unstructured content.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">This comprehensive eBook covers:</h3><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why traditional CMS and keyword‑based search bury your best content and slow buying decisions, and how generative search removes friction with grounded, natural‑language answers</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How agentic RAG technology can ingest web pages, PDFs, videos and more to surface precise, citation‑backed insights tailored to user intent across languages and formats</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Which features make an enterprise‑grade generative CMS:</p></li></ul><ol><li><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Structured ingestion</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Multimodal search</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Modular pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: left;\">LLM‑agnostic flexibility that deploys in weeks, not years</p></li></ol><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How organizations can eliminate time‑consuming search, content re-creation and cross‑team inefficiencies through context‑aware answers and dynamic experience delivery</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What agentic RAG‑powered search can scale beyond marketing-from sales and support to product workflows-turning siloed assets into adaptive, personalized experiences at every touchpoint</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>', 'Websites Supercharged: Turn Your CMS into a Generative AI Answer Engine – Free Ebook', 'Discover how agentic RAG-powered generative search transforms website content into a trusted answer engine. Download this free ebook to accelerate customer journeys, empower teams, and unlock unstructured content with GenAI.', 'generative AI, agentic RAG, retrieval-augmented generation, CMS, content management system, generative search, answer engine, enterprise search, unstructured content, AI-powered search, natural language search, multimodal search, LLM, customer experience, digital transformation, knowledge management, free AI ebook, enterprise GenAI, content strategy, sales enablement', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-05-02 13:18:06', 'published', 64436, 0, 1, NULL, '2023-05-02 13:18:06', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(166, 2, 7, 2, 'The RAG Cookbook', 'the-rag-cookbook', 'RAG projects are failing at scale-42% of AI initiatives were scrapped in 2025, and production costs run 380% over budget. This cookbook gives you a practical, metric-driven framework to build RAG pipelines that actually work-from fundamental principles to advanced techniques like multi-step queries and metadata integration. Packed with grounded metrics and smart configuration guidance using Progress Agentic RAG, it\'s your recipe for enterprise-grade AI success.', '[\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"RAG\",\"Retrieval-Augmented\",\"Generation\",\"Generative AI\",\"LLMs\",\"Enterprise AI\",\"AI Implementation\",\"Machine Learning\",\"NLP\",\"AI Pipeline\",\"Agentic AI\",\"Data Retrieval\",\"AI Cost Optimization\"]', 'banner_image-1784138726262-232576632.webp', 'pdf_file-1784138726320-160283447.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784138670034,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784138670633,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784138670825,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784138671850,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2><strong>Why this Cookbook matters right now</strong></h2><ul><li><p>42% of companies scrapped most of their AI initiatives in 2025, up from 17% the year before – most because their RAG couldn’t scale past pilot</p></li><li><p>Average cost overrun for RAG projects at production scale is 380% versus pilot</p></li><li><p>Legal AI hallucination rates still hit 69%–88% on domain-specific questions without grounding</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What\'s inside the Cookbook</strong></h3><p>Use the official Cookbook TOC verbatim as a 5-point visual checklist:</p><ul><li><p>Fundamental RAG principles and how it bridges retrieval and generation</p></li><li><p>Key strategies to enrich context and enhance relevance of AI responses</p></li><li><p>Relevant metrics like relevance and grounded to evaluate your RAG pipeline</p></li><li><p>Advanced techniques: multi-step queries, data augmentation, metadata integration</p></li><li><p>Smart configuration of your RAG pipeline using Progress Agentic RAG</p></li></ul><p>Not ready to download? Get the 2-page executive summary instead - 6 stats your CFO needs to approve RAG spend.”</p>', 'The RAG Cookbook – Enterprise AI Implementation Guide', '42% of AI projects fail to scale. Learn how to build production-ready RAG pipelines with grounded metrics, advanced techniques, and smart configuration. Download the free RAG Cookbook now.', 'RAG, retrieval-augmented generation, artificial intelligence, generative AI, LLMs, enterprise AI, AI implementation, RAG pipeline, machine learning, NLP, AI metrics, hallucination reduction, scalable AI, Progress Agentic RAG, AI cost management, production AI, AI cookbook', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-05-04 17:01:37', 'published', 110697, 3, 1, NULL, '2023-05-04 17:01:37', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL);
INSERT INTO `contents` (`id`, `user_id`, `content_type_id`, `category_id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `tags`, `banner_image`, `pdf_file`, `video_file`, `email_subject`, `email_template`, `case_study_headline`, `case_study_summary`, `custom_fields`, `webhook_url`, `builder_layout`, `builder_content_elements`, `builder_page_data`, `webhook_field_mapping`, `content`, `seo_meta_title`, `seo_meta_description`, `seo_meta_keywords`, `scheduled_publish_date`, `webinar_date`, `hosted_by`, `platform`, `webinar_type`, `join_link`, `published_date`, `status`, `view_count`, `views_count`, `reading_time`, `admin_comment`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_visible_on_site`, `redirect_url`) VALUES
(167, 2, 7, 3, 'The Developer’s Guide to Connecting CRM Data, AI and App Experience, at Scale', 'the-developers-guide-to-connecting-crm-data-ai-and-app-experience-at-scale', 'Over 40% of agentic AI projects will fail by 2027-not because of bad models, but because of bad data. This developer-focused guide shows you how to build AI agents that tap into the full breadth of enterprise knowledge using Salesforce Data 360, Agentforce, and Heroku. Learn how to move beyond siloed CRM data, leverage RAG for accuracy, and collapse integration complexity to ship scalable, reliable AI applications faster.', '[\"Agentic AI\",\"CRM Data Integration\",\"Salesforce Data 360\",\"Agentforce\",\"Heroku\",\"Retrieval-Augmented Generation\",\"Enterprise AI\",\"AI Infrastructure\",\"Developer Guide\",\"Unstructured Data\",\"AI Scalability\",\"Data Foundation\"]', 'banner_image-1784146589550-531555611.webp', 'pdf_file-1784146589710-545733875.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784146351647,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784146351807,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784146351975,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784146352138,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The promise of agentic AI is real. So is the failure rate. More than 40% of agentic AI projects will be canceled by 2027, and most failures trace back to the same root cause: AI agents operating without the full enterprise context they need to act reliably. Bad data - siloed, fragmented, and largely unstructured - is the silent killer of AI projects that looked promising on paper.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The fix isn’t a better model. It’s a better foundation. This ebook by author Drew Robb shows developers and technical leaders how to build agentic AI applications that go beyond CRM data to tap the full breadth of enterprise knowledge - and how Salesforce Data 360, Agentforce, and Heroku work together to make that possible. Whether you’re evaluating your AI infrastructure stack or actively building agents for production, this guide gives you the architecture, tools, and practical framework to get there.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this ebook, you’ll discover:</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Why agentic AI projects really fail</strong> - and why the data foundation, not the model, is almost always the deciding factor.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How to move beyond CRM data</strong> - and give AI agents access to the unstructured enterprise knowledge that makes up 80-90% of your organization’s information.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>The RAG advantage</strong> - how retrieval-augmented generation resolves the accuracy-versus-latency tradeoff that slows most enterprise AI deployments.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How Heroku collapses integration complexity</strong> - turning a 14-step Salesforce integration process into a streamlined developer experience that lets lean teams ship faster.</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>How Agentforce and Heroku complement each other</strong> - and how the combination of Data 360, Agentforce, and Heroku creates a complete stack for building, deploying, and scaling autonomous AI agents across the enterprise.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">94% of business leaders feel they aren’t taking full advantage of the information available to them. The developers who close that gap - by building AI agents on a trusted, unified, enterprise-wide data foundation - will be the ones delivering measurable results while others are still troubleshooting hallucinations and cancelling projects.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Get your copy of “The Developer’s Guide to Connecting CRM Data, AI, and App Experience at Scale” and let us know what you think!</p>', 'The Developer’s Guide to Connecting CRM Data, AI and App Experience at Scale – Free Ebook', 'Over 40% of agentic AI projects fail due to bad data, not bad models. Download this free developer guide to build scalable AI agents with Salesforce Data 360, Agentforce, and Heroku. Includes RAG strategies, integration tips, and practical architecture.', 'agentic AI, CRM data integration, Salesforce Data 360, Agentforce, Heroku, RAG, retrieval-augmented generation, enterprise AI, AI agents, developer guide, unstructured data, AI infrastructure, AI scalability, data foundation for AI, Salesforce development, enterprise knowledge management, AI integration', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-05-08 12:44:08', 'published', 160177, 0, 2, NULL, '2023-05-08 12:44:08', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(168, 2, 7, 3, 'Better, Faster, Stronger: How Generative AI Transforms Software Development', 'better-faster-stronger-how-generative-ai-transforms-software-development', 'Generative AI is reshaping software development-but how do you separate hype from real value? This ebook, authored by TNS\'s Janakiram MSV and sponsored by Tabnine, cuts through the noise. It offers a clear roadmap for integrating GenAI across the SDLC, boosting developer productivity, navigating security risks, and choosing the right AI coding assistants-all while keeping your team ahead of the curve.', '[\"Generative AI\",\"Software Development\",\"AI Coding Assistants\",\"SDLC\",\"Developer Productivity\",\"Tabnine\",\"Janakiram MSV\",\"Large Language Models\",\"AI Security\",\"DevOps\",\"Code Generation\",\"AI Tools\",\"Software Engineering\"]', 'banner_image-1784202482940-292501961.webp', 'pdf_file-1784202483119-687735372.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784202437468,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784202437660,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784202437828,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784202438467,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>Whether you believe generative AI is the next big thing, worry it will ultimately be the downfall of humanity, or aren’t sure what you think about the topic, it’s clear that GenAI is here and the world will never be the same. But what is its impact on software development - and how can you reap the benefits?</p><p>In this strange, new landscape of transforming tech and constantly emerging tools, it can be difficult to determine how your team should apply generative AI to the software development life cycle. Thanks to TNS author Janakiram MSV and our sponsor, Tabnine, we’ve assembled the ultimate resource to guide you through this evolution of software engineering.</p><p>With your copy, you’ll learn:</p><ul><li><p>What generative AI is and how it differs from previous attempts at AI.</p></li><li><p>How generative AI affects developers (and how it can improve developer productivity).</p></li><li><p>How generative AI can enhance all phases of the software development life cycle.</p></li><li><p>Where the security risks are and how to mitigate them.</p></li><li><p>What to consider when evaluating AI coding assistants, large language models and more.</p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Get your copy now and let us know what you think!</p>', 'Better, Faster, Stronger: How Generative AI Transforms Software Development – Free Ebook', 'Discover how GenAI boosts developer productivity, secures your SDLC, and transforms software engineering. Free ebook by Janakiram MSV & Tabnine-download now.', 'generative AI software development, AI coding assistants, GenAI SDLC, developer productivity AI, Tabnine, Janakiram MSV, large language models coding, AI security software, software engineering AI, free AI ebook, AI tools for developers, future of software development', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-05-10 14:27:39', 'published', 73792, 1, 1, NULL, '2023-05-10 14:27:39', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(169, 2, 7, 3, 'AI for the Enterprise: The Playbook for Developing and Scaling Your AI Strategy', 'ai-for-the-enterprise-the-playbook-for-developing-and-scaling-your-ai-strategy', 'Enterprise AI adoption is rushing ahead, but without a strategic plan, organizations risk security failures, wasted investment, and eroded trust. This playbook, backed by Red Hat, Intel, and TNS writer Jennifer Riggins, offers a phased, intentional framework to measure true ROI, secure your data, and future-proof your strategy for the agentic era. Move beyond AI hype with actionable lessons from multinational companies on what actually works.', '[\"Enterprise AI\",\"AI Strategy\",\"AI ROI\",\"AI Governance\",\"Data Security\",\"Agentic AI\",\"Red Hat\",\"Intel\",\"Digital Transformation\",\"AI Implementation\",\"Generative AI\",\"AI Playbook\",\"AI Culture\",\"Developer Productivity\"]', 'banner_image-1784202884721-702420507.webp', 'pdf_file-1784202884830-797883130.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784202831860,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784202832036,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784202832199,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784202832340,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>There’s no debate that enterprises are rapidly adopting AI technology. The vast majority believe they must embrace it now or fall irrevocably behind. But in the rush to adopt, too many organizations are putting their long-term reliability and security at risk - alongside their employees’ trust. It’s time for a strategic, top-down plan that empowers your people, not just your technology.</p><p>This isn’t about splattering AI everywhere. It’s about taking an intentional approach to a massive investment. This playbook shares lessons from what’s working at multinational organizations - and what’s not. It’s both a snapshot in time and a look ahead, providing a framework to measure the ROI on your AI and an intentional way to chip away at the toil that distracts your teams from their best work. Thanks to TNS writer Jennifer Riggins, Red Hat, and Intel, this free book shows you how to ground your AI strategy in what’s working while inspiring a culture of continuous experimentation and learning.</p><p>In this playbook, you’ll discover:</p><ul><li><p>The Incremental Approach to AI: Learn how to implement AI in phases and use the “two-speed” investment model to tackle proven use cases while still making big bets on the future.</p></li><li><p>Best Practices for Data &amp; Security: Understand why data is your organization’s most important asset and how to centralize, clean, and secure it to unlock the true value of AI.</p></li><li><p>Ways to Measure AI’s True ROI: Move beyond simple productivity metrics. Get the frameworks and tools you need to measure the real impact of AI on everything from developer satisfaction to technical debt and overall cost.</p></li><li><p>How to Future-Proof Your Strategy: Move beyond today’s AI tools. Learn how to prepare for an agentic future and create a flexible, open source-backed strategy that helps you adapt to inevitable change.</p></li></ul><p>AI is no longer a fad. It must be a measurable strategy. By implementing an intentional, measurable, cross-organizational AI gameplan, you can unlock productivity gains, solve those previously impossible problems, and gain a true competitive edge.</p><h3>What do readers have to say about this ebook?</h3><p>“I really enjoyed reading the AI for the Enterprise eBook. It was well written and incredibly informative. A lot of media coverage is centered on the lack of AI ROI, but doesn’t actually point to actionable steps companies can take to prove it. I found that section to be especially helpful and recommended it to a few clients.”<br><em>Lauren Olvera, director media strategy, Archetype</em></p><p>“What a well written book; such useful guidance!”<br><em>- David Biesack, chief API officer, Apiture</em></p><p>“Finally an honest review on ugly truths behind the AI hype (and how to use AI right). I especially loved the part of developers feeling they deliver faster, while they are actually delivering slower. I also liked the importance of CAIO, and the governance process.”<br>- <em>Nikita Koselev, lead software development engineer, Mastercard</em></p><p>“Book recommendation for anyone serious about enterprise AI. What I particularly appreciated is that this book doesn’t treat AI as hype or a side project. It frames AI as an enterprise-wide transformation, grounded in real constraints: security, data, governance, developer experience, and, most importantly, measurable outcomes. IMO, she has done a great job showing how organizations can move from scattered experiments to scalable, repeatable AI practices, with a strong emphasis on incremental value rather than ‘big bang’ promises.”<br>- <em>David Roldán Martínez, chief AI officer and chief integration officer</em></p>', 'AI for the Enterprise: The Playbook for Developing & Scaling Your AI Strategy – Free eBook', 'Download this free enterprise AI playbook from Red Hat, Intel, and Jennifer Riggins. Learn a phased framework to measure AI ROI, secure data, and build a scalable, future-proof AI strategy that empowers people and drives real business outcomes.', 'enterprise AI, AI strategy, scaling AI, AI ROI measurement, AI governance, data security AI, agentic AI future, Red Hat Intel AI, Jennifer Riggins AI, AI playbook, two-speed AI model, AI implementation framework, enterprise digital transformation, AI best practices, AI culture change, technical debt AI, developer productivity AI, open source AI strategy', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-05-12 10:10:10', 'published', 78430, 1, 3, NULL, '2023-05-12 10:10:10', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(170, 2, 7, 3, 'The Developer\'s Guide to Cloud Infrastructure, Efficiency and Sustainability', 'the-developers-guide-to-cloud-infrastructure-efficiency-and-sustainability', 'Your cloud VM choices directly impact both efficiency and carbon footprint-yet CPU selection is often overlooked. In this ebook, technology writer Charles Humble (with insights from Google and AMD) explores how developers can build sustainable cloud infrastructure. Learn best practices for VM selection, measuring carbon emissions, and turning cloud computing from a climate problem into a climate solution.', '[\"Cloud Infrastructure\",\"Green Computing\",\"Sustainable Cloud\",\"CPU Optimization\",\"VM Selection\",\"Cloud Efficiency\",\"Carbon Footprint\",\"Environmental Sustainability\",\"Google Cloud\",\"Cloud Computing\",\"Energy Efficiency\"]', 'banner_image-1784203190162-134216352.webp', 'pdf_file-1784203190302-641700541.pdf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":1784203133964,\"name\":\"first_name\",\"label\":\"First Name\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"First Name\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"fname\"},{\"id\":1784203146908,\"name\":\"last_name\",\"label\":\"Last Name \",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Last Name \",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"lname\"},{\"id\":1784203147069,\"name\":\"contact\",\"label\":\"Contact\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Contact\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"phone\"},{\"id\":1784203147238,\"name\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"text\",\"placeholder\":\"Email\",\"options\":\"\",\"required\":true,\"webhook_key\":\"email\"}]', NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>The choices you make for your cloud infrastructure can have a major influence on environmental sustainability and efficiency. CPU choice gets less attention than it should for its impact on sustainability. Certain workloads perform best on certain CPUs and virtual machine types, and matching your workload to the appropriate VM instance helps you gain the most efficiency while minimizing the carbon footprint of your cloud instance.</p><p>Climate change is a difficult problem to solve, but there are things we can do - and are doing - to improve the situation. Thanks to Google and AMD, technology writer Charles Humble explores how cloud computing has been implicated as both a cause of and a solution for greenhouse gas emissions.</p><p>In this ebook, you’ll learn about:</p><ul><li><p>How developers are helping build a sustainable future</p></li><li><p>Developer best practices for choosing a cloud VM</p></li><li><p>The positive and negative environmental impact of cloud infrastructure</p></li><li><p>The factors that can make cloud computing “green”</p></li><li><p>How to measure carbon emissions from your cloud infrastructure</p></li></ul><p>Get your copy now and let us know what you think!</p>', 'The Developer\'s Guide to Cloud Infrastructure, Efficiency and Sustainability – Free Ebook', 'Learn how to choose the right cloud VMs and CPUs to boost efficiency while reducing carbon footprint. Free ebook by Charles Humble with insights from Google & AMD on sustainable cloud computing for developers.', 'sustainable cloud computing, green cloud infrastructure, cloud efficiency, CPU selection for sustainability, carbon footprint cloud, developer sustainability guide, Google cloud sustainability, AMD cloud optimization, green IT for developers, eco-friendly cloud computing, VM optimization, energy-efficient cloud, Charles Humble cloud ebook, sustainable development practices, cloud carbon emissions measurement', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-05-16 16:53:41', 'published', 165777, 2, 1, NULL, '2023-05-16 16:53:41', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL),
(174, 2, 3, 6, 'How to improve performance across the intralogistics lifecycle', 'how-to-improve-performance-across-the-intralogistics-lifecycle', 'Global supply chains are being reshaped by forces that are both unpredictable and deeply structural. Geopolitical realignment, trade policy shifts, sustainability demands, and talent shortages are rewriting the rules of global trade. For supply chain leaders, the real risk isn’t disruption itself, it’s not staying ahead of what’s coming.', '[]', 'banner_image-1784299534447-985903948.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{\"id\":\"sec-1784299428634\",\"type\":\"content_type_category\"},{\"id\":\"sec-1784299446569\",\"type\":\"title_description\"},{\"id\":\"sec-1784299464153\",\"type\":\"banner_image\"},{\"id\":\"sec-1784299339394\",\"type\":\"content\"}]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>Global supply chains are being reshaped by forces that are both unpredictable and deeply structural. Geopolitical realignment, trade policy shifts, sustainability demands, and talent shortages are rewriting the rules of global trade. For supply chain leaders, the real risk isn’t disruption itself, it’s not staying ahead of what’s coming.</p>\r\n<p>The mandate is clear: act fast, adapt continuously, and make smarter decisions to rise above your competitors. This e-book shows you how to do just that by strengthening your supply chain planning with a powerful AI framework like UnisonIQ.</p>\r\n<p>Key areas explored in the e-book:</p>\r\n<ul><li>Why AI matters now for supply chain planning, and how it can deliver measurable value, starting today</li></ul>\r\n<ul><li>How to move from process-centric to decision-centric planning</li></ul>\r\n<ul><li>How to employ your teams for the agentic age</li></ul>\r\n<ul><li>How leading companies are implementing AI for measurable outcomes</li></ul>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2023-05-18 11:36:12', 'published', 347548, 0, 1, NULL, '2023-05-18 11:36:12', '2026-10-05 19:46:48', 1, NULL);
