(839, 6, 2, 5, 'Best VPN Services of 2024: Expert-Tested Privacy and Security Picks', 'best-vpn-services-of-2024-expert-tested-privacy-and-security-picks', 'Compare the best VPN services of 2024 for privacy, speed, security, streaming, and device support with expert-tested recommendations.', '[\"VPN\",\"Best VPNs\",\"VPN Services\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"Online Privacy\",\"Internet Security\",\"Network Security\",\"Data Privacy\",\"VPN Security\",\"ExpressVPN\",\"Surfshark\",\"NordVPN\",\"Encryption\",\"Secure Browsing\",\"Privacy Protection\"]', 'banner_image-1789064584632-33617144.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Best VPN Services of 2024: Expert-Tested Privacy and Security Picks</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As online privacy, cybersecurity, and secure internet access become increasingly important, a reliable Virtual Private Network (VPN) can help protect internet traffic while providing greater control over online activity. However, VPN services differ considerably in areas such as speed, privacy practices, features, server coverage, and device compatibility.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Based on expert testing and evaluation, <strong>ExpressVPN, Surfshark, and NordVPN</strong> stand out among the leading VPN services for 2024. Each option has different strengths, making the right choice dependent on individual privacy requirements, budget, performance expectations, and usage patterns.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">ExpressVPN: Best Overall VPN</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ExpressVPN is a leading choice for users looking for a combination of privacy, performance, and ease of use. It received a <strong>CNET Editors’ Choice Award</strong> and achieved an <strong>8.8/10 rating</strong> in testing.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">One of ExpressVPN\'s key advantages is its focus on privacy and transparency. Its privacy policy is designed to clearly explain how user information is handled, while its <strong>Trusted Server technology</strong> is designed to operate VPN servers without permanently storing data on traditional hard drives.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ExpressVPN also uses its <strong>Lightway protocol</strong>, which is designed to provide fast and reliable connections while maintaining strong security. The service is straightforward to configure and can be useful for activities such as everyday browsing and accessing streaming services.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Its Advanced Protection features provide additional security controls, making the platform suitable for both people who are new to VPNs and more experienced privacy-conscious users.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Surfshark: A Cost-Effective VPN Option</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Surfshark is an attractive option for users who want strong VPN capabilities without paying premium prices. Its combination of performance, security features, and pricing makes it particularly appealing to individuals and households managing multiple devices.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During the 2024 comparison, Surfshark offered pricing that was considerably lower than some competing premium VPN services. It also supports <strong>unlimited simultaneous device connections</strong>, allowing users to protect multiple devices under a single subscription.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The service supports a broad range of platforms, including Apple TV and Linux, giving users more flexibility across computers, smartphones, smart TVs, and other connected devices.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">While Surfshark provides a strong collection of privacy and security tools, users with especially demanding privacy requirements may prefer services that place an even greater emphasis on privacy infrastructure and transparency.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">NordVPN: Feature-Rich and Fast</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">NordVPN is another strong choice for users who prioritize speed and advanced privacy capabilities. In 2024 testing, NordVPN recorded an average internet download-speed reduction of approximately <strong>11.1%</strong>, placing it among the faster VPN services evaluated.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Beyond standard VPN functionality, NordVPN offers several advanced tools. These include <strong>Double VPN</strong>, which routes traffic through multiple VPN servers, and <strong>Onion Over VPN</strong>, which combines VPN protection with access to the Tor network.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">NordVPN also provides <strong>Meshnet</strong>, a feature designed to enable secure connections between devices, along with conventional capabilities such as split tunneling.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These features make NordVPN particularly appealing to experienced users who want greater control over their network privacy and security configuration.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">How to Choose the Right VPN</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">There is no single VPN that is perfect for every user. The best option depends on what you value most.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Users primarily interested in straightforward privacy protection may prefer a simple and user-friendly service. People managing several devices may benefit from unlimited simultaneous connections, while power users may prioritize advanced networking and privacy features.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Before purchasing a VPN subscription, consider its performance, privacy practices, server availability, supported devices, and overall cost.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Important Factors to Consider When Choosing a VPN</h2><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Internet Speed</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">VPN encryption and routing can reduce internet speeds because your traffic travels through an encrypted VPN connection. A high-performing VPN should minimize this impact.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For regular browsing, video calls, and streaming, moderate speed reductions may not be noticeable. Gamers and users who frequently stream high-resolution video should look for services with consistently low download and upload performance losses.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Privacy and Security Features</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Privacy should be one of the most important considerations when selecting a VPN. Look for services offering strong encryption, a clearly defined no-logging policy, and DNS leak protection.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Independent security audits and transparency reports can also provide additional insight into how a provider handles user information.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Advanced users may want additional capabilities such as obfuscated connections, Tor integration, or multi-hop and Double VPN functionality.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Server Network</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The size and geographic distribution of a VPN provider\'s server network can influence connection options and performance.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A broad selection of countries can be useful for travelers and users who need connections in specific regions. Users interested in peer-to-peer activities should also check whether the provider supports P2P traffic and whether dedicated servers are available.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Some VPN providers additionally offer specialty servers designed for enhanced privacy or specific networking requirements.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Device Compatibility</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Before subscribing, check whether the VPN supports all of your devices.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Most major VPN services provide applications for Windows, macOS, Android, iOS, and other popular platforms. Some providers also support Linux, smart TVs, browser extensions, and streaming devices.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The number of devices that can be connected simultaneously is another important consideration. Users with several computers, smartphones, tablets, and smart TVs may benefit from plans that allow multiple or unlimited connections.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Final Thoughts</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ExpressVPN, Surfshark, and NordVPN each provide a compelling combination of privacy, security, and performance, but their strengths differ.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>ExpressVPN</strong> is a strong all-around choice for users who prioritize privacy and ease of use. <strong>Surfshark</strong> stands out for its value and unlimited simultaneous connections, while <strong>NordVPN</strong> is particularly attractive to users looking for high performance and advanced security features.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Before choosing a provider, compare its privacy policy, speed, server network, supported devices, security features, and subscription cost. A VPN should ultimately match your specific online privacy and connectivity requirements.</p>', 'Best VPN Services of 2024 | Expert-Tested VPN Guide', 'Explore the best VPN services of 2024 for privacy, security, speed, streaming, server coverage, and multi-device support.', 'best VPN 2024, best VPN services, VPN comparison, VPN security, online privacy, cybersecurity, ExpressVPN, Surfshark, NordVPN, secure browsing, internet security', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-15 17:32:39', 'published', 2617160, 0, 5, NULL, '2026-09-15 17:32:39', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL),
(840, 6, 2, 12, 'How AI-Powered Automation Is Transforming SD-WAN Optimization', 'how-ai-powered-automation-is-transforming-sd-wan-optimization', 'AI-powered automation is transforming SD-WAN optimization by improving network visibility, predicting issues, accelerating troubleshooting, and boosting efficiency.', '[\"SD-WAN\",\"AI Networking\",\"Network Automation\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Machine Learning\",\"AIOps\",\"Network Optimization\",\"SD-WAN Solutions\",\"SD-WAN Managed Services\",\"Network Management\",\"Generative AI\",\"Network Security\",\"IT Networking\",\"Network Operations\",\"Enterprise Networking\"]', 'banner_image-1789064703733-890693324.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">How AI-Powered Automation Is Transforming SD-WAN Optimization</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Software-defined wide area networking (SD-WAN) is becoming increasingly important as organizations operate across cloud platforms, branch offices, remote locations, and distributed IT environments. As network infrastructures become more complex, traditional manual approaches to monitoring and troubleshooting are becoming less effective.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A recent survey of IT and networking professionals highlights the growing importance of artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning (ML), and automation in SD-WAN environments. Nearly all respondents-97%-believe AI and ML-driven automation are essential for modern SD-WAN operations, with some considering these capabilities critical to network performance and management.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The research, conducted by TechTarget’s Enterprise Strategy Group (ESG), included 374 networking professionals from the United States and Canada. The findings demonstrate that organizations are looking for more dynamic and intelligent ways to manage increasingly distributed network infrastructures.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI and Automation Improve Network Operations</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Network operations teams are under increasing pressure to identify problems quickly and resolve them before they affect users or business applications. Two important performance measurements are mean time to detect (MTTD) and mean time to repair (MTTR).</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI, ML, and automation can help organizations improve both metrics by continuously analyzing network activity and identifying potential problems. According to the survey, 40% of respondents identified unusual activity detection as an important AI capability. Predictive analytics and early issue identification were highlighted by 39%, while another 39% pointed to faster troubleshooting as a major advantage.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These capabilities can allow network teams to move from reactive troubleshooting toward a more proactive approach. Instead of waiting for an outage or performance problem to occur, AI-powered systems can analyze patterns and provide early warnings about potential network issues.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI can also recommend configuration changes, identify opportunities to optimize network performance, and eventually automate certain remediation tasks. As organizations gain confidence in AI-driven recommendations, more network operations could be performed with limited human intervention.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI Capabilities Are Expanding Across Network Equipment</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The growing demand for intelligent network operations has encouraged networking vendors to integrate AI and ML capabilities into their products and services. These developments are strengthening the role of AIOps in network management and creating new possibilities for SD-WAN solutions and managed networking services.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Cisco has introduced AI-enhanced networking, security, and visibility capabilities designed to provide organizations with greater insight into their digital environments. These technologies can help IT teams understand network conditions, identify risks, and respond to operational challenges more efficiently.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Extreme Networks has also expanded its AI capabilities through AI Expert. The service gathers information from across the network and uses it to provide insights, improve operational efficiency, and identify potential problems. Examples include detecting network overloads and identifying Wi-Fi coverage issues.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Juniper Networks has similarly expanded AI-driven capabilities for SD-WAN environments. Its Marvis technology has been extended to support SD-WAN operations, helping identify authentication problems, conduct continuous network testing, and diagnose issues before they become more serious.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These developments demonstrate how AI is moving beyond simple monitoring and becoming an increasingly important part of network management.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Generative AI Could Become a Network Administrator Copilot</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Generative AI (GenAI) is another technology that could significantly influence the future of network administration. The networking industry is facing a skills shortage, while modern SD-WAN infrastructures require professionals with increasingly specialized knowledge.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">John Burke, chief technology officer at Nemertes Research, has noted that many newer IT professionals enter the industry with broad IT knowledge rather than deep networking specialization. GenAI could help address some of this gap by assisting less-experienced administrators with routine networking activities and incident response.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the future, GenAI could function as a network administrator copilot, helping teams document SD-WAN environments, develop network policies, review configurations, and perform audits.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Generative AI may also assist network engineers with scripting and automation. However, AI-generated scripts should still be carefully reviewed and tested by experienced professionals before being deployed in production environments.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI Can Make SD-WAN Management More Proactive</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">One of the biggest advantages of AI-driven SD-WAN automation is the ability to continuously analyze large volumes of network data. This can help organizations identify unusual behavior, discover performance bottlenecks, predict potential failures, and prioritize issues based on their business impact.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Instead of relying entirely on manual dashboards and alerts, IT teams can use intelligent systems to surface the most important problems and recommend appropriate actions.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For organizations using SD-WAN managed services, these capabilities can also improve service delivery by helping providers monitor network environments more efficiently and respond to incidents faster.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Future of AI in SD-WAN</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The integration of AI, ML, and automation into SD-WAN management reflects the growing complexity of modern enterprise networks. With businesses adopting cloud services, remote work models, branch connectivity, and distributed applications, network teams need more intelligent tools to maintain performance and security.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Fully autonomous network management is still some distance away, particularly for critical enterprise environments where human oversight remains essential. However, AI-powered tools can already provide valuable assistance with monitoring, troubleshooting, optimization, and decision-making.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As these technologies continue to mature, AI is likely to become an important component of SD-WAN solutions. Organizations that combine intelligent automation with experienced network professionals can improve operational efficiency, reduce response times, and build more resilient network infrastructures.</p>', 'AI-Powered Automation for SD-WAN Optimization', 'Discover how AI, ML, and automation are improving SD-WAN optimization, network monitoring, troubleshooting, predictive analytics, and IT efficiency.', 'SD-WAN, AI-powered SD-WAN, SD-WAN automation, network automation, AI networking, machine learning networking, SD-WAN optimization, AIOps, SD-WAN solutions, SD-WAN managed services, network management, generative AI networking, IT networking, network operations', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-16 12:02:52', 'published', 3027599, 0, 5, NULL, '2026-09-16 12:02:52', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL),
(841, 6, 2, 12, 'Single-Vendor SASE Trends and the Evolution of SD-WAN in 2024', 'single-vendor-sase-trends-and-the-evolution-of-sd-wan-in-2024', 'Explore 2024 SASE and SD-WAN trends, including single-vendor adoption, Zscaler\'s strategy, AI integration, zero trust, and market growth.', '[\"SASE\",\"Single-Vendor SASE\",\"SD-WAN\",\"Zscaler\",\"Network Security\",\"Secure Access Service Edge\",\"Software-Defined WAN\",\"Zero Trust\",\"Enterprise Networking\",\"Cloud Security\",\"Network Transformation\",\"AI Networking\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"WAN Connectivity\",\"SASE Trends\"]', 'banner_image-1789064959011-628756041.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Understanding the Shift Toward Single-Vendor SASE</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Secure Access Service Edge (SASE) market entered an important phase of development in 2024 as enterprises increasingly showed interest in single-vendor solutions. Instead of deploying separate networking and security products from multiple providers, organizations are looking for integrated platforms that can simplify WAN connectivity, security management, and operational processes.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This transition is being driven by the growing complexity of enterprise networks. Hybrid work, cloud applications, distributed offices, remote users, and expanding edge environments have made traditional WAN architectures more difficult to manage. SASE brings networking and security capabilities together to provide organizations with a more unified approach.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Zscaler Expands Into SD-WAN</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A major development in the SASE landscape has been Zscaler\'s expansion into the SD-WAN market. The company has traditionally been recognized for its Security Service Edge (SSE) capabilities, but its move into SD-WAN allows it to address a broader range of enterprise networking requirements.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">By combining SD-WAN capabilities with its existing security portfolio, Zscaler is positioning itself to compete in the growing single-vendor SASE market. The strategy reflects a broader industry movement in which security and networking providers are expanding their portfolios to deliver more complete SASE platforms.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">According to market analysis from the Dell\'Oro Group, single-vendor SASE solutions accounted for a substantial portion of SASE revenue during the first quarter of 2024. The strong share demonstrates the increasing preference among enterprises for consolidated networking and security services.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For customers, a single-vendor architecture can potentially reduce deployment complexity, simplify management, and provide a more consistent security and networking experience across distributed environments.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">SD-WAN and SASE Market Outlook</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The relationship between SD-WAN and SASE is expected to become increasingly important over the coming years. Gartner has projected that by 2027, a significantly larger percentage of new SD-WAN deployments will be purchased as part of single-vendor SASE offerings compared with 2024.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This expected increase highlights how enterprise buyers are moving toward platforms that combine connectivity, security, cloud access, and centralized management rather than purchasing each capability independently.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The trend also creates opportunities for vendors to expand their addressable market. Networking companies can add security capabilities, while security vendors can introduce networking functions such as SD-WAN. As a result, the boundaries between traditional networking and security providers are becoming less distinct.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Major SASE and SD-WAN Trends in 2024</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Several developments are influencing the SASE and SD-WAN markets in 2024.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>1. Continued SD-WAN Market Expansion</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SD-WAN has become an important component of modern enterprise networking. The market surpassed $5 billion by the end of 2023, while continued adoption is expected to drive further growth over the coming years.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Organizations are adopting SD-WAN to improve connectivity across branch offices, cloud environments, data centers, and remote locations. Its ability to provide centralized control and dynamically manage network traffic makes it particularly relevant for distributed businesses.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>2. Growing Global Adoption</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SD-WAN adoption is expanding across global enterprises as businesses modernize their network infrastructure. Enterprises increasingly require flexible connectivity that can support cloud applications, remote employees, multiple offices, and geographically distributed operations.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The continued deployment of SD-WAN is expected to strengthen demand for SASE platforms because organizations can combine networking modernization with security transformation.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>3. Consolidation of Networking and Security Features</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">One of the most important SASE trends is the consolidation of multiple technologies into a unified platform.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Single-vendor solutions can bring capabilities such as SD-WAN, secure web access, cloud security, zero trust access, firewall functionality, and other security services under a common management framework.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This model may be particularly attractive to small and mid-sized businesses that have limited IT resources and want to avoid managing numerous independent security and networking products.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>4. AI-Driven Network and Security Operations</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Artificial intelligence is becoming an increasingly important component of networking and security technologies.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI-powered analytics can help organizations identify unusual traffic patterns, detect potential security risks, optimize network performance, and automate routine operational tasks.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As AI capabilities mature, SASE and SD-WAN platforms are expected to use intelligent automation to improve visibility, troubleshooting, policy management, and overall network efficiency.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>5. Convergence of SD-WAN and SASE</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The traditional distinction between SD-WAN and SASE is becoming less obvious.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SD-WAN primarily focuses on connectivity and network optimization, while SASE extends the architecture by incorporating cloud-delivered security capabilities. As vendors combine these technologies, organizations can increasingly deploy networking and security through a single integrated architecture.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This convergence is particularly relevant as enterprise networks expand beyond traditional office locations and data centers into cloud platforms, remote environments, and edge locations.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>6. Zero Trust as a Core Security Model</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Zero trust is another major element of the SASE transformation.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Rather than automatically trusting users or devices based on their network location, zero trust requires continuous verification and access control. Users and devices are granted access according to identity, context, security posture, and defined policies.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Integrating zero trust principles with SASE allows organizations to build security controls around users, applications, devices, and data rather than relying primarily on traditional network perimeters.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why Enterprises Are Moving Toward Single-Vendor SASE</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The increasing adoption of single-vendor SASE is closely connected to the need for simpler IT operations.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Managing separate networking and security products can create integration challenges, increase administrative workloads, and make troubleshooting more complicated. A consolidated platform can provide centralized management and potentially reduce the number of technologies that IT teams need to operate.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For larger organizations, single-vendor SASE can also support consistent security policies across branches, remote users, cloud applications, and other distributed environments.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the same time, enterprises need to evaluate factors such as interoperability, scalability, security capabilities, vendor flexibility, performance, and long-term costs before committing to a single-vendor architecture.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">What the Future Holds for SASE</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The SASE market is moving toward greater convergence between networking and security. Vendors are expanding their portfolios, while enterprises are looking for platforms that can support increasingly distributed IT environments.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Zscaler\'s move into SD-WAN represents one example of this broader market direction. Other vendors are similarly combining networking and security technologies to compete for a larger share of the enterprise technology market.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As AI, zero trust, cloud adoption, and edge computing continue to influence enterprise infrastructure, SASE is likely to become an increasingly important framework for connecting and securing users, applications, devices, and locations.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ultimately, the growth of single-vendor SASE reflects a broader shift toward <strong>integrated, cloud-based, and centrally managed networking and security architectures</strong>. Organizations that successfully adopt these technologies can simplify infrastructure while improving visibility, security, and connectivity across their modern IT environments.</p>', 'Single-Vendor SASE & SD-WAN Trends 2024', 'Explore 2024 SASE and SD-WAN trends, single-vendor adoption, Zscaler\'s strategy, AI, zero trust, and the future of enterprise networking.', 'SASE market trends 2024, single-vendor SASE, SD-WAN market, Zscaler SD-WAN, SASE solutions, SD-WAN trends, network security, zero trust, cloud security, enterprise networking, SASE adoption, AI networking', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-16 14:48:05', 'published', 3136854, 0, 6, NULL, '2026-09-16 14:48:05', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL),
(842, 6, 1, 5, 'ExpressVPN Cuts Subscription Prices With New 2-Year Deal and Free Extra Months', 'expressvpn-cuts-subscription-prices-with-new-2-year-deal-and-free-extra-months', 'ExpressVPN has reduced its long-term subscription price, offering users a more affordable VPN plan with three additional months of free protection.', '[\"ExpressVPN\",\"VPN\",\"VPN Solutions\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"Online Privacy\",\"Internet Security\",\"VPN Security\",\"Data Protection\",\"Network Security\",\"Privacy Protection\",\"Small Business Security\",\"Secure Browsing\",\"Remote Work Security\",\"Endpoint Security\"]', 'banner_image-1789065147369-212055602.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">ExpressVPN Introduces Lower Pricing With a New Long-Term Offer</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ExpressVPN, one of the widely recognized names in the VPN solutions market, has introduced lower pricing for its long-term subscription plans. The move makes the service more accessible to users looking for stronger online privacy, secure browsing, streaming access, and protection across multiple devices.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">VPN services have become increasingly important for individuals and businesses seeking to protect internet traffic, particularly when using public networks or accessing online services from different locations. ExpressVPN has positioned itself as a user-friendly option for both beginners and experienced VPN users.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The latest pricing change addresses one of the major concerns previously associated with the service: its comparatively higher subscription cost.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">New ExpressVPN 2-Year Pricing</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Under the new offer, users can access ExpressVPN for approximately <strong>$5.32 per month when subscribing to the 2-year plan</strong>. The promotion also includes <strong>three additional months at no extra cost</strong>, providing a total of 27 months of service while paying for 24 months.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This represents a considerable change from the previous long-term pricing structure and improves the overall value for customers who are willing to commit to a longer subscription period.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The standard 1-year subscription continues to be available, but it does not provide the same three-month extension included with the promotional 2-year package.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The promotional pricing is particularly relevant for customers who have been considering a premium VPN but were previously discouraged by subscription costs.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">What Makes ExpressVPN Popular?</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ExpressVPN has built its reputation around privacy, security, performance, and ease of use. Its applications are designed to make VPN configuration relatively simple, allowing users to establish protected connections without requiring extensive technical knowledge.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The service supports a wide range of devices and platforms, making it suitable for people who regularly switch between computers, smartphones, tablets, and other connected devices.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Some of its commonly highlighted features include:</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Secure encrypted internet connections</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">User-friendly applications</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Support across multiple platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">High-speed VPN connections</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Privacy-focused features</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Streaming and location-access capabilities</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Simplified VPN configuration</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Protection when using public Wi-Fi networks</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These capabilities have helped ExpressVPN remain a frequently considered option among consumers looking for a premium VPN service.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Independent Privacy Audits</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Another factor contributing to ExpressVPN\'s reputation is its use of independent security and privacy assessments. The company has undergone multiple independent audits intended to provide greater transparency around its privacy and security practices.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Independent assessments can be particularly valuable in the VPN industry because users generally have limited visibility into how a provider handles network activity and customer information.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For users who prioritize privacy, third-party audits can therefore provide an additional layer of confidence when evaluating VPN providers.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">A Practical Option for New VPN Users</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ExpressVPN\'s simple interface makes it suitable for people who may be unfamiliar with VPN technology. Instead of requiring users to manually configure complex settings, its applications are designed to make connecting to a VPN server straightforward.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This ease of use can also benefit small businesses and remote workers that need a convenient way to improve network security while working from different locations.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The combination of accessibility, performance, security features, and broad device support has helped ExpressVPN appeal to a wide range of users.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Better Value for Long-Term Subscribers</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The new 2-year pricing structure could make ExpressVPN more attractive to customers who plan to use a VPN service for an extended period. The additional three months included with the promotion further increases the overall value of the package.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Lower pricing could also increase competition among VPN providers, encouraging other companies to improve their subscription offers, features, and customer benefits.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For consumers comparing VPN services, pricing should still be considered alongside factors such as privacy policies, security features, connection performance, supported devices, server availability, and customer support.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Final Thoughts</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ExpressVPN\'s updated 2-year pricing gives users another reason to consider the service, particularly those who previously viewed its subscription cost as a disadvantage.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With the promotional plan priced at approximately <strong>$5.32 per month</strong> and three additional months included, the offer provides a more competitive option for users seeking a premium VPN solution.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Whether the service is being considered for personal privacy, secure remote work, public Wi-Fi protection, streaming, or small-business use, the new pricing makes ExpressVPN more accessible to customers looking for long-term VPN protection.</p>', 'ExpressVPN Lowers Prices With New 2-Year VPN Deal', 'ExpressVPN has lowered its 2-year subscription price to $5.32 per month and added three free months, making its VPN service more affordable.', 'ExpressVPN, ExpressVPN deal, ExpressVPN price, VPN deal, VPN solutions, best VPN, VPN security, cybersecurity, online privacy, internet security, secure VPN, business VPN, small business VPN, data protection', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-16 17:33:18', 'published', 3371492, 0, 4, NULL, '2026-09-16 17:33:18', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL),
(843, 6, 2, 10, 'Best VPN Solutions for Windows: Secure, Fast, and Private Browsing', 'best-vpn-solutions-for-windows-secure-fast-and-private-browsing', 'Discover the best VPN solutions for Windows with secure encryption, fast connections, global servers, and simple privacy features for everyday use.', '[\"VPN\",\"Windows VPN\",\"VPN Solutions\",\"Online Privacy\",\"Internet Security\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"Data Encryption\",\"Secure Browsing\",\"Forest VPN\",\"Network Security\"]', 'banner_image-1789065270350-275837165.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Best VPN Solutions for Windows: Secure, Fast, and Private Browsing</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In an increasingly connected digital environment, protecting online activity has become an important priority for Windows users. From personal browsing and online transactions to remote work and accessing business resources, internet traffic can be exposed to various privacy and security risks.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A Virtual Private Network (VPN) helps address these concerns by encrypting internet traffic and masking the user\'s IP address. This creates a more secure connection between the device and the internet, making it harder for unauthorized parties to monitor online activity.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With numerous VPN applications available for Windows, choosing the right solution requires a balance of security, performance, usability, and pricing. Forest VPN is designed to provide Windows users with a straightforward way to improve their online privacy without making the experience unnecessarily complicated.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why Consider Forest VPN for Windows?</h3><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Strong Security and Privacy</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Security is one of the primary reasons users choose a VPN. Forest VPN uses advanced encryption technology to help protect information transmitted over an internet connection.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The solution highlights several privacy-focused features:</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>No-Logging Approach:</strong><br>\r\nForest VPN states that it does not maintain records of users\' browsing activity, providing an additional layer of privacy.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>AES-256 Encryption:</strong><br>\r\nAES-256 encryption is widely used for protecting sensitive information. By encrypting network traffic, VPN services can help reduce the risk of unauthorized access to data.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Simple Setup and User-Friendly Experience</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A VPN should provide protection without requiring users to understand complicated networking configurations. Forest VPN focuses on a simple interface suitable for both new and experienced VPN users.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>One-Click Connection:</strong><br>\r\nUsers can activate the VPN connection with a single click, allowing them to establish protected connectivity quickly.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Unlimited Data:</strong><br>\r\nForest VPN provides unlimited data usage, making it suitable for activities such as browsing, streaming, and downloading.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Global Server Access:</strong><br>\r\nThe service offers access to more than 50 server locations across over 30 countries, giving users greater flexibility when selecting a virtual connection location.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Fast and Reliable Connections</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Security is important, but connection performance also plays a major role in choosing a VPN. Poorly optimized VPN connections can introduce latency and reduce browsing speeds.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Forest VPN is designed to maintain stable connectivity while minimizing performance issues. Users can also switch between available servers if their current connection does not provide the desired performance.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Battery Optimization:</strong><br>\r\nA battery-saving feature is designed to reduce power consumption, which can be useful for people using VPN protection on laptops and other portable Windows devices.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Easy Server Switching:</strong><br>\r\nIf a particular server becomes congested or delivers slower performance, users can select another available server to improve their connection experience.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Affordable VPN Protection</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For many individuals and businesses, cost is another consideration when selecting a VPN service. Forest VPN aims to provide privacy and security features at an accessible price point.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Transparent pricing can also make it easier for users to understand what they are paying for before committing to a VPN service.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">What Users Look for in a Windows VPN</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">VPN users commonly prioritize a combination of security, performance, and convenience. A practical Windows VPN should ideally provide strong encryption, a simple interface, reliable connections, and flexible server options.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Features such as a no-logging policy and unlimited data can also be important for users who want consistent privacy protection during everyday internet use.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Tips for Using a VPN Effectively</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Getting the most from a VPN involves more than simply installing the application. Windows users can follow a few practices to improve their overall experience.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Use Split Tunneling:</strong><br>\r\nSplit tunneling allows users to decide which applications use the VPN connection and which connect directly to the internet. This can help optimize network traffic for specific use cases.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Experiment With Different Servers:</strong><br>\r\nConnection performance can vary depending on server location and network conditions. Trying another server may improve speed or provide access to region-specific online services.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Keep the VPN Application Updated:</strong><br>\r\nRegular software updates can introduce security improvements, bug fixes, performance enhancements, and new features. Keeping the VPN client updated helps ensure users are running the latest version.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Future of VPN Solutions for Windows</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Online privacy and cybersecurity threats continue to evolve as more personal and professional activities move online. VPN providers therefore need to continuously improve their technologies to address emerging security and connectivity challenges.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For Windows users, a VPN can be an important component of a broader online security strategy. However, it should be used alongside other security practices such as strong passwords, multi-factor authentication, updated software, and awareness of phishing and other online threats.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Forest VPN focuses on combining security, performance, and usability into a single Windows-oriented VPN solution. Whether the goal is safer everyday browsing, protecting data while using public networks, or improving online privacy, a reliable VPN can provide an additional layer of protection.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Conclusion</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Choosing the right VPN solution for Windows depends on factors such as encryption, privacy practices, connection speed, server availability, ease of use, and pricing. Forest VPN brings these considerations together with features including AES-256 encryption, a no-logging approach, unlimited data, global server access, and simple connection controls.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For Windows users looking for a convenient way to strengthen their online privacy and secure internet traffic, evaluating a VPN based on these features can help them make a more informed decision.</p>', 'Best VPN Solutions for Windows | Secure & Private Browsing', 'Explore the best VPN solutions for Windows with strong encryption, fast connections, global servers, unlimited data, and enhanced online privacy.', 'best VPN for Windows, Windows VPN, VPN solutions, Forest VPN, VPN software, online privacy, internet security, secure browsing, VPN encryption, Windows security, data protection, cybersecurity, VPN servers', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-17 12:03:31', 'published', 1732424, 0, 5, NULL, '2026-09-17 12:03:31', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL);
