(844, 6, 2, 5, 'How to Secure Your Wi-Fi Network with a VPN and Stronger Privacy Practices', 'how-to-secure-your-wi-fi-network-with-a-vpn-and-stronger-privacy-practices', 'Learn how VPN technology can strengthen Wi-Fi security, protect sensitive data, and reduce online risks when using public or home networks.', '[\"Wi-Fi Security\",\"VPN\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"Network Security\",\"Online Privacy\",\"Data Protection\",\"Internet Security\",\"Public Wi-Fi\",\"Encryption\",\"Remote Work\",\"Cyber Threats\",\"Digital Security\",\"VPN Solutions\"]', 'banner_image-1789065426452-595957927.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">How to Secure Your Wi-Fi Network with a VPN and Stronger Privacy Practices</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As more business activities, communications, financial transactions, and personal interactions move online, securing your internet connection has become increasingly important. Wi-Fi networks are convenient, but poorly secured networks can expose users and organizations to threats such as data interception, malicious websites, phishing attempts, and unauthorized access.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A Virtual Private Network (VPN) can provide an additional layer of protection by encrypting internet traffic and helping keep online activity private. When combined with strong Wi-Fi settings, updated devices, and good security practices, a VPN can significantly improve your overall digital security.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">What Is a VPN and How Does It Improve Security?</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A Virtual Private Network creates an encrypted connection between your device and a VPN server. Instead of sending internet traffic directly across the network, the VPN routes that traffic through an encrypted tunnel.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This can make it more difficult for third parties on the same network to monitor or intercept your internet traffic. A VPN can also mask your device\'s IP address, providing an additional level of privacy while browsing.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For example, consider an employee working from a coffee shop, airport, hotel, or other location that provides public Wi-Fi. Connecting to an unsecured network can create opportunities for attackers to intercept poorly protected communications. Using a reputable VPN can help reduce this exposure by encrypting the connection between the device and the VPN service.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">However, a VPN should not be considered a complete cybersecurity solution. It works best when combined with other security controls such as multi-factor authentication, strong passwords, endpoint protection, and secure network configurations.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why Wi-Fi Security Matters</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Wi-Fi networks are now used by laptops, smartphones, tablets, smart TVs, business systems, IoT devices, and other connected equipment. This expanding ecosystem increases the number of potential entry points for cyber threats.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Public Wi-Fi can be particularly challenging because users generally have little control over how the network is configured or who else is connected to it. Attackers may attempt to exploit weak configurations, create malicious hotspots, or target users through phishing and other techniques.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Home networks also require attention. A compromised router or weak Wi-Fi password could potentially provide attackers with access to connected devices and sensitive information.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For businesses, unsecured wireless connections can create even greater risks because employees may access corporate applications, cloud platforms, customer information, and internal systems remotely.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">How a VPN Protects Your Internet Traffic</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">One of the primary benefits of a VPN is encryption. Encryption converts readable information into an encoded format that is difficult for unauthorized parties to understand.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When you use a VPN, your internet traffic is encrypted before it travels through the network to the VPN server. This can help protect information such as:</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Login credentials</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Business communications</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Personal information</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Financial transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Browsing activity</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Files transferred over the internet</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The strength of the protection depends on the VPN provider, protocols, device configuration, and the services you access. Users should therefore choose established VPN providers with transparent security practices and reliable encryption technologies.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Using a VPN on Public Wi-Fi</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Public Wi-Fi networks are convenient for remote workers and travelers, but they can introduce additional security risks.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Before connecting to a public network, verify that you are using the legitimate network provided by the business or location. Attackers can sometimes create networks with names that resemble legitimate hotspots to trick users into connecting.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Once connected, using a VPN can provide an encrypted connection for your internet traffic.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For example, a remote employee working from a café may use a VPN before accessing business email, cloud applications, or company resources. The VPN helps protect traffic between the employee\'s device and the VPN server, reducing the risk associated with transmitting information over an untrusted local network.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Nevertheless, sensitive activities should still be performed cautiously on public networks.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">VPNs for Remote and Hybrid Work</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Remote and hybrid working have made secure internet access increasingly important for businesses.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Employees may connect to company resources from homes, hotels, coworking spaces, airports, or other locations. A VPN can help establish a protected connection when employees are working outside the corporate network.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Organizations can combine VPN technology with other security measures, including:</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Multi-factor authentication</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Endpoint security</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Zero Trust security principles</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Identity and access management</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Secure DNS</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Device encryption</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Security monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Strong password policies</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This layered approach helps organizations reduce their dependence on any single security technology.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key VPN Features to Consider</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When evaluating a VPN solution, businesses and individual users should look beyond basic encryption. Important capabilities may include:</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Encryption and Secure Protocols</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A reliable VPN should use modern encryption standards and secure VPN protocols. These technologies help protect data as it travels between the user\'s device and the VPN infrastructure.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Threat and Malware Protection</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Some VPN providers offer additional security features designed to block malicious websites, suspicious downloads, trackers, or other online threats. These capabilities can complement, but should not replace, dedicated endpoint security software.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Device Compatibility</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A VPN should support the operating systems and devices used by your organization or household. Support for Windows, macOS, Linux, Android, and iOS can be important for users with multiple devices.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Secure Remote Connectivity</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Features that support secure connections between devices can be useful for remote workers and distributed teams. Depending on the provider, these capabilities may allow users to connect securely to selected devices or resources.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Account and Credential Protection</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Strong authentication and password management can further improve security. Users should consider solutions that support multi-factor authentication and encourage the use of unique passwords for every account.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Privacy Controls</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Before choosing a VPN provider, review its privacy policy and understand what information it collects, how long it retains that information, and under what circumstances it may share data with third parties.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">VPN and Password Security Work Together</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A VPN protects the network connection, but it does not automatically protect every account you use.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Strong password practices remain essential. Users should create unique passwords for important accounts and avoid reusing the same password across multiple services.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A password manager can help generate and store strong credentials, while multi-factor authentication adds another layer of protection if a password is compromised.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The combination of:</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>VPN + strong passwords + multi-factor authentication + updated devices</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">provides significantly stronger protection than relying on a VPN alone.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Best Practices for Safer Wi-Fi</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A VPN is only one part of a broader Wi-Fi security strategy. Consider the following practices:</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Keep Devices Updated</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Install operating system, browser, application, and security updates regularly. Software updates frequently include patches for known vulnerabilities.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Use a Strong Wi-Fi Password</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Your home or office wireless network should use a long, unique password that is difficult to guess. Avoid using names, birthdays, phone numbers, or commonly used phrases.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Enable Modern Wi-Fi Security</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Where supported, use modern wireless security standards such as WPA3. If WPA3 is unavailable, WPA2 with strong configuration is generally preferable to older, outdated security methods.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Change Default Router Credentials</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Routers often come with default administrator credentials. Change them during initial setup and use a strong, unique password for router administration.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Secure Your Router</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Keep the router\'s firmware updated and disable unnecessary features or services. Review connected devices periodically to identify anything unfamiliar.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Be Careful on Public Networks</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Avoid connecting automatically to unknown Wi-Fi networks. Confirm the network name with the business or location when possible.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Use HTTPS</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A VPN provides network-level protection, but users should still make sure websites and applications use secure HTTPS connections, particularly when entering sensitive information.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Turn Off Automatic Wi-Fi Connections</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Disabling automatic connections to unknown networks can reduce the possibility of accidentally connecting to an unsafe hotspot.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Is a VPN Enough to Protect Your Wi-Fi?</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A VPN can significantly improve privacy and security, but it is not a complete cybersecurity solution.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A VPN generally protects traffic between your device and the VPN server. It does not automatically protect you from every phishing email, malware infection, compromised website, weak password, or account takeover attempt.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For this reason, users should adopt a layered security strategy that includes secure Wi-Fi configuration, updated software, endpoint protection, strong authentication, password management, and cybersecurity awareness.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Choosing the Right VPN Solution</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When selecting a VPN for personal or business use, consider factors such as:</p><ul><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Security protocols and encryption</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Privacy and data-retention policies</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Device and operating-system support</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Number of supported devices</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Connection performance</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Server availability</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Customer support</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Additional security features</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Business administration capabilities</p></li><li><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pricing and subscription terms</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Solutions such as NordVPN provide VPN connectivity along with additional security and privacy features. However, organizations should evaluate any provider against their specific security, compliance, privacy, and operational requirements rather than choosing a solution based only on its feature list.</p><h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Bottom Line</h2><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Wi-Fi has become an essential part of modern work and everyday digital activity, but convenience should not come at the expense of security.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A VPN can encrypt internet traffic, improve privacy, and provide an additional layer of protection when connecting through public or untrusted networks. Combined with strong passwords, multi-factor authentication, updated software, secure router settings, and user awareness, it can become an important component of a broader cybersecurity strategy.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For businesses supporting remote and hybrid employees, investing in secure connectivity is particularly important. The right combination of VPN technology and layered security controls can help organizations protect data while enabling employees to work productively from virtually anywhere.</p>', 'How to Secure Wi-Fi with a VPN | Wi-Fi Security Guide', 'Learn how VPN technology can protect Wi-Fi connections, encrypt internet traffic, improve privacy, and reduce security risks on public and home networks.', 'Wi-Fi security, VPN security, VPN solution, network security, public Wi-Fi security, Wi-Fi protection, online privacy, internet security, data encryption, cybersecurity, remote work security, secure Wi-Fi network, VPN for business', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-17 14:48:44', 'published', 2825065, 0, 9, NULL, '2026-09-17 14:48:44', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL),
(845, 6, 2, 12, 'Nokia, NTT and Anritsu Validate Elastic Networking for Next-Generation Networks', 'nokia-ntt-and-anritsu-validate-elastic-networking-for-next-generation-networks', 'Nokia, NTT and Anritsu validate Elastic Networking, enabling dynamic resource allocation, stronger performance and more resilient next-generation networks.', '[\"Elastic Networking\",\"Nokia\",\"NTT\",\"Anritsu\",\"Network Automation\",\"Software Defined Networking\",\"SDN\",\"Network Function Virtualization\",\"NFV\",\"AI Networking\",\"Machine Learning\",\"Network Slicing\",\"5G\",\"Telecom\",\"Network Management\",\"Network Optimization\"]', 'banner_image-1789065532478-957010546.webp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Nokia, NTT and Anritsu Validate Elastic Networking for Next-Generation Networks</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The telecommunications industry is moving toward networks that can respond dynamically to changing traffic, application requirements, and service demands. In this environment, <strong>Elastic Networking</strong> is emerging as an important approach for creating more flexible, efficient, and resilient network infrastructure.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A collaborative validation involving <strong>Nokia, NTT, and Anritsu</strong> represents an important step toward demonstrating how networks can dynamically adjust their resources according to real-time requirements. The work highlights the potential of Elastic Networking to improve service delivery, optimize infrastructure utilization, and support increasingly demanding digital applications.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Why Elastic Networking Matters</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Traditional network architectures often depend on predefined configurations and manually managed resources. While these approaches have supported telecommunications infrastructure for decades, they can become difficult to manage as data volumes and application requirements continue to increase.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The rapid growth of cloud computing, video services, connected devices, edge applications, and other bandwidth-intensive technologies is placing greater pressure on network infrastructure. At the same time, service providers need to introduce new services faster while maintaining consistent performance and reliability.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Elastic Networking addresses these challenges by allowing network resources to adapt according to changing conditions. Instead of relying entirely on fixed configurations, an elastic network can dynamically respond to traffic patterns, application requirements, and available resources.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This approach can help operators create networks that are more responsive, efficient, and capable of supporting future digital services.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Nokia, NTT and Anritsu Collaboration</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The validation involving Nokia, NTT, and Anritsu brings together complementary capabilities from across the telecommunications ecosystem.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Nokia</strong> contributes its expertise in telecommunications infrastructure and programmable networking technologies. Its technologies provide an important foundation for creating networks that can be dynamically controlled and optimized.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>NTT</strong>, as a major telecommunications operator, brings practical network environments and use cases that help demonstrate how elastic networking concepts can be applied in operational scenarios.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Anritsu</strong> contributes its network testing and measurement expertise. Testing and measurement are essential for determining whether dynamically configured networks can maintain the required performance, reliability, and service quality.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Together, the organizations have demonstrated the potential for network resources to be adjusted based on changing traffic and service requirements.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The validation illustrates how network parameters such as bandwidth and performance characteristics can be dynamically managed rather than remaining fixed. This capability could become increasingly important as networks support diverse applications with different performance requirements.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key Technologies Behind Elastic Networking</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Elastic Networking is enabled by several technologies working together.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Software-Defined Networking</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Software-Defined Networking (SDN)</strong> separates network control functions from the underlying forwarding infrastructure. This allows network behavior to be controlled programmatically and makes it easier for operators to modify configurations based on changing requirements.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SDN can provide the centralized visibility and programmability needed to coordinate dynamic network resources.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Network Function Virtualization</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Network Function Virtualization (NFV)</strong> enables network functions to operate as software rather than depending entirely on dedicated hardware.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Functions such as routing, security, and traffic management can be deployed, scaled, or modified as demand changes. This flexibility can help operators respond more quickly to changes in network workloads.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AI and ML can analyze network telemetry and identify traffic patterns, performance changes, and potential resource requirements.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">By applying predictive analytics and automation, these technologies can help networks respond proactively rather than waiting for congestion or performance problems to occur.</p><h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Network Slicing</h4><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Network slicing enables a physical network infrastructure to support multiple logical networks, with each slice designed for particular applications or customers.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Different services can therefore receive different combinations of bandwidth, latency, reliability, and other performance characteristics. This capability is particularly relevant to advanced 5G and future telecommunications environments.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Benefits of Elastic Networking</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The ability to dynamically adapt network resources can provide several advantages.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Better Network Performance:</strong><br>\r\nNetworks can respond to traffic fluctuations and allocate resources where they are most needed, potentially reducing congestion and improving application performance.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Improved Resource Utilization:</strong><br>\r\nDynamic allocation can reduce the amount of unused capacity and help operators make better use of existing infrastructure.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Faster Service Deployment:</strong><br>\r\nAutomation can reduce the time required to configure and provision new services, allowing operators to respond more quickly to customer requirements.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Greater Network Resilience:</strong><br>\r\nElastic architectures can support automated traffic adjustments and alternative routing when network conditions change or failures occur.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Increased Operational Flexibility:</strong><br>\r\nOperators can adapt network configurations to accommodate new applications, technologies, and business requirements without relying exclusively on manual intervention.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Impact on the Future of Telecommunications</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The validation of Elastic Networking demonstrates how telecommunications infrastructure could evolve toward more automated and adaptive operating models.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As <strong>5G, edge computing, cloud services, and IoT</strong> continue to expand, networks will need to support a wider range of workloads. These workloads can have significantly different requirements for bandwidth, latency, reliability, and availability.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Elastic Networking can help operators address this diversity by dynamically adjusting infrastructure according to application and service needs.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For example, an application requiring extremely low latency could receive resources optimized for fast response times, while another workload could prioritize bandwidth or capacity. This type of flexibility could allow service providers to build more differentiated and customized offerings.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Elastic Networking may also contribute to more efficient network operations. Greater automation and intelligent resource management could reduce manual configuration requirements while helping operators identify opportunities to optimize infrastructure.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Challenges to Wider Adoption</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Despite its potential, Elastic Networking still faces several challenges.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Standardization:</strong><br>\r\nCommon standards are important to ensure that technologies from different vendors can operate together effectively. Greater interoperability will be necessary for large-scale adoption.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Security:</strong><br>\r\nAs networks become increasingly programmable and automated, security must remain a central consideration. Dynamic network environments require appropriate controls to protect infrastructure, applications, and data.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Operational Complexity:</strong><br>\r\nManaging highly automated networks can introduce new levels of complexity. Operators need appropriate monitoring, orchestration, testing, and skilled personnel to manage these environments effectively.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Integration with Existing Infrastructure:</strong><br>\r\nMany telecommunications providers operate large networks built over multiple generations of technology. Integrating elastic capabilities with legacy infrastructure can require significant planning and investment.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Addressing these challenges will be important for moving Elastic Networking from successful validation projects toward broader commercial deployment.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Looking Ahead</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The collaboration between Nokia, NTT, and Anritsu highlights the industry\'s continued movement toward more programmable and adaptive telecommunications infrastructure.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Elastic Networking has the potential to change how network resources are managed by allowing infrastructure to respond more dynamically to traffic conditions and service requirements. Combined with SDN, NFV, AI/ML, network slicing, and advanced automation, it could provide an important foundation for future network architectures.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As digital services continue to generate new performance and scalability requirements, the ability to dynamically adapt infrastructure will become increasingly valuable. Continued testing, standardization, and technology development will determine how quickly these capabilities become widespread.</p><h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Conclusion</h3><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The validation of Elastic Networking by Nokia, NTT, and Anritsu represents an important development in the evolution of network technology. It demonstrates how collaboration between infrastructure providers, telecommunications operators, and testing specialists can help advance more dynamic networking models.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">By enabling networks to respond to changing traffic patterns and service requirements, Elastic Networking can support improved resource utilization, faster service deployment, greater flexibility, and enhanced resilience.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As telecommunications networks evolve to support 5G, edge computing, IoT, cloud applications, and future digital services, elastic and programmable infrastructure could become a key component of the next generation of connected networks.</p>', 'Nokia, NTT & Anritsu Validate Elastic Networking', 'Explore how Nokia, NTT and Anritsu validated Elastic Networking and its potential to improve network performance, automation, flexibility and resilience.', 'Elastic Networking, Nokia Elastic Networking, NTT, Anritsu, network automation, SDN, NFV, network slicing, AI networking, 5G networking, telecom networks, network optimization, network management, next-generation networks, telecommunications', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-17 17:33:57', 'published', 2304967, 1, 7, NULL, '2026-09-17 17:33:57', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL),
(846, 6, 1, 14, 'SehatUP Unveils Integrated Digital Health Clinic to Transform Personalized Healthcare in India', 'sehatup-unveils-integrated-digital-health-clinic-to-transform-personalized-healthcare-in-india', 'SehatUP launches an integrated digital health clinic combining modern medicine, Ayurveda and Homeopathy for personalized healthcare in India.', '[\"SehatUP\",\"Digital Health\",\"HealthTech\",\"Healthcare Technology\",\"Digital Healthcare\",\"Healthcare Innovation\",\"Personalized Healthcare\",\"Ayurveda\",\"Homeopathy\",\"Modern Medicine\",\"Telehealth\",\"Health and Wellness\",\"Healthcare Startups\",\"India Healthcare\",\"Sexual Wellness\",\"Weight Management\"]', 'banner_image-1789130990187-225129354.jpg', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SehatUP, an emerging health technology startup, has launched an integrated digital health clinic designed to bring multiple healthcare disciplines together on a single platform. The initiative combines modern medicine with traditional approaches such as Ayurveda and Homeopathy to provide users with more personalized and holistic healthcare solutions.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The launch comes in line with the Indian government’s broader vision of creating a more unified healthcare ecosystem, including greater integration of modern and traditional systems of medicine. SehatUP aims to contribute to this evolving healthcare landscape by bringing different medical practices together across healthcare delivery, education, and research.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">According to Karan Bhargava, Founder and CEO of SehatUP, the platform is designed to offer users a more comprehensive approach to long-term wellness. By combining modern medical practices with traditional healthcare systems, the company seeks to address individual health requirements while focusing on sustainable wellness and underlying health concerns.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The digital health clinic provides users with personalized healthcare plans and access to doctor consultations. The platform is initially focusing on areas including sexual wellness and weight management, offering users access to healthcare guidance based on their individual requirements.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In addition to consultations and customized wellness plans, SehatUP provides access to a range of medicines and natural supplements. The platform is designed to make healthcare solutions more accessible while bringing different approaches to health and wellness together within a single digital experience.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SehatUP has also built a network of more than 50 doctors and health coaches who contribute to the platform’s personalized healthcare approach. Through technology-enabled consultations and customized treatment plans, users can receive guidance that may incorporate modern medical practices as well as traditional approaches where appropriate.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Privacy and user convenience are another important component of the platform. SehatUP provides discreet delivery options, particularly for users seeking support for sensitive healthcare requirements. This approach is intended to create a more private and comfortable experience throughout the healthcare journey.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With the launch of its integrated digital health clinic, SehatUP is positioning technology as a bridge between different healthcare systems. The initiative reflects the growing role of digital platforms in improving access to personalized healthcare while supporting greater integration between modern and traditional approaches to wellness in India.</p>', 'SehatUP Launches Integrated Digital Health Clinic in India', 'SehatUP launches an integrated digital health clinic combining modern medicine, Ayurveda and Homeopathy for personalized healthcare solutions in India.', 'SehatUP, digital health clinic India, health tech startup India, digital healthcare, personalized healthcare, healthcare technology, Ayurveda, Homeopathy, telehealth India, integrated healthcare, healthcare innovation, digital health platform', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-18 13:26:40', 'published', 4874681, 1, 2, NULL, '2026-09-18 13:26:40', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL),
(847, 6, 2, 14, 'Canada’s Major AI Healthcare Investment Set to Transform Patient Care and Empower Health Professionals', 'canadas-major-ai-healthcare-investment-set-to-transform-patient-care-and-empower-health-professionals', 'Canada’s latest AI healthcare initiative aims to reduce administrative workloads, improve patient access, and help healthcare professionals deliver better care.', '[\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"AI in Healthcare\",\"Healthcare Technology\",\"Digital Health\",\"Health Compass II\",\"Healthcare Innovation\",\"Patient Care\",\"Medical AI\",\"Electronic Medical Records\",\"AI Investment\",\"Healthcare Professionals\",\"Patient Navigation\",\"Clinical Documentation\",\"Canada Healthcare\",\"Healthcare Automation\"]', 'banner_image-1789131108158-509414316.jpg', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Canada is making a major investment in artificial intelligence to strengthen its healthcare system and improve the way patients receive care. The initiative, known as <strong>Health Compass II</strong>, builds on the achievements of the original Health Compass project, which introduced AI-powered technologies into electronic medical records (EMRs).</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The first Health Compass initiative demonstrated how AI could help healthcare professionals manage time-consuming administrative responsibilities. It integrated AI capabilities into EMR systems and introduced <strong>Tali AI’s voice assistant</strong>, helping physicians reduce the amount of time spent on clinical documentation and administrative tasks.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Health Compass II will take these capabilities further by expanding the consortium and bringing additional technology and healthcare partners into the initiative. The project is expected to focus on AI-powered solutions that can support <strong>clinical documentation, referrals, patient navigation, and other healthcare workflows</strong>.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">According to <strong>ORX CEO Peder Sande</strong>, reducing administrative workloads is an important part of improving healthcare delivery. By allowing doctors to spend less time on repetitive administrative activities, AI tools can give them more time to concentrate on patients and clinical decision-making.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The initiative could also contribute to reducing pressure on emergency departments. More efficient access to primary and specialty care may help patients receive appropriate treatment earlier, potentially preventing some health concerns from becoming more serious and requiring emergency services.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Simon Fraser University (SFU)</strong> is also participating in Health Compass II, providing students with opportunities to gain practical experience through applied research involving the initiative’s partner organizations. Professor Fred Popowich highlighted the value of this collaborative approach, where universities, technology companies, and other organizations can build on one another’s expertise to accelerate innovation.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The broader investment also reflects Canada’s growing focus on artificial intelligence as a tool for healthcare transformation. Since 2018, <strong>DIGITAL</strong> has committed more than <strong>$500 million</strong> toward AI-related projects, including initiatives focused on healthcare innovation.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With continued investment and collaboration between healthcare organizations, technology companies, and academic institutions, projects such as Health Compass II could play an important role in modernizing healthcare delivery. AI-powered tools have the potential to reduce administrative workloads, improve operational efficiency, and ultimately give healthcare professionals more time to focus on patient care.</p>', 'Canada’s AI Healthcare Investment to Transform Patient Care', 'Canada’s Health Compass II uses AI to reduce healthcare workloads, improve patient access, streamline documentation, and support better patient care.', 'AI in healthcare, Canada AI healthcare, Health Compass II, healthcare technology, artificial intelligence healthcare, digital health, medical AI, AI investment, patient care, healthcare innovation, electronic medical records, healthcare automation', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-18 17:34:23', 'published', 1935387, 0, 2, NULL, '2026-09-18 17:34:23', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL),
(848, 6, 2, 4, 'AI Enables Real-Time Brain Tumor Diagnosis During Surgery', 'ai-enables-real-time-brain-tumor-diagnosis-during-surgery', 'AI technology can identify brain tumor types during surgery, helping surgeons make faster decisions and potentially enabling more targeted treatments.', '[\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"AI in Healthcare\",\"Brain Tumor\",\"Brain Cancer\",\"Cancer Diagnosis\",\"Machine Learning\",\"Deep Learning\",\"Medical AI\",\"Healthcare Technology\",\"Precision Medicine\",\"Tumor Diagnosis\",\"Genetic Sequencing\",\"Molecular Diagnostics\",\"Neurosurgery\",\"Oncology\"]', 'banner_image-1789131279390-594734378.jpg', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"meta\",\"title\",\"banner\",\"content\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Artificial intelligence is opening new possibilities in brain tumor diagnosis by enabling surgeons to identify tumor types and subtypes while an operation is still underway. A new AI-based approach can analyze tumor DNA in real time and provide detailed molecular information that could help doctors make more informed surgical decisions.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The innovative technique, described in a study published in <em>Nature</em>, uses artificial intelligence to examine sections of a brain tumor\'s DNA and detect specific chemical modifications. These molecular patterns can provide important information about the tumor\'s type and subtype, allowing doctors to obtain a more detailed diagnosis much earlier than with conventional genetic testing.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Jeroen de Ridder, an associate professor at the Center for Molecular Medicine at UMC Utrecht in the Netherlands, highlighted the importance of obtaining this information during surgery. According to de Ridder, the technology makes it possible to perform a detailed and reliable tumor diagnosis while the procedure is still taking place.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AI system, known as <strong>Sturgeon</strong>, was initially evaluated using frozen tumor samples collected from earlier brain cancer surgeries. During testing, the system successfully diagnosed 45 of 50 samples within approximately 40 minutes after genetic sequencing began. For the remaining five samples, the system did not provide a diagnosis because the available information did not meet its confidence requirements.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Researchers then moved the technology into real surgical environments, testing it during 25 brain tumor operations. Many of these procedures involved pediatric patients. Sturgeon successfully generated 18 correct diagnoses, while it declined to provide a diagnosis in seven cases because the results did not reach the required confidence level.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">One of the most significant aspects of the technology is its speed. The system was capable of producing diagnoses in less than 90 minutes. This timeframe could potentially make molecular information available early enough to influence decisions made by surgeons during an operation.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Currently, obtaining comprehensive genetic information about a brain tumor can require sending tissue samples to specialized laboratories. Depending on the testing process, obtaining complete results can take several weeks. Such delays can make it difficult for physicians to immediately understand the precise genetic characteristics of a tumor when planning treatment.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The new approach addresses this challenge by using rapid genetic sequencing and concentrating on a relatively small portion of the genome. By combining this sequencing technique with deep learning, researchers can analyze tumor characteristics much faster and potentially deliver useful molecular information while surgery is still in progress.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Real-time tumor classification could have several potential benefits. Surgeons may be able to better determine how aggressively a tumor should be removed, while oncologists could eventually use molecular information to select treatments that are better suited to a patient\'s specific tumor subtype.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">However, the technology still has important limitations. Some tumor types can be difficult for the system to classify, and expert pathologists remain important for identifying and selecting appropriate tissue samples. Tumors can also contain different populations of cells, creating additional challenges for molecular diagnosis.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Another consideration is the technical expertise required to operate the sequencing and AI systems effectively. Hospitals adopting this approach may need trained specialists who can manage the technology, interpret results and troubleshoot problems when necessary.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Despite these challenges, AI-assisted molecular diagnosis represents an important development in precision medicine. By reducing the time required to obtain detailed information about brain tumors, technologies such as Sturgeon could eventually help doctors make faster and more personalized treatment decisions.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the same time, the research demonstrates that identifying the molecular characteristics of a tumor is only one part of improving cancer care. Translating increasingly detailed biological information into effective, personalized therapies remains a major challenge for researchers and clinicians.</p>', 'AI Enables Real-Time Brain Tumor Diagnosis During Surgery', 'AI technology can diagnose brain tumor types during surgery by analyzing tumor DNA, helping surgeons make faster and more informed treatment decisions.', 'AI brain tumor diagnosis, artificial intelligence in healthcare, brain tumor diagnosis, AI cancer diagnosis, Sturgeon AI, brain cancer, machine learning healthcare, deep learning, genetic sequencing, molecular diagnostics, precision medicine, neurosurgery AI, tumor classification', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'live', NULL, '2026-09-21 12:04:36', 'published', 1913705, 0, 4, NULL, '2026-09-21 12:04:36', '2026-10-05 19:46:47', 1, NULL);
